COLLDATA("adabaalien","en",[[1,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was only sent to perfect noble character.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (8952)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (273)، والبزار في مسنده (8949)."],[2,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah does not look at your outward appearances or your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2564، 34)."],[3,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I guarantee a house on the outskirts of Paradise for the one who abandons arguing even when he is right, a house in the middle of Paradise for the one who abandons lying even when joking, and a house in the highest part of Paradise for the one whose character is excellent.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4800)."],[4,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, the upright Muslim may attain, through the nobility of his natural disposition and his good character, the rank of one who constantly fasts and stands in prayer reciting the verses of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (7052)."],[5,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, a man may attain through his good character the rank of one who stands in prayer during the night.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (284)."],[6,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is nothing heavier on the Scale than good character.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4799)، وأحمد (27517)، وصححه ابن حبان (481)."],[7,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will not be able to encompass all people with your wealth, but let them be encompassed by your cheerful faces and your good character.”","حسن: رواه البزار (9651)، وابن أبي الدنيا في التواضع والخمول (190)."],[8,"Masrūq narrated: We entered upon ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr when he came to Kūfah with Muʿāwiyah. He mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “He was neither obscene in speech nor deliberately vulgar.” And he said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, among the best of you are those who have the best character.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6029)، ومسلم (2321)."],[9,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you who among you are most beloved to me and will sit closest to me on the Day of Resurrection?” The people remained silent, so he repeated it two or three times. They then said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Those among you with the best character.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (6735)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (272)."],[10,"Jābir ibn Samurah narrated: I was in a gathering in which the Prophet ﷺ was present, while my father Samurah was sitting in front of me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Obscenity and deliberately behaving obscenely are not part of Islam in any way. Indeed, the people whose Islam is best are those whose character is best.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (20831)، وأبو يعلى (7468)."],[11,"Usāmah ibn Sharīk narrated: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ as though birds were perched upon our heads, and none of us spoke. Then some Bedouins came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling concerning such-and-such; give us a ruling concerning such-and-such.” He said: “O people, Allah has removed hardship from you, except for a man who attacks the honor of his brother; that is the one who has fallen into sin and destruction.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, should we seek medical treatment?” He replied: “Yes. Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down a cure for it, except for one disease.” They asked: “What is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Old age.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, which people are most beloved to Allah?” He said: “The people most beloved to Allah are those with the best character.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3436)، وأحمد (18454)، وصححه ابن حبان (486)، والحاكم (8214)."],[12,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you who the best among you are?” They replied: “Yes.” He said: “The best among you are those with the best character—I think he also said: those who are easygoing and pleasant for others to be around.”","حسن: رواه البزار في مسنده (1723)."],[13,"Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, those of you most beloved to me and closest to me in sitting on the Day of Resurrection will be those with the best character. And those of you most hated by me and farthest from me in sitting on the Day of Resurrection will be the excessive talkers, the affected speakers, and the mutafayhiqūn.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, we know who the excessive talkers and affected speakers are, but who are the mutafayhiqūn?” He replied: “The arrogant.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2018)."],[14,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ say: “The best among you are those with the best character, when they possess understanding.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (10022)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (285)."],[15,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak the truth until he is recorded as a thoroughly truthful person. Lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie until he is recorded as a habitual liar.” In another wording: “Adhere to truthfulness, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak truthfully and carefully pursue truthfulness until he is recorded with Allah as a thoroughly truthful person. Beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie and deliberately pursue lying until he is recorded with Allah as a habitual liar.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6094)، ومسلم (2607، 103) باللفظ الأول، ورواه مسلم (2607، 105) باللفظ الثاني."],[16,"Awsaṭ ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Awsaṭ al-Bajalī narrated that he heard Abū Bakr, after the Prophet ﷺ had passed away, say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in this very place of mine last year.” Then Abū Bakr wept and said: “Adhere to truthfulness, for it is joined with righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it is joined with wickedness, and both are in the Fire. Ask Allah for well-being, for after certainty no one has been given anything better than well-being. Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not cut one another off, do not turn your backs upon one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3849)، وأحمد (5، 17)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (724)."],[17,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of goodness.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2592، 74-75)."],[18,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Gentleness is not present in anything except that it beautifies it, and it is not removed from anything except that it disgraces it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2594، 78)."],[19,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿĀ’ishah, Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness. He grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness and what He does not grant for anything else.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2593)."],[20,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “O ʿĀ’ishah, be gentle, for when Allah intends good for a household, He guides them to the door of gentleness.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (24734)."],[21,"Jābir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When Allah intends good for a people, He brings gentleness among them.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1965)."],[22,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness in every matter.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3689)، وأحمد (24553)."],[23,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and He grants for it what He does not grant for harshness.”","حسن: رواه البزار (7114)، والطبراني في الصغير (221)، والبيهقي في الشعب (10554)."],[24,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and He grants for it what He does not grant for harshness.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3688)، والبزار في مسنده (9253)، وصححه ابن حبان (549)."],[25,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Indeed, Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and He grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (902)، وأبو يعلى (490)."],[26,"Khālid ibn Maʿdān narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Gentle, loves gentleness, and grants for it what He does not grant for harshness.”","حسن: رواه عبد الرزاق في مصنفه (9251)."],[28,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Charity does not decrease wealth. Allah does not increase a servant who forgives except in honor, and no one humbles himself for Allah except that Allah raises him.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2588)."],[29,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated: I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me: “O ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, maintain ties with the one who cuts you off, give to the one who deprives you, and forgive the one who wrongs you.” Then I later came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me: “O ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, control your tongue, weep over your sin, and let your home be sufficient for you.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (17452)."],[31,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on that occasion: “Let the Jews know that there is spaciousness and ease in our religion. Indeed, I have been sent with a pure and tolerant monotheistic religion.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (24855)."],[32,"Abū al-Sawwār al-ʿAdawī narrated: I heard ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn say that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty brings nothing but good.” Bashīr ibn Kaʿb said: “It is written in wisdom that some forms of modesty produce dignity, and some forms of modesty produce tranquility.” ʿImrān said to him: “I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you narrate to me from your written pages?”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6117)، ومسلم (37، 60)."],[33,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man from the Anṣār who was advising his brother regarding his excessive modesty. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave him, for modesty is part of faith.” In another wording: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who was reproaching his brother for being too modest, saying: “You are excessively shy,” as though he meant that his modesty was harming him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave him, for modesty is part of faith.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (10)، والبخاري (24)، ومسلم (36)، وروى البخاري (6118) باللفظ الثاني."],[34,"Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated: A companion of mine and I entered upon a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ named Usayr. He said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Modesty brings nothing but good.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى - المطالب العالية (2627) - ومن طريقه الضياء في المختارة (1483)."],[35,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more modest than a virgin secluded in her private chamber. Whenever he disliked something, we could recognize it from his face.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6102)، ومسلم (2320)."],[36,"Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī, ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr, narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the sayings that people have retained from the earliest prophethood is: ‘If you feel no shame, then do whatever you wish.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6120)."],[37,"Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among what people have retained from the teachings of the earliest prophethood is: ‘If you feel no shame, then do whatever you wish.’”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23254)، والبزار (2835)."],[38,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Modesty is from faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Obscene speech is from harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2009)، وأحمد (10512)، وصححه ابن حبان (608)، والحاكم (172)."],[39,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Obscenity is not present in anything except that it disgraces it, and modesty is not present in anything except that it beautifies it.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1974)، وابن ماجه (4185)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (601)، وابن حبان (551)."],[40,"Saʿīd ibn Yazīd al-Azdī narrated that a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He said: “I advise you to be modest before Allah just as you would be modest before a righteous man from among your people.”","صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (248)، ومحمد بن نصر المروزي في تعظيم قدر الصلاة (826)."],[41,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every religion has a distinctive character, and the distinctive character of this religion is modesty.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الصغير (1/13)، والخطيب في تاريخ بغداد (4034)."],[42,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise. Obscene speech is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (4184)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1314)، وابن حبان (5704)."],[43,"ʿAwn ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I said to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz: “So-and-so, a man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me”—and ʿUmar recognized who he was—“that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Modesty, chastity, inarticulateness—meaning inarticulateness of the tongue, not of the heart—and understanding are from faith. These are among the qualities that increase one’s reward in the Hereafter even if they diminish one’s worldly share, and what they increase in the Hereafter is greater. Obscene speech, harshness, and miserliness are from hypocrisy. These are among the qualities that may increase one’s worldly share but diminish one’s reward in the Hereafter, and what they diminish in the Hereafter is greater.’”","حسن: رواه الدارمي (526)."],[44,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Modesty and faith have been joined together; when one of them is removed, the other is removed as well.”","صحيح: رواه الحاكم (58)، والبيهقي في الشعب (7331)."],[45,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: Umm Sulaym, the wife of Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth. Must a woman perform ghusl if she has a sexual dream?” He replied: “Yes, if she sees the fluid.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (88)، والبخاري (6121)، ومسلم (313)."],[46,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6021)."],[47,"Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity. Among good deeds is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face and pour from your bucket into his vessel.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (14709)."],[48,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (18741)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (2118)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (231)."],[49,"Ḥudhayfah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1005)."],[50,"Abū Tamīmah al-Hujaymī narrated from a man of Bal-Hujaym who said: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, to what do you call people?” He replied: “I call to Allah alone—the One who, if harm touches you and you call upon Him, removes it from you; the One who, if you become lost in a barren land and call upon Him, guides you back; and the One who, if drought afflicts you and you call upon Him, causes vegetation to grow for you.” I said: “Then advise me.” He said: “Do not insult anyone, and do not regard any good deed as insignificant, even if it is only to meet your brother with a cheerful face, or to pour from your bucket into the vessel of someone asking for water. Wear your lower garment to the middle of the shin; if you refuse, then down to the ankles. Beware of letting the lower garment hang below the ankles, for letting it hang low is from arrogance, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not love arrogance.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (20636)."],[51,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Your smiling in the face of your brother is charity for you. Your commanding what is right and forbidding what is wrong is charity. Guiding a man who is lost is charity for you. Helping a man with poor eyesight to see his way is charity for you. Removing a stone, thorn, or bone from the road is charity for you. And pouring from your bucket into your brother’s bucket is charity for you.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (1556)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (891)، وابن حبان (529)."],[52,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever grants the use of a milk-producing animal, lends silver, or guides someone through a passageway will have a reward like that of freeing a slave.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1957)، وأحمد (18516)، وصححه ابن حبان (5096)."],[53,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are forty virtuous deeds, the highest of which is lending a milk-goat for another person to benefit from. No one performs any one of these deeds hoping for its reward and believing in the promised reward except that Allah will admit him into Paradise because of it.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2631)."],[54,"Abū Dharr narrated: The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Do not consider any good deed insignificant, even if it is only to meet your brother with a cheerful face.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2626)."],[55,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity. Among good deeds is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face and pour from your bucket into your brother’s vessel.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (1970)، وأحمد (14877)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (304)."],[56,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “I never saw the Prophet ﷺ laugh so fully that I could see the back of his throat. Rather, he would only smile.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6092)، ومسلم (899، 16)."],[57,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Rifāʿah al-Quraẓī divorced his wife irrevocably. Afterward, she married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I was married to Rifāʿah and he divorced me with the final of three divorces. Then I married ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Zubayr, but by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing more than something like this fringe.” She took hold of a fringe from her garment to illustrate what she meant. Abū Bakr was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, while Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ was sitting at the door of the room waiting for permission to enter. Khālid began calling out to Abū Bakr: “O Abū Bakr, will you not stop this woman from speaking so openly in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did nothing more than smile. Then he said: “Perhaps you want to return to Rifāʿah? No, not until you taste his sweetness and he tastes your sweetness.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6084)، ومسلم (1433، 112، 113)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[58,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some women from Quraysh were with him, asking him questions and requesting more from him, their voices raised above his voice. When ʿUmar sought permission to enter, the women hurried behind the curtain. The Prophet ﷺ gave him permission, and ʿUmar entered while the Prophet ﷺ was laughing. ʿUmar said: “May Allah keep you smiling, O Messenger of Allah. May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I was amazed at these women who were with me. As soon as they heard your voice, they hurried behind the curtain.” ʿUmar said: “You are more deserving that they should fear you, O Messenger of Allah.” Then he turned toward the women and said: “O enemies of yourselves! Do you fear me but not fear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They replied: “You are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Enough, O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb! By the One in whose hand is my soul, whenever Satan encounters you traveling along a path, he takes another path different from yours.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6085)، ومسلم (2396)."],[59,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I am ruined! I had intercourse with my wife during Ramadan.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Free a slave.” He replied: “I do not have one.” He said: “Then fast two consecutive months.” The man replied: “I am unable.” He said: “Then feed sixty poor people.” The man replied: “I have nothing.” Then a basket containing dates was brought. Ibrāhīm explained that al-ʿaraq means a large basket. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Where is the questioner? Give this in charity.” The man said: “To someone poorer than me? By Allah, there is no household between the two lava fields of Madinah poorer than my family.” The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molar teeth became visible, then said: “Then give it to your own family.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6087)، ومسلم (1111)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[60,"Jarīr narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ never prevented me from entering upon him after I embraced Islam, and whenever he saw me, he smiled in my face.” I complained to him that I could not remain steady on horseback. So he struck my chest with his hand and said: “O Allah, make him firm, and make him one who guides others and is himself rightly guided.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6089)، ومسلم (2475، 135)."],[61,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ on a Friday while he was delivering the sermon in Madinah and said: “The rain has failed. Ask your Lord to send us rain.” The Prophet ﷺ looked toward the sky, and we could see no clouds. He prayed for rain, and clouds began forming and gathering together. Then rain fell until the drainage channels of Madinah began to flow. The rain continued without stopping until the following Friday. Then that same man—or another man—stood while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon and said: “We are being flooded. Ask your Lord to hold it back from us.” The Prophet ﷺ laughed and then said two or three times: “O Allah, around us and not upon us.” The clouds began splitting apart from Madinah to the right and left. Rain fell around us, while none fell upon the city itself. Allah thereby showed them the honor of His Prophet ﷺ and the acceptance of his supplication.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6093، 1014)، ومسلم (897، 8)."],[62,"Jābir narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ was never asked for anything and replied, ‘No.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6034)، ومسلم (2311)."],[63,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with a cloak. Sahl asked the people: “Do you know what a burdah is?” They replied: “It is a mantle.” Sahl said: “It is a woven mantle with a border.” The woman said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have brought this to clothe you.” The Prophet ﷺ took it because he needed it and wore it. A man from among the Companions saw it on him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful this is! Give it to me to wear.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Yes.” When the Prophet ﷺ left, the man’s companions reproached him and said: “You did not do well. You saw that the Prophet ﷺ had taken it because he needed it, and then you asked him for it, even though you knew that he never refuses anyone who asks him for something.” The man replied: “I hoped for its blessing after the Prophet ﷺ had worn it, so that perhaps I could be shrouded in it.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6036)."],[64,"Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr narrated that she came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of Allah, I possess nothing except what al-Zubayr brings to me. Is there any sin upon me if I give a little from what he brings me?” He replied: “Give what you are able, and do not withhold and hoard, lest Allah withhold from you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1434)، ومسلم (1029، 89)."],[65,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A beggar asked for something, so I instructed the servant to bring something out for him. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: “O ʿĀ’ishah, do not count, lest Allah count against you.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (24418)، وابن حبان (3365)، وأبو يعلى (4463)."],[66,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah is Generous. He loves generosity and noble character, and He dislikes base and petty character.”","صحيح: رواه ابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (1/269)، والطبراني في الكبير (5928)."],[67,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4811)، والترمذي (1954)، وأحمد (7504)، وصححه ابن حبان (3407)."],[68,"Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said from the pulpit: “Whoever does not show gratitude for a little will not show gratitude for much. Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah. Speaking about Allah’s blessings is gratitude, while concealing them is ingratitude. Unity is mercy, and division is punishment.”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد المسند (18449، 19351)، والبزار (كشف الأستار - 1637)."],[69,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (2501)."],[70,"Al-Ashʿath ibn Qays narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (21838)."],[71,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is given a gift and has the means should repay it. If he does not have the means, then let him praise the giver for it. Whoever praises him has thanked him, and whoever conceals it has shown ingratitude for it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4813)."],[72,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is granted a favor and mentions it has shown gratitude for it, while whoever conceals it has shown ingratitude for it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4814)."],[74,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to al-Ashajj of ʿAbd al-Qays: “Indeed, you possess two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (17، 25)."],[75,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to al-Ashajj of ʿAbd al-Qays: “Indeed, you possess two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberation.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (18، 26)."],[76,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Sarjis al-Muzanī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Good demeanor, deliberation, and moderation are one part out of twenty-four parts of Prophethood.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2010)، وعبد بن حميد (512)."],[77,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Righteous conduct, good demeanor, and moderation are one part out of twenty-five parts of Prophethood.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4776)، وأحمد (2698)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (791)."],[78,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon a group of people who were sitting and said: “Shall I tell you who among you are the best and who are the worst?” They remained silent. He repeated this three times. Then a man said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Tell us who among us are the best and who are the worst.” He said: “The best of you are those whose good is hoped for and from whose harm people feel safe. The worst of you are those whose good is not hoped for and from whose harm people do not feel safe.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2263)، وأحمد (8812، 8920)، وصححه ابن حبان (527، 528)."],[80,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to Banū ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf in order to reconcile between them, and the time for prayer arrived.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (61)، والبخاري (684)، ومسلم (421، 102)."],[81,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: The people of Qubāʾ fought one another until they began throwing stones at each other. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed of this, so he said: “Come, let us go and reconcile between them.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2693)."],[82,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of something better in rank than fasting, prayer, and charity?” They replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Reconciling people, for corruption between people is the shaver.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4919)، والترمذي (2640)."],[83,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The son of Ādam does not perform anything better than prayer, reconciling people, and good character.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في التاريخ الكبير (1/63)، ومن طريقه البيهقي في الشعب (10580)."],[84,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A man sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “Allow him to enter. What a bad member of his clan—or what a bad brother of his clan—he is.” When the man entered, the Prophet ﷺ spoke gently to him. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, you said what you said about him, yet afterward you spoke gently to him?” He replied: “O ʿĀ’ishah, among the people of the worst rank with Allah are those whom people leave alone—or avoid—out of fear of their obscenity.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6131)، ومسلم (2591)."],[85,"Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrated: Some cloaks were brought to the Prophet ﷺ. My father Makhramah said to me: “Come with me to him; perhaps he will give us something from them.” My father stood at the door and spoke. The Prophet ﷺ recognized his voice and came out carrying a cloak, showing him its fine qualities while saying: “I saved this for you. I saved this for you.” In another wording: Some cloaks of brocade, buttoned with gold, were presented to the Prophet ﷺ. He distributed them among some of his Companions and set one aside for Makhramah. When Makhramah came, the Prophet ﷺ said: “I saved this for you.” Ayyūb said: “He held out the garment and showed it to him, because there was something difficult in Makhramah’s temperament.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2657)، ومسلم (1058، 130)."],[86,"ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār, the brother of Banū Mujāshiʿ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has revealed to me that you should humble yourselves, so that no one boasts over another and no one transgresses against another.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2865، 64)."],[87,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has revealed to me that you should humble yourselves and that none of you should transgress against another.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (4214)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (426)."],[88,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated from ʿUmar, and he said: I do not know it except as being raised to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: ‘Whoever humbles himself for Me like this’” —and Yazīd turned the palm of his hand toward the ground and lowered it— “‘I will raise him like this.’” Then he turned the palm of his hand toward the sky and raised it upward.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (309)، والبزار (175)، وأبو يعلى (187)."],[89,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who eats together with his servant, rides a donkey through the marketplaces, and holds a sheep himself and milks it has not behaved arrogantly.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (550)."],[90,"Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith narrated: We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were young men of similar age, and we stayed with him for twenty nights. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was merciful and gentle. He thought that we had begun to miss our families, so he asked us about those we had left behind. We told him, and he said: “Return to your families, stay among them, teach them, and instruct them. When the time for prayer arrives, let one of you call the adhān, then let the eldest among you lead you in prayer.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6008)، ومسلم (674)."],[91,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer and we stood with him. A Bedouin said during the prayer: “O Allah, have mercy upon me and Muḥammad, and do not have mercy upon anyone else with us.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said to the Bedouin: “You have restricted something vast.” Meaning the mercy of Allah.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6010)."],[92,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.” In another wording: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not show mercy to him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6013)، ومسلم (2319)."],[93,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī while al-Aqraʿ ibn Ḥābis al-Tamīmī was sitting with him. Al-Aqraʿ said: “I have ten children, and I have never kissed any one of them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and then said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5997)، ومسلم (2318)."],[94,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ would stick out his tongue playfully for al-Ḥusayn, and the child would see the redness of his tongue and eagerly move toward him. ʿUyaynah ibn Ḥiṣn ibn Badr said to him: “I see you doing this with this child! By Allah, I have a son who has already grown into manhood, yet I have never kissed him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان (5596)، وأبو الشيخ في أخلاق النبي ﷺ (ص 86)."],[95,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man from the Anṣār was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he had a young son with him. He began drawing the child close to himself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Do you have mercy on him?” He replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Then Allah is more merciful to you than you are to him, and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy.”","حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (7664) - واللفظ له -، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (377)."],[96,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Some Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Do you kiss children? We do not kiss them.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “What can I do for you if Allah has removed mercy from your heart?”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5998)، ومسلم (2317)."],[97,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the truthful and trusted Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū al-Qāsim, the occupant of the chamber, say: “Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4942)، والترمذي (1923)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (374)، وأحمد (8001)."],[98,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ: “Those who show mercy will be shown mercy by the Most Merciful. Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One above the heavens will show mercy to you.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4941)، والترمذي (1924)، واللفظ لأبي داود."],[99,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said while standing on the pulpit: “Show mercy and you will be shown mercy. Forgive and Allah will forgive you. Woe to the funnels of speech, and woe to those who persist in what they have done while knowing.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (6541)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (380)."],[100,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, Allah places His mercy only upon one who is merciful.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, all of us show mercy.” He replied: “It is not merely that one of you shows mercy to his companion; rather, he should show mercy to all people.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (4258)، والبيهقي في الشعب (10549)، والبيهقي في الشعب (10548)."],[101,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While a man was walking along a road, he became extremely thirsty. He found a well, descended into it, drank, and then came out. There he saw a dog panting and eating moist earth because of severe thirst. The man said: ‘This dog has been afflicted by the same thirst that afflicted me.’ So he went down into the well, filled his leather sock with water, held it in his mouth until he climbed back up, and gave the dog water. Allah appreciated his deed and forgave him.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, is there a reward for us even in serving animals?” He replied: “There is a reward for kindness to every living creature.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (23)، والبخاري (2363)، ومسلم (2244)."],[102,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman was punished because of a cat which she confined until it died, and because of it she entered the Fire. She neither fed it nor gave it water while keeping it confined, nor did she release it so that it could eat from the creatures of the earth.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3482)، ومسلم (2242، 143) عقب (2618)."],[103,"Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah narrated from his father that a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, when I slaughter a sheep, I feel compassion for it,” or he said: “I feel compassion for the sheep when I slaughter it.” He replied: “If you show mercy even to a sheep, Allah will show mercy to you. If you show mercy even to a sheep, Allah will show mercy to you.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (15592)، والبزار (كشف الأستار - 1221)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (373)."],[104,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever shows mercy, even to an animal being slaughtered, Allah will show mercy to him on the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (381)."],[105,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to our young and recognize the right of our elders is not of us.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4943)، وأحمد (7073)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (354)، والحاكم (209)."],[106,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (353)، وابن أبي الدنيا في النفقة على العيال (186)، وصححه الحاكم (7353)."],[107,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to our young and show reverence to our elders is not of us.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (356)، وابن أبي الدنيا في النفقة على العيال (187)."],[108,"Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated: Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd and ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl went toward Khaybar and separated among the date palms. ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl was killed, and they suspected the Jews. His brother ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and his two cousins, Ḥuwayyiṣah and Muḥayyiṣah, came to the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān began speaking about his brother, although he was younger than the other two. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let the elder speak first.” Or he said: “Let the oldest begin.” So the two older men spoke concerning their companion. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fifty of you should swear an oath against one of them, and he will be handed over in full liability.” They said: “It is something we did not witness, so how can we swear?” He said: “Then the Jews will clear themselves before you through the oaths of fifty of them.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, they are disbelieving people!” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid the blood money himself. Sahl said: “One day I entered an enclosure belonging to them, and one of those camels kicked me with its leg.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6142-6143)، ومسلم (1669، 2)."],[109,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tell me of a tree whose example is like that of a Muslim: it produces its fruit at all times by permission of its Lord, and its leaves do not fall.” It occurred to me that it was the date palm, but I disliked speaking because Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were present. When neither of them spoke, the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is the date palm.” When I later went out with my father, I said: “My father, it occurred to me that it was the date palm.” He said: “What prevented you from saying it? Had you said it, that would have been more beloved to me than such-and-such.” I replied: “Nothing prevented me except that I did not see you or Abū Bakr speaking, so I disliked speaking.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6144)، ومسلم (2811، 64)."],[110,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, part of honoring Allah is honoring an elderly Muslim, a bearer of the Qur’an who neither exceeds its proper bounds nor neglects it, and a just ruler.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4843)."],[111,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Overlook the slips of people of dignity and good standing, except in matters involving prescribed legal punishments.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4375)، وأحمد (25474)، والنسائي في الكبرى (7294)."],[112,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: When Banū Qurayẓah agreed to accept the judgment of Saʿd, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him, and he was nearby. He came riding on a donkey. When he drew near, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Stand up for your leader.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3043)، ومسلم (1768)."],[113,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated his account of when he stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabūk, and he mentioned the lengthy hadith. In it, after he was given the glad tidings that his repentance had been accepted, he said: “I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and people met me group after group congratulating me on my repentance, saying, ‘May Allah’s acceptance of your repentance bring you joy,’ until I entered the mosque. Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh stood up and hurried toward me, shook my hand, and congratulated me. No other man from among the Muhājirūn stood up for me besides him, and I will never forget that of Ṭalḥah.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4418)، ومسلم (2769)."],[114,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I never saw anyone more closely resemble the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in manner, bearing, and conduct when standing and sitting than Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: Whenever she entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would stand up for her, kiss her, and seat her in his place. And whenever the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her, she would stand from her place, kiss him, and seat him in her place.","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3872)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (947)."],[115,"Jābir narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became ill, so we prayed behind him while he was seated, and Abū Bakr was making his takbīrs audible to the people. The Prophet ﷺ turned toward us and saw us standing, so he gestured for us to sit. We then prayed seated, following his prayer. When he gave salām, he said: “A short while ago, you were about to do what the Persians and Romans do: they stand over their kings while their kings are seated. Do not do that. Follow your imams. If the imam prays standing, then pray standing; and if he prays seated, then pray seated.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (413)."],[116,"Muʿāwiyah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever loves that men should stand before him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5229)، والترمذي (2755)."],[117,"Anas narrated: There was no person more beloved to them than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Yet when they saw him, they would not stand up for him because they knew that he disliked that.","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2754)، وأحمد (12345)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (946)."],[118,"Abū Dharr narrated: I asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Which deed is best?” He replied: “Faith in Allah and striving in His cause.” I asked: “Which slaves are best to free?” He said: “Those that are most valuable in price and most precious to their owners.” I asked: “What if I am unable to do that?” He said: “Help a skilled worker, or do something for a person who is unable to work properly.” I asked: “What if I cannot do that?” He replied: “Then refrain from harming people, for that is a charity that you give on behalf of yourself.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2518)، ومسلم (84)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[119,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Every Muslim must give charity.” They asked: “What if he finds nothing to give?” He said: “Then let him work with his hands, benefit himself, and give charity.” They asked: “What if he is unable to do that, or does not do it?” He said: “Then let him help someone in desperate need.” They asked: “What if he does not do that?” He said: “Then let him command what is good,” or he said: “what is right.” They asked: “What if he does not do that?” He said: “Then let him refrain from evil, for that is charity for him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6022)، ومسلم (1008)."],[120,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him: “O Prophet of Allah, which deeds are best?” He replied: “Faith in Allah and striving in the cause of Allah.” He asked: “What if I am unable to do that? Which slaves are the most rewarding to free?” He replied: “Those that are most expensive and most precious to their owners.” He asked: “What if I am unable to do that?” He replied: “Then help someone who is helpless, or do something for one who lacks skill.” He asked: “What if I am unable to do that?” He replied: “Then restrain yourself from evil, for that is a charity you give on behalf of yourself.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (9038)."],[121,"Yūsuf ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Yūsuf, seated me on his lap, and stroked my head.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (367)، وأحمد (16402، 23836، 23837)."],[122,"Al-Aswad narrated: I asked ʿĀ’ishah: “What did the Prophet ﷺ do while he was with his family?” She replied: “He would be occupied in serving his family, and when the time for prayer came, he would get up for the prayer.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6039)."],[123,"ʿUrwah narrated: ʿĀ’ishah was asked: “What did the Prophet ﷺ do in his home?” She replied: “He did what any one of you does: he repaired his sandal and patched his garment.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (24479)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (540)، وأبو الشيخ في أخلاق النبي ﷺ (120)."],[124,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The example of a righteous companion and a bad companion is like that of a seller of musk and a blacksmith blowing the bellows. The seller of musk may give you some, or you may buy some from him, or at least you will find a pleasant fragrance from him. As for the one blowing the bellows, he may burn your clothes, or you will find an unpleasant smell from him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5534)، ومسلم (2628)."],[125,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A person follows the religion and way of his close friend, so let each of you carefully consider whom he takes as a close friend.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4833)، والترمذي (2378)، وأحمد (8028)، والحاكم (7320)."],[127,"Abū Mūsā narrated: Whenever someone came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking for a need, he would turn to those sitting with him and say: “Intercede, and you will be rewarded. Allah will decree through the tongue of His Prophet whatever He wills.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6028)، ومسلم (2627)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[128,"Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān said: “Intercede and you will be rewarded. Sometimes I intend to carry out a matter, but I delay it so that you may intercede and thereby receive a reward, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Intercede and you will be rewarded.’”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5132)، والنسائي في الكبرى (2349)."],[129,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No servant conceals the faults of another servant in this world except that Allah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2590، 72)."],[130,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah does not conceal a servant’s faults in this world except that He will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2590، 71)."],[131,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There are three things concerning which I swear: Allah will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share in it. The shares of Islam are three: fasting, prayer, and charity. Allah does not take a servant under His care and then hand him over to someone else on the Day of Resurrection. And no man loves a people except that he will come with them on the Day of Resurrection. As for a fourth matter, if I were to swear concerning it, I would not fear that I had sinned: Allah does not conceal the faults of His servant in this world except that He will conceal them for him in the Hereafter.” ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz said: “When you hear something like this from someone like ʿUrwah, preserve it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (4566)."],[132,"Abū Barzah al-Aslamī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O assembly of those who have believed with their tongues while faith has not entered their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims and do not search for their faults. Whoever searches for their faults, Allah will pursue his faults; and whoever Allah pursues for his faults, He will expose him even inside his own home.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4880)، وأحمد (19776)، والبيهقي في الآداب (137)."],[133,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When I was taken up, I passed by people who had fingernails of copper with which they were scratching their faces and chests. I asked, ‘Who are these, O Jibrīl?’ He said, ‘These are the people who used to eat the flesh of others and attack their honor.’”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4878)، وأحمد (13340)، والبيهقي في الآداب (138)."],[134,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, among the gravest forms of usury is unjustly attacking the honor of a Muslim.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4876)، وأحمد (1651)، والبيهقي في الآداب (145)."],[135,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “All of my Ummah may be pardoned except those who openly publicize their sins. Part of openly publicizing sin is that a man commits a deed at night, then morning comes while Allah has concealed it for him, yet he says, ‘O so-and-so, last night I did such-and-such.’ His Lord had concealed him throughout the night, but in the morning he removes Allah’s covering from himself.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6069)، ومسلم (2990)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[136,"Abū Mālik al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purification is half of faith. ‘Al-ḥamdu lillāh’ fills the Scale. ‘Subḥānallāh’ and ‘al-ḥamdu lillāh’ fill—or one of them fills—what is between the heavens and the earth. Prayer is light, charity is proof, patience is illumination, and the Qur’an is evidence either for you or against you. Every person goes out in the morning selling his own soul, either freeing it or destroying it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (223)."],[137,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ distributed something in the manner he sometimes distributed things. A man from the Anṣār said: “By Allah, this is a distribution by which Allah’s Face was not intended.” I said: “I will certainly tell the Prophet ﷺ.” So I went to him while he was among his Companions and spoke to him privately. This distressed the Prophet ﷺ. His face changed and he became angry, until I wished that I had never told him. Then he said: “Mūsā was harmed with more than this, yet he remained patient.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6100)، ومسلم (1062، 141)."],[138,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer who mixes with people and patiently bears their harm has a greater reward than the one who does not mix with them and does not patiently bear their harm.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2507)، وابن ماجه (4032)، وأحمد (5022) - واللفظ له."],[140,"Muʿādh ibn Anas al-Juhanī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever restrains his anger while being capable of acting upon it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will call him before all creation on the Day of Resurrection and allow him to choose whichever of the ḥūr al-ʿayn he wishes.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4777)، والترمذي (2021، 2493)، وابن ماجه (4186)."],[141,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one whose advice is sought is entrusted.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5128)، والترمذي (2822)، وابن ماجه (3745)."],[142,"Muʿāwiyah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A nation will not be sanctified in which judgment is not made according to truth and the weak cannot take their right from the strong without being intimidated or made to hesitate.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (19/ح 903)."],[146,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There are three qualities which, if found in a person, cause him to experience the sweetness of faith: that Allah and His Messenger are more beloved to him than everything else; that he loves a person only for the sake of Allah; and that he hates to return to disbelief just as he hates to be thrown into the Fire.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (16)، ومسلم (43، 67)."],[147,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant does not truly believe until I am more beloved to him than his family, his wealth, and all people.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (44، 69)."],[148,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say on the Day of Resurrection: ‘Where are those who loved one another for My Majesty? Today I shall shade them in My shade, on a day when there is no shade except My shade.’”","صحيح: رواه مالك (10)، ومسلم (2566، 37)."],[149,"Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī narrated: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw a young man with bright, shining teeth. The people were gathered around him. Whenever they differed concerning something, they referred the matter to him and accepted his judgment. I asked who he was, and I was told: “This is Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” The next day I went early, but found that he had arrived before me and was praying. I waited until he finished his prayer, then approached him from the front, greeted him with salām, and said: “By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.” He asked: “By Allah?” I replied: “By Allah.” He asked again: “By Allah?” I replied: “By Allah.” He asked a third time: “By Allah?” I replied: “By Allah.” He then took hold of the edge of my cloak, pulled me toward him, and said: “Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: My love has become obligatory for those who love one another for My sake, sit together for My sake, visit one another for My sake, and spend upon one another for My sake.’”","صحيح: رواه مالك (16)، وأحمد (22030)، وصححه ابن حبان (575)، والحاكم (7314)."],[150,"Abū Idrīs ʿĀʾidh Allah ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: One day, during the early period of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb’s caliphate, he entered the mosque and found a gathering of more than twenty of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They were all discussing hadiths of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Among them was a young man with a dark complexion, pleasant speech, a radiant appearance, and he was the youngest among them. Whenever something in the hadith became unclear to them, they referred it back to him, and he would clarify it for them. While ʿĀʾidh Allah was sitting with them, the prayer was established and the gathering dispersed. He said: “By Allah, no night that ever passed over me—not even one of severe illness or an urgent need—felt longer than that night, because I was hoping morning would come so that I could meet them again.” In the morning he went to the mosque, walking back and forth, but did not find any of them. Later, he returned early and saw the same young man whom they had been referring to the day before, praying beside a pillar in the mosque. ʿĀʾidh Allah stood by the pillar in front of him. When the young man finished praying, he leaned his back against it. I kept looking at him until he realized that I needed something from him. I said: “Have you finished your prayer, may Allah rectify you?” The young man replied: “Yes.” I sat opposite him with my knees drawn up. Neither did he say anything to me, nor did I begin speaking, until I thought the prayer might separate us. Then I said: “May Allah rectify you, narrate to me. By Allah, I love you and I love your narrations.” He asked: “By Allah, do you truly love me and love my narrations?” I replied: “By Allah, besides whom there is no deity, I truly love you and love your narrations.” The young man asked: “Why do you love me and my narrations? By Allah, there is no kinship between you and me, nor have I ever given you wealth.” I replied: “I love you because of the Majesty of Allah.” He asked: “Do you truly love me because of the Majesty of Allah?” I replied: “By Allah, I love you because of the Majesty of Allah.” He then took hold of the cloth wrapped around my knees and pulled it toward himself until he brought me close. Then he said: “Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Indeed, those who love one another for the Majesty of Allah will be beneath the shade of Allah’s Throne on a day when there will be no shade except His shade.’” When he had narrated this hadith to me, the prayer was established. I asked: “Who are you, O servant of Allah?” He replied: “Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” ʿĀʾidh Allah thereafter frequently narrated this hadith of Muʿādh ibn Jabal.","حسن: رواه البزار (2672)، والطبراني في الكبير (20/78)."],[151,"Abū Muslim al-Khawlānī narrated: I came to the mosque of the people of Damascus and saw a gathering containing elderly men from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. Among them was a young man with dark-lined eyes and bright teeth. Whenever they differed concerning something, they referred it to that young man. I asked the man sitting beside me: “Who is this?” He replied: “This is Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” I came later that evening, but they were not there. The next morning I returned, but they still had not arrived. Later, I came back and saw the young man praying beside a pillar. I prayed, then moved closer to him. He gave salām, and I approached him and said: “Indeed, I love you for the sake of Allah.” He pulled me closer and asked: “What did you say?” I replied: “Indeed, I love you for the sake of Allah.” He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrating from his Lord: ‘Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be upon pulpits of light beneath the shade of the Throne on a day when there will be no shade except His shade.’” I then left until I met ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit and mentioned to him the hadith of Muʿādh ibn Jabal. He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrating from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic: ‘My love has become obligatory for those who love one another for My sake. My love has become obligatory for those who give generously to one another for My sake. My love has become obligatory for those who visit one another for My sake. And those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be upon pulpits of light beneath the shade of the Throne on a day when there will be no shade except His shade.’”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (22064) - واللفظ له -، والترمذي (2390)، وصححه ابن حبان (577)."],[152,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No servant loves another servant for the sake of Allah except that he thereby honors his Lord, Mighty and Majestic.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (22229)."],[153,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ: “There are no two men who love one another for the sake of Allah while apart from one another except that the one more beloved to Allah is the one whose love for his companion is stronger.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (5275)."],[154,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No two men love one another for the sake of Allah except that the better of the two is the one who loves his companion more strongly.”","حسن: رواه ابن الجعد (3192)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (544)، وابن حبان (566)."],[155,"Abū Ẓabyah narrated: Shuraḥbīl ibn al-Simṭ called ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah al-Sulamī and said: “O Ibn ʿAbasah, will you narrate to me a hadith that you yourself heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, without addition or falsehood, and not something you heard from another person who heard it from him?” He replied: “Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: My love has become obligatory for those who love one another for My sake; My love has become obligatory for those who maintain pure affection for one another for My sake; My love has become obligatory for those who visit one another for My sake; My love has become obligatory for those who give generously to one another for My sake; and My love has become obligatory for those who support one another for My sake.’”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن المبارك في الزهد (716)، وأحمد (19438)."],[156,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves for the sake of Allah, hates for the sake of Allah, gives for the sake of Allah, and withholds for the sake of Allah has perfected faith.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4681)."],[157,"Muʿādh ibn Anas al-Juhanī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever gives for the sake of Allah, withholds for the sake of Allah, loves for the sake of Allah, hates for the sake of Allah, and gives in marriage for the sake of Allah has perfected his faith.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2521)، والإمام أحمد (15638)، والحاكم (2694)."],[158,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the souls of the believers meet one another from a distance of a day’s journey, even though one of them may never have seen his companion before.”","حسن: رواه ابن وهب في الجامع (ص 27)، وأحمد (6636)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (261)."],[159,"Khuzaymah ibn Thābit narrated: I saw in a dream that I was prostrating upon the forehead of the Prophet ﷺ. I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of this, and he said: “Indeed, one soul meets another soul.” The Prophet ﷺ then tilted his head back in this manner, and Khuzaymah placed his forehead upon the forehead of the Prophet ﷺ.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (21864)، وابن أبي شيبة (11/78)، والطبراني في الكبير (4/97)."],[160,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibrīl and says: ‘Indeed, I love so-and-so, so love him.’ Then Jibrīl loves him. After that, he announces in the heaven: ‘Indeed, Allah loves so-and-so, so love him,’ and the inhabitants of heaven love him. Then acceptance is placed for him on the earth. And when Allah hates a servant, He calls Jibrīl and says: ‘Indeed, I hate so-and-so, so hate him.’ Then Jibrīl hates him. After that, he announces among the inhabitants of heaven: ‘Indeed, Allah hates so-and-so, so hate him.’ Then they hate him, and hatred is placed for him on the earth.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (1637)، والبخاري (7485)."],[161,"Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you loves his brother, let him tell him that he loves him.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5124)، والترمذي (2392)، وأحمد (17171)، وصححه ابن حبان (507)."],[162,"Abū Dharr narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If one of you loves his companion, let him go to him at his home and tell him that he loves him for the sake of Allah.” He then said: “And I have come to you at your home for that reason.”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن المبارك في الزهد (712) - ومن طريقه أحمد (21294) -، وعبد الله بن وهب في جامعه (232)."],[163,"Mujāhid narrated: A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ met me and took hold of my shoulder from behind. He said: “Indeed, I love you.” I replied: “May the One for whose sake you love me love you.” He said: “Had the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not said, ‘If a man loves another man, let him tell him that he loves him,’ I would not have told you.” Then he began offering me a marriage proposal and said: “We have a slave girl, though she is one-eyed.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (543)."],[164,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A man was with the Prophet ﷺ when another man passed by. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, indeed I love this man.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Have you told him?” He replied: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Tell him.” So he caught up with the man and said: “Indeed, I love you for the sake of Allah.” The man replied: “May the One for whose sake you love me love you.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5125)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (182)، وأحمد (12430، 12514)."],[165,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came to him, greeted him with salām, and then left. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, indeed I love this man for the sake of Allah.” He asked: “Have you informed him of that?” I replied: “No.” He said: “Then inform your brother.” So I followed him until I caught up with him, took hold of his shoulder, greeted him with salām, and said: “By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.” He replied: “By Allah, I also love you for the sake of Allah.” I said: “Had the Prophet ﷺ not commanded me to tell you, I would not have done so.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان (569)، والطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (4989)، وفي الكبير (12/366)."],[166,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you loves his brother, let him inform him, for he may find that his brother feels toward him the same thing that he feels toward his brother.”","صحيح: رواه ابن أبي الدنيا في الإخوان (74)، والبيهقي في الشعب (8595)."],[167,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man visited a brother of his in another village. Allah placed an angel in wait for him along his path. When the man reached him, the angel asked, ‘Where are you going?’ He replied, ‘I am going to visit a brother of mine in this village.’ The angel asked, ‘Do you have some favor with him that you are seeking to maintain or improve?’ He replied, ‘No, except that I love him for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.’ The angel said, ‘I am a messenger from Allah to you, informing you that Allah has loved you just as you loved him for His sake.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2567)."],[168,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No Muslim servant goes to visit his brother for the sake of Allah except that a caller from heaven calls out: ‘May you be blessed, and may Paradise be blessed for you.’ And Allah says in the dominion of His Throne: ‘My servant has visited for My sake, so his hospitality is upon Me.’ Allah is not pleased to give him any reward less than Paradise.”","حسن: رواه البزار (6466)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (665)، وأبو يعلى (4140)."],[169,"Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who visits a sick person remains in the fruit-garden of Paradise until he returns.” In another narration: “In the harvested fruits of Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2568، 39-41)."],[170,"Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Come with us to Banū Wāqif so that we may visit that blind man.” Sufyān said: “Banū Wāqif were a clan from the Anṣār, and the man had lost his eyesight.”","صحيح: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1920)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (4356)."],[171,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I were leaving the mosque, we met a man at the entrance of the mosque. He asked: “O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour be?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “What have you prepared for it?” The man seemed humbled by the question, then said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have not prepared for it a great amount of prayer, fasting, or charity, but I love Allah and His Messenger.” He said: “Then you will be with those whom you love.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7153)، ومسلم (2639، 164)."],[172,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who loves a people but has not reached their level?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “A person will be with those whom he loves.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7169)، ومسلم (2640)."],[173,"Abū Mūsā narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was asked: “A man loves a people but has not yet reached their level?” He replied: “A person will be with those whom he loves.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6170)، ومسلم (2641)."],[174,"Abū Dharr said: “O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people but is unable to perform deeds like theirs.” He replied: “O Abū Dharr, you will be with those whom you love.” Abū Dharr said: “Indeed, I love Allah and His Messenger.” He replied: “Then you will be with those whom you love.” Abū Dharr repeated it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated the same answer.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5126)، وأحمد (21379، 21463)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (351)."],[175,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: I saw the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rejoice over something more intensely than I had ever seen them rejoice over anything else. A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, a man loves another because of the righteous deeds he performs, although he himself does not perform deeds equal to his?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “A person will be with those whom he loves.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5127)."],[176,"Abū Hurayrah narrated a hadith which he attributed to the Prophet ﷺ: “People are like mines of silver and gold. The best of them in the Jāhiliyyah are the best of them in Islam when they gain understanding. Souls are like conscripted soldiers: those among them that recognize one another become harmonious, while those that are unfamiliar with one another differ.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2638، 160)."],[177,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Souls are like conscripted soldiers: those among them that recognize one another become harmonious, while those that are unfamiliar with one another differ.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (10557)."],[178,"ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated: There was a humorous woman in Makkah who stayed with another woman who was similar to her. When this reached ʿĀ’ishah, she said: “My beloved spoke the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Souls are like conscripted soldiers: those among them that recognize one another become harmonious, while those that are unfamiliar with one another differ.’”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (4381)."],[179,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks the pleasure of Allah even though it angers people, Allah, the Exalted, will be pleased with him and will cause the people to be pleased with him. But whoever seeks the pleasure of people by angering Allah, Allah will be angry with him and will cause the people to be angry with him.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان (276)."],[180,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever angers Allah in order to please people, Allah becomes angry with him and causes those whom he pleased through Allah’s displeasure to become angry with him. And whoever pleases Allah despite people’s displeasure, Allah becomes pleased with him and causes those who were angered by his seeking Allah’s pleasure to become pleased with him, until He makes him, his words, and his deeds appear beautiful in their eyes.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (11696)."],[181,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, those closest to me on the Day of Resurrection are the people of taqwā, even if some lineage is closer to me than another. Let not other people come to me carrying righteous deeds while you come carrying the worldly life upon your necks, saying: ‘O Muḥammad!’ Then I will say like this and like this: ‘No.’” He then turned away on both sides.","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (897)."],[182,"Al-Maʿrūr ibn Suwayd narrated from Abū Dharr: I saw Abū Dharr wearing a cloak, while his servant was wearing a similar cloak. I said: “If you took his garment and wore it together with yours, you would have a complete outfit, and you could give him another garment.” He replied: There was once an argument between me and another man whose mother was non-Arab, and I insulted him through his mother. He complained about me to the Prophet ﷺ, who said to me: “Did you insult so-and-so?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Did you insult him because of his mother?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “You are a man in whom there is still some Jāhiliyyah.” I asked: “Even at this stage of my life, despite my old age?” He said: “Yes. They are your brothers whom Allah has placed under your authority. So whoever has a brother whom Allah has placed under his authority should feed him from what he himself eats, clothe him from what he himself wears, and not burden him with work that overwhelms him. If he does burden him with something overwhelming, then let him help him with it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6050)، ومسلم (1661)."],[183,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ used to instruct people to treat enslaved persons well, saying: “Feed them from what you eat, clothe them from what you wear, and do not torture the creation of Allah.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (188، 199)."],[184,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An enslaved person is entitled to his food and clothing, and he must not be burdened with work beyond what he is capable of.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1662، 41)."],[185,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When the servant of one of you brings him his food, if he does not seat him with himself, then let him at least give him a morsel or two, or a portion or two, because he endured the work of preparing it.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2557)."],[186,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the servant of one of you prepares his food and then brings it to him after enduring its heat and smoke, let him seat the servant with him and let him eat. If the food is scarce and little, then let him place in his hand a portion or two.” Dāwūd said: “Meaning, a morsel or two.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1663، 42)."],[187,"Abū al-Zubayr narrated that he heard a man ask Jābir about a person’s servant who had spared him the hardship and heat of preparing the food: “Did the Prophet ﷺ command that he be invited to eat?” Jābir replied: “Yes. If one of you dislikes having him eat alongside him, then let him at least place a portion of the food in his hand.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (198)."],[188,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, how many times should we pardon a servant?” He remained silent. The man repeated the question, and he remained silent again. When he asked a third time, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Pardon him seventy times every day.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5164)، والترمذي (1949 في الرواية الثانية)، والبخاري في التاريخ الكبير (7/3)."],[189,"Zādhān Abū ʿUmar narrated: I came to Ibn ʿUmar after he had freed a slave. He picked up a stick or something similar from the ground and said: “There is not even this much reward in what I have done, except that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever slaps his slave or strikes him, the expiation for that is to free him.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1657)."],[190,"Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī narrated: I was striking a servant of mine when I heard a voice behind me saying: “Know, O Abū Masʿūd, that Allah has more power over you than you have over him.” I turned around and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, he is free for the sake of Allah.” He replied: “Had you not done so, the Fire would have scorched you,” or: “the Fire would have touched you.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1659، 35)."],[191,"Hilāl ibn Yasāf narrated: An elderly man became hasty and slapped a female servant of his. Suwayd ibn Muqarrin said to him: “Could you find nothing to strike except her face? I remember when I was one of seven brothers from Banū Muqarrin, and we had only one female servant. The youngest of us slapped her, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to free her.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1658، 32)."],[192,"Muʿāwiyah ibn Suwayd narrated: I slapped a servant belonging to us and then fled. I returned shortly before Ẓuhr and prayed behind my father. He called the servant and called me, then said: “Take retaliation from him.” But the servant pardoned me. Then my father said: “We, Banū Muqarrin, during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only one female servant. One of us slapped her, and this reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: ‘Free her.’ They said: ‘They have no servant besides her.’ He said: ‘Then let them continue to employ her until they no longer need her, and when they can do without her, let them set her free.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1658، 31)."],[193,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ say: “Whoever falsely accuses his slave of zinā while the slave is innocent of what he said will be flogged on the Day of Resurrection, unless the accusation was in fact true.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6858)، ومسلم (1660، 37)."],[194,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a slave is sincere to his master and worships Allah well, he receives his reward twice.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (43)، والبخاري (2546)، ومسلم (1664، 43)."],[195,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A righteous slave who fulfills his duties receives two rewards.” Abū Hurayrah then said: “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abū Hurayrah, were it not for striving in the cause of Allah, performing Ḥajj, and dutifulness to my mother, I would have loved to die while being a slave.” It was also reported to us that Abū Hurayrah would not perform Ḥajj while his mother was alive because he remained with her in service and companionship.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2548)، ومسلم (1665، 44)."],[196,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Three people will be given their reward twice: a man who has a female slave, teaches her and teaches her well, disciplines and educates her well, then frees her and marries her—he has two rewards; a believer from the People of the Book who had already believed and then believed in the Prophet ﷺ—he has two rewards; and a slave who fulfills the right of Allah and is sincere to his master.” Then al-Shaʿbī said: “I have given this hadith to you for nothing, whereas a man used to travel to Madinah for something less important than this.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3011)، ومسلم (154، 241)."],[197,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “How excellent it is for one of them to worship his Lord well and be sincere to his master.” In another wording: “How excellent it is for a slave to die while worshipping Allah well and maintaining good companionship with his master. How excellent that is for him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2549)، ومسلم (1667، 46)."],[198,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a slave fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he receives two rewards.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1666، 45)."],[199,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every one of you is a shepherd and every one of you is responsible for those under his care. The ruler over the people is a shepherd over them and is responsible for them. A man is a shepherd over the members of his household and is responsible for them. A woman is a shepherd over the home of her husband and his children and is responsible for them. A slave is a shepherd over the property of his master and is responsible for it. Indeed, every one of you is a shepherd, and every one of you is responsible for his flock.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2554)، ومسلم (1829)."],[200,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never struck anything with his hand—neither a woman nor a servant—except when fighting in the cause of Allah. Nor was he ever personally wronged and then took revenge against the one who wronged him, unless one of Allah’s sacred limits was violated; then he would act for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2328)."],[201,"Anas narrated: “I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years, and he never once said to me, ‘Uff!’ nor did he say, ‘Why did you do that?’ or, ‘Why did you not do that?’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6038)، ومسلم (2309)."],[202,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “He is not of us who corrupts a woman against her husband or a slave against his master.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2175)، وأحمد (9157)، وابن حبان (568، 5560)، والحاكم (2795)."],[203,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it.”","حسن: رواه أبو نعيم في الحلية (1818)."],[204,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it, for it serves as discipline for them.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (10671)، وفي الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (3130)."],[205,"Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim narrated from his father that the Prophet ﷺ said concerning the captives of Badr: “Had al-Muṭʿim ibn ʿAdī been alive and then spoken to me concerning these foul-smelling captives, I would have released them for his sake.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (3139)."],[206,"Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ mentioning one of his sons-in-law from Banū ʿAbd Shams. He praised him for the way he had conducted himself as a son-in-law and spoke well of him. He said: “He spoke to me and told me the truth, and he made me a promise and fulfilled it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3729)، ومسلم (2449، 95)."],[207,"Al-Mustawrid al-Qurashī narrated—while he was in the presence of ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Hour will be established while the Romans are the majority of mankind.” ʿAmr said to him: “Be careful about what you are saying.” He replied: “I am only saying what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” ʿAmr said: “If you say that, then indeed they possess four qualities: they are the most forbearing of people at the time of tribulation, the quickest to recover after calamity, the quickest to return to battle after fleeing, and the best of people toward the poor, the orphan, and the weak.\nAnd there is a fifth, beautiful and excellent quality: they are the people most capable of preventing the oppression of kings.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2898)."],[208,"Al-Nawwās ibn Samʿān al-Anṣārī narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about righteousness and sin. He replied: “Righteousness is good character, and sin is that which wavers uneasily within your chest and which you dislike for people to discover.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2553)."],[209,"Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.” The Prophet ﷺ looked me over carefully and said: “Righteousness is that with which the soul becomes tranquil and the heart finds reassurance. Sin is that with which the soul does not become tranquil and the heart does not find reassurance, even if those who give legal verdicts give you a verdict.” He also said: “Do not approach the meat of domesticated donkeys, nor any predatory animal possessing fangs.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (17742)."],[210,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Which deeds are most beloved to Allah?” He replied: “Prayer at its proper time.” I asked: “Then which?” He said: “Then dutifulness to one’s parents.” I asked: “Then which?” He replied: “Then striving in the cause of Allah.” Ibn Masʿūd said: “He told me these, and had I asked him for more, he would have given me more.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5970)، ومسلم (85، 139)."],[211,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While three men were walking, rain overtook them, so they took shelter in a cave in a mountain. A rock fell from the mountain over the entrance of their cave and sealed them inside. They said to one another: ‘Think of righteous deeds you performed sincerely for Allah, and supplicate to Allah by means of them; perhaps He will relieve you.’” One of them said: “O Allah, I had two elderly parents and small children for whom I used to graze livestock. When I returned in the evening and milked the animals, I would begin with my parents and give them milk before my children. One day, the grazing took me far away, and I did not return until evening. I found that they had fallen asleep. I milked as I normally did and brought the vessel, then stood by their heads, disliking to wake them from their sleep and also disliking to give my children before them. Meanwhile, the children were crying from hunger at my feet. This remained my condition and theirs until dawn. O Allah, if You know that I did this seeking Your Face alone, then make an opening for us through which we can see the sky.” Allah opened a gap for them until they could see the sky. The second man said: “O Allah, I had a female cousin whom I loved as intensely as a man can love a woman. I sought to have relations with her, but she refused unless I brought her one hundred dinars. I worked until I had gathered one hundred dinars and then came to her with it. When I sat between her legs, she said: ‘O servant of Allah, fear Allah and do not break the seal unlawfully.’ So I got up and left her. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your Face, then open a way for us.” So Allah opened another gap for them. The third said: “O Allah, I once hired a laborer for a faraq of rice. When he completed his work, he said: ‘Give me my wage.’ I offered him what was due to him, but he left it and turned away from it. I continued cultivating and investing it until from it I accumulated cattle and their herdsman. Later he came and said: ‘Fear Allah, do not wrong me, and give me my right.’ I said: ‘Go to those cattle and their herdsman.’ He replied: ‘Fear Allah and do not mock me.’ I said: ‘I am not mocking you. Take those cattle and their herdsman.’ So he took them and went away with them. O Allah, if You know that I did that seeking Your Face, then remove what remains.” Then Allah released them completely.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5974)، ومسلم (2743)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[212,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A child can never fully repay his father except if he finds him enslaved, purchases him, and then frees him.” In another wording: “A child cannot fully repay his father.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1510)."],[213,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated: A man came to him and said: “I have a wife, and my mother is ordering me to divorce her.” Abū al-Dardāʾ replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The father is the middle—and best—of the gates of Paradise. So if you wish, neglect that gate, or preserve it.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1900)، وأحمد (27511)، والحاكم (4/152)."],[214,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “O Messenger of Allah, who among people has the greatest right to my good companionship?” He replied: “Your mother.” The man asked: “Then who?” He replied: “Then your mother.” He asked: “Then who?” He replied: “Then your mother.” He asked: “Then who?” He replied: “Then your father.” In another narration: “Then the nearest to you, and then the next nearest.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5971)، ومسلم (2548، 1). والرواية الثانية رواها مسلم (2548)."],[215,"Bahz ibn Ḥakīm narrated from his father, from his grandfather: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I show the greatest dutifulness?” He replied: “Your mother.” I asked: “Then whom?” He said: “Your mother.” I asked: “Then whom?” He said: “Your mother.” I asked: “Then whom?” He replied: “Then your father, then the closest relative, followed by the next closest.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5139)، والترمذي (1897)، وأحمد (20028)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد."],[216,"Muʿāwiyah ibn Jāhimah al-Sulamī narrated that Jāhimah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I intend to go out for military expedition, and I have come to consult you.” He asked: “Do you have a mother?” He replied: “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Then remain with her, for Paradise is beneath her feet.”","حسن: رواه النسائي (3104)، وابن ماجه (2781)، وأحمد (15538)، والحاكم (2/104)."],[217,"Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah commands you concerning your mothers.” He said it three times. Then he said: “Indeed, Allah commands you concerning your fathers. Indeed, Allah commands you concerning the nearest relative, then the next nearest.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3661) - واللفظ له -، وأحمد (17187)، والحاكم (4/151)."],[218,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Only three spoke while still in the cradle: ʿĪsā ibn Maryam, and the child connected with the story of Jurayj…” Jurayj was a devoted worshipper who had built himself a hermitage and remained there. His mother came to him while he was praying and called: “O Jurayj!” He said to himself: “My Lord, my mother or my prayer?” He chose to continue his prayer, so she left. The next day she came again while he was praying and called: “O Jurayj!” He said: “My Lord, my mother or my prayer?” He continued his prayer, and she left. The following day she came while he was praying and called him again: “O Jurayj!” He said: “My Lord, my mother or my prayer?” He continued his prayer. She then said: “O Allah, do not let him die until he looks upon the faces of prostitutes.” The Children of Israel began discussing Jurayj and his worship. There was a prostitute whose beauty was proverbial. She said: “If you wish, I will tempt him for you.” She presented herself to him, but he paid no attention to her. She then went to a shepherd who used to seek shelter near Jurayj’s hermitage and offered herself to him. He had intercourse with her and she became pregnant. When she gave birth, she said: “The child belongs to Jurayj.” The people came to Jurayj, forced him down from his hermitage, demolished it, and began beating him. He asked: “What is wrong with you?” They replied: “You committed zinā with this prostitute, and she has given birth to your child.” He asked: “Where is the child?” They brought the infant. Jurayj said: “Leave me until I pray.” He prayed, then came to the child, poked him in the stomach, and asked: “O boy, who is your father?” The infant replied: “So-and-so, the shepherd.” The people then turned toward Jurayj, kissing him and touching him seeking blessing, and said: “We will rebuild your hermitage out of gold.” He replied: “No. Rebuild it from clay just as it was.” So they did.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3436)، ومسلم (2550، 8)."],[221,"Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr narrated: My mother came to me while she was still a polytheist, during the period in which Quraysh had a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So I sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, my mother has come to me desiring good relations. Should I maintain ties with my mother?” He replied: “Yes, maintain ties with your mother.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2620)، ومسلم (1003)."],[222,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl while a group of his people were around him. He said: “Ibn Abī Kabshah has stirred up trouble for us.” Then ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh said: “By the One who honored you and sent down the Book to you, if you wish, I will bring you his head.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “No. Rather, be dutiful to your father and keep good companionship with him.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (428)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (2708)."],[223,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May his nose be rubbed in the dust! May his nose be rubbed in the dust! May his nose be rubbed in the dust!” It was asked: “Who, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “The one who lives to see his parents in old age—one of them or both of them—and yet does not enter Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2551)."],[224,"Ubayy ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever lives to see his parents, or one of them, and then still enters the Fire afterward, may Allah cast him far away and remove him from His mercy.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (19027)، والطيالسي (1418)، والبخاري في التاريخ الكبير (2/40)."],[225,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah has forbidden you from disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, withholding what is due while continually asking from others, and He dislikes for you three things: gossiping about what was said, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2408)، ومسلم (593 عقب 1715)."],[226,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the greatest of the major sins?” We replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Associating partners with Allah and disobedience to parents.” He had been reclining, then he sat up and said: “And beware of false speech and false testimony! Beware of false speech and false testimony!” He continued repeating it until I thought: “He will not stop.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5976)، ومسلم (87)."],[227,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the major sins—or was asked about the major sins—and said: “Associating partners with Allah, unlawfully killing a soul, and disobedience to parents.” Then he said: “Shall I inform you of the greatest of the major sins?” He said: “False speech,” or: “False testimony.” Shuʿbah said: “I strongly think that he said: ‘false testimony.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5977)، ومسلم (88، 144)."],[228,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are three whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: one who is disobedient to his parents, a woman who imitates men, and a dayyūth. And there are three who will not enter Paradise: one who is disobedient to his parents, one who is addicted to intoxicants, and one who reminds people of what he has given them.”","حسن: رواه النسائي (2562)."],[229,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays al-Juhanī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the greatest of the major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the deliberately false oath. No person swears a binding oath by Allah and inserts into it even something as small as a mosquito’s wing of falsehood except that a dark mark is placed in his heart until the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (3020)، وأحمد (16043)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (893)."],[230,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the greatest of the major sins is for a man to curse his own parents.” It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how could a man curse his own parents?” He replied: “He insults another man’s father, so that man insults his father; and he insults the other man’s mother, so that man insults his mother.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5973)، ومسلم (90)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[231,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, among the highest forms of dutifulness is for a child to maintain ties with those whom his father loved.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2552، 11) بسنده عن عبد الله بن عمر، أن رجلا من الأعراب لقيه بطريق مكة، فسلم عليه عبد الله، وحمله على حمار كان يركبه، وأعطاه عمامة كانت على رأسه، فقال ابن دينار: فقلنا له: أصلحك الله، إنهم الأعراب، وإنهم يرضون باليسير. فقال عبد الله: إن أبا هذا كان ودا لعمر بن الخطاب، وإني سمعت رسول الله ﷺ يقول: فذكره."],[232,"Abū Burdah narrated: I came to Madinah, and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar came to me and asked: “Do you know why I came to you?” I replied: “No.” He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever wishes to maintain dutiful ties with his father after his father is in the grave should maintain ties with his father’s brothers and close friends after him.” Then he said: “There was brotherhood and affection between my father, ʿUmar, and your father, so I wished to maintain that bond.”","صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (5669)، وصححه ابن حبان (432)."],[233,"Anas narrated: No one more closely resembled the Prophet ﷺ than al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī. A man was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when one of his sons came to him. He took the boy, kissed him, and seated him on his lap. Then a daughter of his came. He took her and seated her. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Why did you not treat the two of them equally?”","حسن: رواه الطحاوي في شرح معاني الآثار (4/89)، والبيهقي في الشعب (8327، 10510)."],[234,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The maternal aunt holds the status of a mother.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2699)."],[235,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a grave sin. Is there any repentance for me?” He asked: “Do you have a mother?” The man replied: “No.” He asked: “Do you have a maternal aunt?” He replied: “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Then be dutiful to her.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1904)، وأحمد (4624)، وابن حبان (435)، والحاكم (7261)."],[236,"Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī narrated: A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise.” The people said: “What is wrong with him? What is wrong with him?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He has an important need.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish the prayer, give zakāh, and maintain the ties of kinship. Let go of it.” The narrator said: “It was as though the man was holding onto the Prophet’s riding animal.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5983)، ومسلم (13، 13)."],[237,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during his illness: “Your family ties! Your family ties!”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (436)."],[238,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The act of obedience whose reward comes most quickly is maintaining the ties of kinship. A household may even be sinful, yet their wealth increases and their numbers multiply when they maintain ties with one another. No household maintains kinship ties and remains in need.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه (440)."],[239,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The act of obedience whose reward comes most quickly is maintaining kinship ties. A household may be sinful, yet their wealth increases and their numbers multiply when they maintain their kinship ties. And the sins whose punishment comes most quickly are transgression and betrayal. A deliberately false oath destroys wealth, diminishes family ties, and leaves homes desolate and barren.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (2108)."],[240,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the bond of kinship is a branch connected to al-Raḥmān. Allah says to it: ‘Whoever maintains you, I will maintain My connection with him; and whoever severs you, I will sever him.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5988)."],[241,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah created creation, and when He had finished creating them, the bond of kinship stood and said: ‘This is the place of one seeking refuge from being severed.’ Allah said: ‘Yes. Would you not be pleased that I maintain My connection with whoever maintains you, and sever whoever severs you?’ It replied: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘Then that is granted to you.’” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite, if you wish: ‘Would you then, if you were given authority, spread corruption in the land and sever your ties of kinship? Those are the ones whom Allah has cursed, so He made them deaf and blinded their sight. Do they not then reflect upon the Qur’an, or are there locks upon their hearts?’”\n[Sūrat Muḥammad 47:22–24]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5987)، ومسلم (2554)."],[242,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The bond of kinship is suspended from the Throne, saying: ‘Whoever maintains me, Allah will maintain His connection with him; and whoever severs me, Allah will sever him.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5989)، ومسلم (2555) - واللفظ له."],[243,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the bond of kinship is a branch that clings to the waist-wrapper of al-Raḥmān. He maintains His connection with whoever maintains it and severs whoever severs it.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (2953)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1883)، والطبراني (10/398)."],[244,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: ‘I am al-Raḥmān. I created the bond of kinship, al-raḥim, and derived its name from My Name. Whoever maintains it, I will maintain My connection with him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him.’”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1907)، وأبو داود (1695)، وأحمد (1681)، وابن حبان (443)، والحاكم (7271)."],[245,"ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say openly and not secretly: “Indeed, the family of so-and-so are not my close allies. My true Protector is Allah and the righteous believers.” In al-Bukhārī’s narration, he added: “However, I do have ties of kinship with them, and I will keep those ties properly maintained.” Meaning: I will maintain those family ties through the connection due to them.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5990)، ومسلم (215)."],[246,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would love for his provision to be expanded and his lifespan to be extended, let him maintain his ties of kinship.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5986)، ومسلم (2557)."],[247,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would love for his lifespan to be extended and his provision to be increased, let him be dutiful to his parents and maintain his ties of kinship.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (13401)، وابن أبي الدنيا في مكارم الأخلاق (244)، والبيهقي في الشعب (7471)."],[248,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever is pleased that his provision be expanded and his lifespan be extended, let him maintain his ties of kinship.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5985)."],[249,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever would be pleased for his lifespan to be prolonged, his provision to be expanded, and an evil death to be warded off from him, let him fear Allah and maintain his ties of kinship.”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائده على المسند (1213)، والحاكم (7280)."],[250,"The Mother of the Believers ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said to her: “Whoever is granted his share of gentleness has been granted his share of the good of this world and the Hereafter. Maintaining kinship ties, good character, and good treatment of neighbors cause homes to flourish and increase lifespans.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (25259)."],[251,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives whose ties I maintain, but they sever ties with me. I treat them well, but they treat me badly. I remain forbearing toward them, while they behave ignorantly toward me.” He replied: “If you are as you say, it is as though you are feeding them hot ashes, and you will continue to have a supporter from Allah against them for as long as you remain upon that.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2558)."],[252,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who truly maintains kinship is not merely the one who reciprocates. Rather, the true maintainer of kinship is the one who, when his relatives sever ties with him, continues to maintain ties with them.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5991)."],[253,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb saw a striped silk garment being sold near the door of the mosque and said: “O Messenger of Allah, why not buy this garment and wear it on Fridays and when delegations come to you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears this.” Later, some garments of that type came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave one of them to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb. ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, you have clothed me with this even though you said what you said concerning the garment of ʿUṭārid?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “I did not give it to you so that you would wear it.” So ʿUmar gave it to a polytheist brother of his in Makkah. In al-Bukhārī’s narration: “I did not give it to you so that you would wear it; rather, you may sell it or give it to someone else to wear.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (18)، والبخاري (886)، ومسلم (2068)."],[254,"Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, what about the acts of devotion I used to perform during the Jāhiliyyah, such as giving charity, freeing slaves, and maintaining kinship ties? Is there any reward for them?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You embraced Islam together with the good that you had already done.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5992)، ومسلم (123، 195)."],[255,"Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One who severs ties will not enter Paradise.” In Muslim’s wording: “One who severs ties of kinship.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5984)، ومسلم (2556)."],[256,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The bond of kinship is a branch connected to al-Raḥmān. Whoever severs it, Allah forbids Paradise to him.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (1651)، والبزار (1265)، وصححه الحاكم (7266)."],[257,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The deeds of the children of Ādam are presented every Thursday night, the night before Friday, and the deed of one who severs kinship ties is not accepted.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (10272)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (61)."],[258,"Abū Hurayrah narrated, attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ: “Deeds are presented every Monday and Thursday. On that day Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forgives every person who does not associate anything with Allah, except a person between whom and his brother there is hostility. It is said: ‘Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2565، 36)."],[259,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no sin more deserving that Allah hasten its punishment for its perpetrator in this world, while also storing punishment for him in the Hereafter, than transgression and severing ties of kinship.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4902)، والترمذي (2679)، وابن ماجه (4211)، وأحمد (20374)."],[260,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The bond of kinship is a branch connected to al-Raḥmān. Whoever maintains it, He maintains His connection with him, and whoever severs it, He severs him. On the Day of Resurrection it will have an eloquent and fluent tongue.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (54)."],[261,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A woman entered upon me accompanied by her two daughters, asking for something. I had nothing with me except a single date, so I gave it to her. She divided it between her two daughters and did not eat any of it herself. Then she got up and left. The Prophet ﷺ later entered, and I told him what had happened. He said: “Whoever is tested with any of these daughters, they will be a shield for him from the Fire.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1418)، ومسلم (2629)."],[262,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A poor woman came to me carrying her two daughters. I gave her three dates to eat. She gave each daughter one date, then raised the third date to her mouth to eat it. Her two daughters asked her for it, so she split the date she had intended to eat between them. I was impressed by what she had done, so I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Indeed, because of that deed Allah has made Paradise obligatory for her—or has freed her from the Fire because of it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2630)."],[263,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man has two daughters who reach an age at which he cares for them, and then treats them well for as long as they remain with him, except that they will cause him to enter Paradise.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3670)، وأحمد (2104)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (77)، وابن حبان (2945)."],[264,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever supports and raises two girls until they reach maturity will come on the Day of Resurrection with me like this.” He joined his fingers together.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2631)."],[265,"Anas—or another narrator—reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever supports two or three daughters, or two or three sisters, until they die or he dies while still caring for them, then he and I will be like these two.” He pointed with his index and middle fingers.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (12498)."],[266,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever has three daughters and remains patient in caring for them, feeds them, gives them drink, and clothes them from his means, they will be a barrier for him from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3669)، وأحمد (17403)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (76)."],[267,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever supports three daughters, provides sufficiently for them, shows them mercy, and treats them gently will be in Paradise.” A man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what about two?” He replied: “And two.” We thought that if someone had asked: “And one?” he would have said: “And one.”","صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (2210) - والسياق له -، وابن أبي شيبة (943)."],[269,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not dislike daughters, for they are affectionate companions and precious.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (17373)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 856)."],[270,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Which sin is greatest in the sight of Allah?” He replied: “That you set up an equal with Allah even though He created you.” I said: “That is indeed tremendous.” Then I asked: “Then which?” He replied: “That you kill your child out of fear that he will eat with you.” I asked: “Then which?” He replied: “That you commit adultery with your neighbor’s wife.” Another narration adds that Allah revealed in confirmation of the Prophet’s ﷺ words: “And those who do not invoke another deity alongside Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except with right, nor commit unlawful sexual intercourse; and whoever does that will meet a penalty.” [Sūrat al-Furqān 25:68]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6001)، ومسلم (86)، والسياق لمسلم."],[271,"Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while carrying Umāmah, the daughter of Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by Abū al-ʿĀṣ ibn Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbd Shams. When he prostrated, he would put her down, and when he stood up, he would carry her.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (87)، والبخاري (516)، ومسلم (543، 41)."],[272,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī while al-Aqraʿ ibn Ḥābis al-Tamīmī was sitting with him. Al-Aqraʿ said: “I have ten children, yet I have never kissed any one of them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5997)، ومسلم (2318)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[273,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Some Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “Do you kiss your children?” They replied: “Yes.” The Bedouins said: “But by Allah, we do not kiss them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What can I do if Allah has removed mercy from you?” In another wording: “…removed mercy from your heart?”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5998)، ومسلم (2317)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[274,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ placed a baby in his lap in order to perform taḥnīk for him, and the child urinated on him. So he called for water and poured it over the affected area.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6002)، ومسلم (286)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[275,"Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would take me and seat me on one of his thighs, and seat al-Ḥasan on his other thigh. Then he would embrace us both and say: “O Allah, have mercy on them, for indeed I have mercy on them.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6003)."],[276,"Al-Aswad ibn Khalaf narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he took al-Ḥasan and kissed him, then turned toward those present and said: “Indeed, children can be a cause of miserliness, ignorance, and cowardice.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1891)، والحاكم (5284)."],[277,"Umm Khālid bint Khālid ibn Saʿīd narrated: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my father while I was wearing a yellow shirt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Sanah, sanah.” ʿAbdullāh said: “In the Abyssinian language, this means: ‘Beautiful.’” She said: I then began playing with the Seal of Prophethood, so my father rebuked me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave her.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wear it out and replace it, wear it out and replace it, wear it out and replace it.” ʿAbdullāh said: “She lived so long that the length of her life became something people spoke about.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5993)."],[278,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer in relation to another believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other.” Al-Bukhārī added: He then interlaced his fingers.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6026)، ومسلم (2585، 65)."],[279,"Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of the believers in their mutual love, mercy, and compassion is like that of a single body: when one limb suffers, the rest of the body responds with sleeplessness and fever.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6011)، ومسلم (2586)."],[281,"ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say openly, not secretly: “Indeed, the family of Abū so-and-so—” ʿAmr said: “There is a blank space at this point in the manuscript of Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar.” The Prophet ﷺ continued: “—are not my close allies. My true Protector is Allah and the righteous believers.” In al-Bukhārī’s narration: “However, I do have kinship ties with them, which I maintain properly.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5990)، ومسلم (215)."],[282,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah does not look at your outward forms or your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2564، 34)."],[283,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rights of a Muslim over another Muslim are five: returning the salām, visiting the sick, following funeral processions, accepting invitations, and saying ‘yarḥamuk Allah’ to one who sneezes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1240)، ومسلم (2162، 4)."],[284,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rights of a Muslim over another Muslim are six.” It was asked: “What are they, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “When you meet him, greet him with salām. When he invites you, accept his invitation. When he seeks your sincere advice, advise him sincerely. When he sneezes and praises Allah, say ‘yarḥamuk Allah’ to him. When he becomes ill, visit him. And when he dies, follow his funeral.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2162، 5)."],[285,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A Muslim is the brother of another Muslim. He does not wrong him, nor does he abandon him. Whoever attends to the need of his brother, Allah will attend to his need. Whoever relieves a Muslim of a hardship, Allah will relieve him of one of the hardships of the Day of Resurrection. And whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his faults on the Day of Resurrection.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2442)، ومسلم (2580، 58)."],[286,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not envy one another, do not artificially raise prices against one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and do not undercut one another’s sales. Be servants of Allah as brothers. A Muslim is the brother of another Muslim: he does not wrong him, abandon him, or look down upon him. Taqwā is here.” He pointed to his chest three times. Then he said: “It is sufficient evil for a person to despise his Muslim brother. The whole of a Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim: his blood, his wealth, and his honor.” Another narration adds: “Indeed, Allah does not look at your bodies or your outward forms, but He looks at your hearts.” And he pointed with his fingers toward his chest.","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2564، 32، 33)، والبخاري (6066)."],[287,"An elderly man from Banū Sulayṭ narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ to speak with him concerning captives of ours who had been taken during the Jāhiliyyah. I found him seated with a circle of people surrounding him while he addressed them. He was wearing a coarse Qaṭarī waist-wrapper. I heard him say, while pointing with his finger: “A Muslim is the brother of another Muslim. He does not wrong him or abandon him. Taqwā is here. Taqwā is here.” Meaning: in the heart.","حسن: رواه أحمد (16624)."],[288,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is the mirror of the believer, and the believer is the brother of the believer. He protects him from loss and safeguards him in his absence.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4918)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (239)، والبزار (8109)."],[289,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is the mirror of the believer.”","حسن: رواه البزار (6193)، والطبراني في الأوسط (2114) - ومن طريقه الضياء في المختارة (2185)."],[290,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: “I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon establishing prayer, giving zakāh, and offering sincere advice to every Muslim.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1401)، ومسلم (56)."],[291,"ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated: I asked Anas ibn Mālik: “Has it reached you that the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘There is no alliance in Islam’?” He replied: “The Prophet ﷺ established an alliance between Quraysh and the Anṣār in my house.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6083)، ومسلم (2529، 204)."],[292,"Anas narrated: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf came to us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2293)."],[293,"Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no newly established alliance in Islam, but any alliance that existed in the Jāhiliyyah is only strengthened by Islam.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2530)."],[294,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather: When Makkah was conquered for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he mentioned the lengthy sermon, in which the Prophet ﷺ said: “Fulfill the alliances established in the Jāhiliyyah, for Islam only strengthens them, but do not establish new alliances of that kind in Islam.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (6933)، والترمذي (1585)."],[295,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no newly established alliance in Islam. Every alliance that existed in the Jāhiliyyah is only strengthened by Islam. I would not be pleased to have the finest red camels in exchange for having broken the alliance that was established in Dār al-Nadwah.”","حسن: رواه ابن جرير الطبري في تفسيره (1925)."],[296,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the true emigrant is the one who abandons what Allah has forbidden.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6484)، ومسلم (40، 64)."],[297,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, which expression of Islam is best?” He replied: “That of the person from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (11)، ومسلم (42)."],[298,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (41)."],[299,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is the one whom people trust, the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who abandons evil. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no servant whose neighbor is not safe from his harm will enter Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (12561)، وابن حبان (510)، والحاكم (25)."],[300,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the believer is the one whom people trust regarding their lives and their wealth.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2627)، والنسائي (4995)، وابن حبان (180)، والحاكم (22)."],[301,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Shall I tell you who the Muslim is? He is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The believer is the one whom people trust regarding their wealth and their lives. The emigrant is the one who abandons sins and transgressions. And the mujāhid is the one who strives against his own soul in obedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23958، 23968)، وابن ماجه (3934)، وابن حبان (4862)."],[302,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should point a weapon at his brother, for he does not know—perhaps Satan may cause his hand to slip, and he may thereby fall into a pit of the Fire.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7072)، ومسلم (2617)."],[303,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ said: “Whoever points a piece of iron at his brother, the angels curse him until he puts it down, even if the person is his full brother through both his father and mother.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2616)."],[304,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us, and whoever deceives us is not of us.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (101)."],[305,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7070)، ومسلم (98)."],[306,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7071)، ومسلم (100)."],[307,"Iyās ibn Salamah narrated from his father that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not of us.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (99)."],[308,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If one of you passes through our mosque or our marketplace carrying arrows, let him hold their points in the palm of his hand, lest any Muslim be injured by them.” Or he said: “Let him grasp their points.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7075)، ومسلم (2615، 124)."],[309,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you passes through a gathering or a marketplace with arrows in his hand, let him hold their points. Let him hold their points. Let him hold their points.” Abū Mūsā then said: “By Allah, we did not die before we ended up directing them at one another’s faces.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2615، 123)."],[310,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: A man passed through the mosque carrying arrows, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Hold their points.” In another narration: A man passed through the mosque carrying arrows whose points were exposed, so he was instructed to grasp their points so that they would not scratch or injure a Muslim.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7073)، ومسلم (2614، 120) باللفظ الأول."],[311,"Jābir narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he instructed a man who was distributing arrows in charity in the mosque not to pass through with them unless he was holding their points.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2614، 122)."],[312,"Abū Bakrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon some people passing an unsheathed sword between themselves. He said: “May Allah curse whoever does this! Have I not forbidden you from this?” Then he said: “If one of you draws his sword, examines it, and then wishes to hand it to his brother, let him first sheath it and then hand it to him.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (20429)."],[313,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a group sitting together who had drawn a sword and were passing it between themselves while it was unsheathed. He said: “Did I not forbid you from this? When one of you draws a sword, let him sheath it and then hand it to his brother.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14981)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (3335)، وابن حبان (5943)."],[314,"Bannah al-Juhanī narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people in the mosque—or in a gathering—who were drawing a sword and passing it among themselves while it was unsheathed. He said: “May Allah curse whoever does that! Have I not forbidden you from this? When you draw a sword, let the man sheath it and then hand it over in that state.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14742)، وابن سعد (3/353)، وابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (1/102)."],[315,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated: The Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ told us that they were traveling with the Prophet ﷺ when one of them fell asleep. Some of them went and took a rope that was with him, causing him to become frightened. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to frighten another Muslim.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5004)، وأحمد (23064)، والبيهقي في الآداب (542)."],[316,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever defends the honor of his Muslim brother, it becomes a right that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will turn the Fire of Hell away from him on the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (27536)، والترمذي (1931)."],[317,"Asmāʾ bint Yazīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever defends the flesh of his brother when he is being backbitten, it becomes a right upon Allah to free him from the Fire.”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن المبارك في الزهد (687)، ومن طريقه أحمد (27609)، والطبراني في الكبير (24/ح 443)."],[318,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever relieves a believer of one of the hardships of this world, Allah will relieve him of one of the hardships of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever makes things easy for one in difficulty, Allah will make things easy for him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever conceals the faults of a Muslim, Allah will conceal his faults in this world and the Hereafter. And Allah continues to aid the servant as long as the servant continues to aid his brother.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2699)."],[319,"Ḥuṣayn ibn Mālik narrated: A beggar came and asked Ibn ʿAbbās for something. Ibn ʿAbbās asked him: “Do you testify that there is no deity except Allah?” He replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Do you testify that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Yes.” He asked: “And do you fast Ramadan?” He replied: “Yes.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “You have asked, and the one who asks has a right. It is therefore a right upon us to maintain and assist you.” He then gave him a garment and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No Muslim clothes another Muslim with a garment except that he remains under Allah’s protection for as long as even a piece of that garment remains upon him.”","حسن: أخرجه الترمذي (2484) - والسياق له -، والبخاري في التاريخ الكبير (3/9)، والحاكم (4/196)."],[320,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, among the gravest forms of usury is unjustly attacking the honor of a Muslim.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4876)، وأحمد (1651)، والبزار (1264)."],[321,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The gravest form of usury is for a person to unjustly attack the honor of his Muslim brother.”","حسن: رواه أبو القاسم الأصبهاني في الترغيب والترهيب (588)، ورواه أبو داود (4877) مطولا، وفي إسناده ضعف."],[322,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the believer wears down and overcomes his devils just as one of you wears down his camel during a journey.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (8940)."],[323,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A believer is not stung from the same hole twice.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6133)، ومسلم (2998)."],[324,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is innocent-hearted and noble, while the wicked person is deceitful and ignoble.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (6008)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (3128، 3129)، والحاكم (132)."],[325,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer is one who is friendly and easy to befriend. There is no good in one who neither befriends others nor is easily befriended.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (9198)، والبزار (8919)."],[326,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I heard him say: “The Prophet ﷺ commanded us with seven things and prohibited us from seven things. He commanded us to follow funeral processions, visit the sick, accept invitations, support the oppressed, fulfill an oath made on one’s behalf, return the salām, and say ‘yarḥamuk Allah’ to one who sneezes…” to the end of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1239)، ومسلم (2066، 3)."],[327,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you sneezes, let him say: ‘Al-ḥamdu lillāh.’ Then let his brother or companion say to him: ‘Yarḥamuk Allah—may Allah have mercy on you.’ When he says to him, ‘Yarḥamuk Allah,’ let the one who sneezed reply: ‘Yahdīkum Allah wa yuṣliḥu bālakum—may Allah guide you and rectify your affairs.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6224)."],[328,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He responded to one of them and did not respond to the other. The one to whom he did not respond said: “So-and-so sneezed and you said ‘yarḥamuk Allah’ to him, but I sneezed and you did not say it to me.” He replied: “This man praised Allah, while you did not praise Allah.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6221، 6225)، ومسلم (2991)."],[329,"Abū Burdah narrated: I entered upon Abū Mūsā while he was in the house of the daughter of al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās. I sneezed, but he did not say “yarḥamuk Allah” to me. She sneezed, and he did say it to her. I returned to my mother and told her what had happened. When Abū Mūsā later came to her, she said: “My son sneezed in your presence and you did not respond to him, while she sneezed and you responded to her.” He said: “Your son sneezed but did not praise Allah, so I did not respond to him. She sneezed and praised Allah, so I responded to her. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When one of you sneezes and praises Allah, then say “yarḥamuk Allah” to him. If he does not praise Allah, then do not say it to him.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2992)."],[330,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, one of whom was of higher social standing than the other. The man of higher standing sneezed but did not praise Allah, so the Prophet ﷺ did not say “yarḥamuk Allah” to him. The other man sneezed and praised Allah, so the Prophet ﷺ responded to him. The first man said: “I sneezed in your presence and you did not respond to me, while this man sneezed in your presence and you responded to him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “This man remembered Allah, so I remembered him; while you forgot Allah, so I left you without the response.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (8346)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (932)."],[331,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ narrated: A man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, so he said to him: “May Allah have mercy on you.” Then the man sneezed again, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The man has a cold.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2993)."],[332,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sneezed, he would place his hand or his garment over his mouth and lower—or muffle—his voice.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5029)، والترمذي (2745)، وأحمد (9662)."],[333,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. When one of you sneezes and praises Allah, it is a right upon every Muslim who hears him to say, ‘May Allah have mercy on you.’ As for yawning, it is from Satan. So when one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, for when one of you yawns, Satan laughs at him.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6226)."],[334,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yawning is from Satan. When one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2994)."],[335,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters.” In another wording: “When one of you yawns during prayer, let him suppress it as much as he can, for Satan enters.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2995، 57) باللفظ الأول، ورواه (2995، 59) باللفظ الثاني."],[336,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and the one who takes care of an orphan will be in Paradise like this.” He pointed with his index and middle fingers and separated them slightly.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5304)."],[337,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who takes care of an orphan—whether the orphan is related to him or not—and I will be like these two in Paradise.” Mālik pointed with his index and middle fingers.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2983)."],[338,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who strives to support a widow and a poor person is like one who strives in the cause of Allah, or like one who stands in prayer throughout the night and fasts throughout the day.” In another wording: “Like one who stands in prayer without tiring and fasts without breaking his fast.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5353)، ومسلم (2982). واللفظ للبخاري، واللفظ الثاني لمسلم."],[339,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “While a man was in an open stretch of land, he heard a voice coming from a cloud saying: ‘Water the garden of so-and-so.’ The cloud moved away and poured its water onto a rocky tract of land. One channel among the channels collected all of that water. The man followed the water until he found another man standing in his garden directing the water with his shovel. He asked him: ‘O servant of Allah, what is your name?’ He replied with the same name that the man had heard from the cloud. The garden owner then asked: ‘O servant of Allah, why did you ask me my name?’ He replied: ‘I heard a voice in the cloud from which this water came saying: “Water the garden of so-and-so,” mentioning your name. What do you do with this garden?’ He replied: ‘Since you have told me this, I look at what it produces. I give one-third of it in charity, I and my family eat one-third, and I return one-third back into the garden.’” In another wording: “I give one-third to the poor, those who ask, and the stranded traveler.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2984)."],[340,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, I declare inviolable the rights of the two weak ones: the orphan and the woman.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3678)، وأحمد (9666)، وابن حبان (5565)، والحاكم (1/63، 4/128)."],[341,"Abū Shurayḥ al-Khuzāʿī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, I declare inviolable the rights of the two weak ones: the right of the orphan and the right of the woman.”","حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (9105)."],[342,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to our young and recognize the right of our elders is not of us.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4943)، وأحمد (7073)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (354)، والحاكم (209)."],[343,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (353)، وابن أبي الدنيا في النفقة على العيال (186)."],[345,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6014)، ومسلم (2624)."],[346,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6015)، ومسلم (2625، 141)."],[347,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3674)، وأحمد (8046، 9746)."],[348,"A man from the Anṣār narrated: I left my family intending to go to the Prophet ﷺ, and I found him standing with another man who was facing him. I assumed that they had some important matter to discuss. The Anṣārī said: “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained standing for so long that I began to feel pity for him because of the length of the standing.” When the man left, I said: “O Messenger of Allah, that man kept you standing so long that I began to feel sorry for you.” He asked: “Did you see him?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Do you know who he was?” I replied: “No.” He said: “That was Jibrīl, peace be upon him. He continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.” Then he said: “Had you greeted him with salām, he would have returned the salām to you.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (20350، 23093)."],[349,"Abū Umāmah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeatedly advise concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make the neighbor an heir.","حسن: رواه أحمد (22298)."],[350,"Abū Dharr narrated: The Prophet ﷺ, my beloved, advised me: “When you cook broth, increase its water, then look to a household among your neighbors and give them some of it in a good manner.” In another wording: “O Abū Dharr, when you cook broth, increase its water and remember your neighbors by sharing it with them.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2625، 143)، ورواه مسلم أيضا (2625، 142) باللفظ الثاني."],[351,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best companions in the sight of Allah are those who are best to their companions, and the best neighbors in the sight of Allah are those who are best to their neighbors.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (1944)، وأحمد (6566)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (115)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2539)."],[352,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: There was once a time—or a period—when none of us considered himself more entitled to his dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother. But now the dinar and dirham have become more beloved to one of us than his Muslim brother. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “How many a neighbor will cling to his neighbor on the Day of Resurrection and say: ‘My Lord, this man closed his door to me and withheld his kindness from me.’”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (111)."],[353,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr had a sheep slaughtered for his household. When he returned, he asked: “Did you send some as a gift to our Jewish neighbor? Did you send some as a gift to our Jewish neighbor?” Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Jibrīl continued to advise me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5152)، والترمذي (1943) - واللفظ له -، وأحمد (6496)."],[354,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Muslim women, no female neighbor should belittle what she gives to another female neighbor, even if it is only a sheep’s hoof.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6017)، ومسلم (1030)."],[355,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors. To which of them should I give a gift?” He replied: “To the one whose door is closer to yours.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6020)."],[356,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6018)، ومسلم (47، 75)."],[357,"Abū Shurayḥ al-ʿAdawī narrated: My ears heard and my eyes saw when the Prophet ﷺ spoke and said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest with his due hospitality.” It was asked: “What is his due hospitality, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “One day and one night, while hospitality is for three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity for him. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6019)، ومسلم (48، 14، عقب الحديث 1726)."],[358,"Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Hospitality is for three nights, and whatever is beyond that is charity.”","صحيح: رواه البزار (3779)، والطبراني في الكبير (5187)."],[359,"Some men from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should fear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should fear Allah and honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should fear Allah and speak what is true, or remain silent.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (20285، 20286)."],[360,"The Mother of the Believers ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (24404)."],[361,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining about his neighbor. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Go and be patient.” The man came back two or three times, whereupon the Prophet ﷺ said: “Go and place your belongings out on the road.” So he placed his belongings on the road. People began asking him what had happened, and he told them the story. They began cursing the neighbor and saying: “May Allah do such-and-such to him!” Eventually, the neighbor came to him and said: “Go back home. You will never again see from me anything that you dislike.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5153)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (124)، وصححه الحاكم (4/165-166)."],[362,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is mentioned for the abundance of her prayer, fasting, and charity, but she harms her neighbors with her tongue.” He said: “She is in the Fire.” The man then said: “O Messenger of Allah, another woman is mentioned for the small amount of her fasting, charity, and prayer, and she gives pieces of dried curd in charity, but she does not harm her neighbors with her tongue.” He said: “She is in Paradise.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (9675)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (119)، وصححه ابن حبان (5674)."],[363,"Al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked his Companions: “What do you say concerning zinā?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it remains forbidden until the Day of Resurrection.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “For a man to commit zinā with ten women would be less serious for him than committing zinā with the wife of his neighbor.” He then asked: “What do you say concerning theft?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it, so it is forbidden.” He said: “For a man to steal from ten houses would be less serious for him than stealing from his neighbor.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (23854)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (103)، والطبراني في الكبير (20/256)."],[364,"Abū Shurayḥ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “By Allah, he does not believe! By Allah, he does not believe! By Allah, he does not believe!” It was asked: “Who, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “The one whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful conduct.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6016)."],[365,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By Allah, he does not believe! By Allah, he does not believe! By Allah, he does not believe!” They asked: “What does that mean, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “The person whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful conduct.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is meant by his harmful conduct?” He replied: “His evil.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (7878، 8432)، والحاكم (1/101، 4/165)."],[366,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful conduct will not enter Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (46)."],[367,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant’s faith will not become upright until his heart becomes upright, and his heart will not become upright until his tongue becomes upright. And a man whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful conduct will not enter Paradise.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (13048)."],[368,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A neighbor must not prevent his neighbor from inserting his timber into his wall.” Abū Hurayrah would then say: “Why do I see you turning away from this? By Allah, I will certainly throw it between your shoulders”—meaning, “I will certainly narrate it to you.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (34)، والبخاري (2463)، ومسلم (1609)."],[369,"Nāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥārith narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the things that contribute to a person’s happiness are a righteous neighbor, a comfortable means of transportation, and a spacious home.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (15372)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (116)، والحاكم (7306)."],[370,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Four things are from happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious home, a righteous neighbor, and a comfortable means of transportation. And four things are from misery: a bad neighbor, a bad wife, a cramped home, and a bad means of transportation.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (4032)."],[371,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The first two disputants on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbors.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (17372)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 836)."],[373,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: On the Day of Sacrifice, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās riding behind him on the back of his mount. Al-Faḍl was a handsome young man. The Prophet ﷺ stopped to answer people’s religious questions, and a beautiful woman from Khathʿam came forward to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a question. Al-Faḍl began looking at her and was impressed by her beauty. The Prophet ﷺ turned and saw al-Faḍl looking at her, so he reached his hand backward, took hold of al-Faḍl’s chin, and turned his face away from looking at her. She said: “O Messenger of Allah, Allah’s obligation of Ḥajj upon His servants has become due upon my father while he is an elderly man who cannot sit firmly on a riding animal. Will it fulfill the obligation on his behalf if I perform Ḥajj for him?” He replied: “Yes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6228)، ومسلم (1334)."],[374,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās said: I have not seen anything more closely resembling the minor lapses referred to as lamam than what Abū Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah has decreed for the son of Ādam his share of zinā, which he will inevitably encounter. The zinā of the eye is looking, the zinā of the tongue is speaking, and the soul desires and longs; then the private parts either confirm all of that or deny it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6243)، ومسلم (2657، 20)."],[375,"Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about an accidental, sudden glance, and he commanded me to turn my gaze away.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2159)."],[376,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would enter upon him without seeking permission. One day I came and entered upon him, and he said: “My son, a new ruling has now been introduced, so do not enter upon me unless you have permission.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (13176)، وأبو يعلى (4276)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (807)."],[377,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: A man looked through a hole into one of the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ while the Prophet ﷺ had a comb-like instrument with which he was scratching his head. He said: “Had I known that you were looking, I would have stabbed you in the eye with it. Seeking permission was only prescribed because of the gaze.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6241)، ومسلم (2156)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[378,"Anas narrated: A man peered into one of the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ got up holding a sharp arrowhead or several arrowheads. It is as though I can still see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moving stealthily toward the man in order to stab him.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6242)، ومسلم (2157، 42)."],[379,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man were to look into your home without permission, and you threw a pebble at him and put out his eye, there would be no sin upon you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6902)، ومسلم (2158، 44)."],[380,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever peers into the house of a people without their permission, it becomes permissible for them to put out his eye.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2158، 43)."],[381,"Saʿd stood at the door of the Prophet ﷺ seeking permission to enter. He stood directly at the doorway—ʿUthmān said: facing the door. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Stand like this, to the side—or like this—for seeking permission was prescribed because of looking.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5174)."],[382,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Once the gaze has entered, seeking permission is of no benefit.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5173)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1082)، والبيهقي (17660)."],[384,"Anas narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when seeking permission, would give salām three times, and when he spoke a statement he would repeat it three times.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6244)."],[385,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: I was sitting in one of the gatherings of the Anṣār when Abū Mūsā came looking frightened. He said: “I sought permission from ʿUmar three times, but permission was not given to me, so I returned.” ʿUmar asked him: “What prevented you from waiting?” He replied: “I sought permission three times and was not given permission, so I returned, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘If one of you seeks permission three times and permission is not granted, let him return.’” ʿUmar said: “By Allah, you must bring evidence for this. Is there anyone among you who heard this from the Prophet ﷺ?” Ubayy ibn Kaʿb said: “By Allah, only the youngest among us will go with you.” I was the youngest of them, so I went with Abū Mūsā and informed ʿUmar that the Prophet ﷺ had indeed said that.\nIn another narration: We were sitting in a gathering with Ubayy ibn Kaʿb when Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī came angrily and stood before us. He said: “I adjure you by Allah, did any of you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Seeking permission is three times. If permission is granted to you, enter; otherwise, return.’” Ubayy asked: “What happened?” Abū Mūsā replied: “Yesterday I sought permission to enter upon ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb three times, but permission was not given, so I returned. Today I came to him and entered, and I told him that yesterday I had come, given salām three times, and then left.” ʿUmar said: “We heard you, but at that moment we were occupied. Why did you not continue seeking permission until we let you in?” Abū Mūsā replied: “I sought permission in accordance with what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say.” ʿUmar said: “By Allah, I will cause pain to your back and your stomach unless you bring someone who will testify to this for you.” Ubayy ibn Kaʿb said: “By Allah, only the youngest of us will go with you. Get up, O Abū Saʿīd.” So I went until I reached ʿUmar and said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6245)، ومسلم (2153، 33)، والسياق للبخاري."],[386,"Abū Saʿīd narrated: Abū Mūsā came to the door of ʿUmar and sought permission. ʿUmar said: “One.” He sought permission a second time. ʿUmar said: “Two.” He sought permission a third time. ʿUmar said: “Three.” Then Abū Mūsā left. ʿUmar had someone follow him and bring him back, then said: “If this is something you memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then produce it; otherwise, I will make an example of you.” Abū Saʿīd said: Abū Mūsā came to us and said: “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Seeking permission is three times’?” They began laughing. I said: “Your Muslim brother has come to you frightened, and you are laughing? Come, I will share with you in this punishment.” So I went with him to ʿUmar, and he said: “This is Abū Saʿīd.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2153، 35)."],[387,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: Abū Mūsā came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and said: “Peace be upon you. This is ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays.” Permission was not given. He said: “Peace be upon you. This is Abū Mūsā.” Then: “Peace be upon you. This is al-Ashʿarī.” Then he left. ʿUmar said: “Bring him back to me! Bring him back to me!” When Abū Mūsā returned, ʿUmar asked: “O Abū Mūsā, why did you leave? We were occupied.” He replied: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Seeking permission is three times. If permission is granted to you, enter; otherwise, return.’” ʿUmar said: “You must bring me evidence for this, or else I will do such-and-such to you.” So Abū Mūsā went away. ʿUmar said: “If he finds evidence, you will find him by the minbar this evening. If he does not find evidence, you will not find him there.” When evening came, they found him there. ʿUmar asked: “O Abū Mūsā, what do you say? Have you found someone?” He replied: “Yes, Ubayy ibn Kaʿb.” ʿUmar said: “He is trustworthy.” Then he asked: “O Abū al-Ṭufayl, what do you say concerning what this man says?” Ubayy said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that. O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, do not become a hardship upon the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” ʿUmar replied: “Subḥānallāh! I merely heard something and wished to verify it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2154، 37)."],[388,"ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr narrated: Abū Mūsā sought permission to enter upon ʿUmar three times. It seemed that he found ʿUmar occupied, so he returned. ʿUmar then said: “Did I not hear the voice of ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays? Give him permission.” So Abū Mūsā was called back. ʿUmar asked: “What made you do what you did?” He replied: “We used to be commanded to do this.” ʿUmar said: “You must produce evidence for this, or else I will take action.” So Abū Mūsā went out and came to a gathering of the Anṣār. They said: “Only the youngest among us will testify for you concerning this.” Abū Saʿīd stood and said: “We used to be commanded to do this.” ʿUmar then said: “This matter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ escaped my knowledge. Business dealings in the marketplaces distracted me from it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7353)، ومسلم (2153، 36)."],[389,"Anas—or another narrator—reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought permission to enter upon Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah and said: “Peace and the mercy of Allah be upon you.” Saʿd replied: “And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah,” but the Prophet ﷺ did not hear him. The Prophet ﷺ gave salām three times, and Saʿd responded three times without making his response audible to him. The Prophet ﷺ then turned to leave. Saʿd followed him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you! You did not give a single salām except that I heard it. I responded to you, but I did not let you hear me because I wanted to receive more of your salām and its blessing.” Then he brought the Prophet ﷺ into his house and offered him raisins. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ ate from them. When he finished, he said: “May the righteous eat your food, may the angels invoke blessings upon you, and may fasting people break their fast with you.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (12406) عن عبد الرزاق، وهو في مصنفه (19425)."],[390,"Kaldah ibn Ḥanbal narrated: Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ carrying milk, a young gazelle, and ḍaghābīs, while the Prophet ﷺ was in the upper part of Makkah. I entered without giving salām. He said: “Go back and say: ‘Peace be upon you.’” This occurred after Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah had embraced Islam.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5176)، والترمذي (2710)، والنسائي في الكبرى (6702)، وأحمد (15425)."],[391,"A man from Banū ʿĀmir narrated: He sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: “May I enter?” The Prophet ﷺ said to his servant: “Go out to him, for he does not know how to seek permission properly. Tell him to say: ‘Peace be upon you. May I enter?’” The man said: I heard him say that, so I said: “Peace be upon you. May I enter?” Then permission was granted to me—or he said: I entered.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23127) - واللفظ له -، وأبو داود (5179)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (316)."],[392,"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in an upper room and said: “Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. Peace be upon you. May ʿUmar enter?”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5201)، والنسائي في الكبرى (10080)."],[393,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Your permission to enter upon me is that the curtain be raised and that you hear my private conversation, until I tell you otherwise.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2169)."],[394,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I entered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he found some milk in a bowl. He said: “O Abū Hirr, go to the people of al-Ṣuffah and invite them to come to me.” I went to them and invited them. They came, sought permission to enter, and when permission was granted they entered.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6246)."],[395,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man’s messenger to another man constitutes his permission.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5189)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1076)."],[396,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you is invited to a meal and comes along with the messenger who invited him, then that itself constitutes permission for him to enter.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5190)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1075)، والإمام أحمد (10894)."],[397,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the door of a people, he would not stand directly facing the doorway. Rather, he would stand to its right side or left side and say: “Peace be upon you. Peace be upon you.” That was because houses at that time did not have curtains covering their entrances.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5186)، وأحمد (17694)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1078)."],[398,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ concerning a debt that was owed by my father and knocked on the door. He asked: “Who is it?” I replied: “It is me.” He said: “Me, me?” as though he disliked that answer.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6250)، ومسلم (2155)."],[399,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you visits his brother and sits with him, he should not get up to leave until he seeks his permission.”","حسن: رواه أبو الشيخ في طبقات المحدثين بأصبهان (2/205)."],[400,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah created Ādam upon his form, and his height was sixty cubits. When He created him, He said: ‘Go and greet that group of angels who are sitting there, and listen to how they greet you, for that will be your greeting and the greeting of your descendants.’ So Ādam said: ‘Peace be upon you.’ They replied: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,’ adding, ‘and the mercy of Allah.’ Everyone who enters Paradise will be in the form of Ādam, and mankind has continued to decrease in stature since then until now.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6227)، ومسلم (2841)."],[401,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: When we prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, we used to say: “Peace be upon Allah before His servants. Peace be upon Jibrīl. Peace be upon Mīkāʾīl. Peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he turned his face toward us and said: “Indeed, Allah is al-Salām. When one of you sits in prayer, let him say: ‘All greetings belong to Allah, as do all prayers and all pure words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.’ For when he says that, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens and the earth. Then he should say: ‘I testify that there is no deity except Allah, and I testify that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger.’ After that, he may choose whatever supplication he wishes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6230)، ومسلم (402)."],[402,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, al-Salām is one of the Names of Allah, the Exalted, which Allah has placed upon the earth, so spread salām among yourselves.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (989)."],[403,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, al-Salām is one of the Names of Allah which He has placed upon the earth, so spread it among yourselves. When a man gives salām to a group and they return it, he has a degree of superiority over them because he was the one who reminded them of it. If they do not return his salām, then those who are better and purer than them will return it to him.”","حسن: رواه البزار (1770)، والطبراني في الكبير (10391)، وابن حبان في روضة العقلاء (ص 74)."],[404,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things: Visiting the sick, following funeral processions, saying “yarḥamuk Allah” to one who sneezes, supporting the weak, helping the oppressed, spreading salām, and fulfilling the oath of one who adjures another… to the end of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6235)، ومسلم (2066)."],[405,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not truly believe until you love one another. Shall I not direct you to something which, if you do it, will cause you to love one another? Spread salām among yourselves.” In another wording: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (54)."],[406,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, whenever I see you, my soul feels good and my eyes are comforted. So tell me about everything.” He said: “Everything was created from water.” I then said: “Tell me of an action which, if I hold firmly to it, will cause me to enter Paradise.” He replied: “Spread salām, feed people, maintain kinship ties, and stand in prayer at night while people are asleep; then enter Paradise in peace.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (7932)، وصححه ابن حبان (508، 2559)، والحاكم (7174)."],[407,"Abū Umāmah narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to spread salām.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3693)، وأبو بكر بن أبي شيبة (26251)، والطبراني في الكبير (8/130-131)."],[408,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Spread salām and you will be safe, and arrogance and insolence are evil.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (18530)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (787، 1266)، وصححه ابن حبان (491)."],[409,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, the people rushed toward him, and it was announced: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has arrived!” I came among the people to look at him. When I clearly saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I knew that his face was not the face of a liar. The first words I heard him say were: “O people, spread salām, feed people, and pray at night while people are asleep; you will enter Paradise in peace.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2485)، وابن ماجه (1334)، وأحمد (23784)، والحاكم (7277)."],[410,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Spread salām, feed people, and be brothers as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded you.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3252)، وأحمد (6450)."],[411,"Hāniʾ ibn Yazīd narrated: I asked the Prophet ﷺ: “Tell me what will make Paradise obligatory for me?” He replied:","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (811)، وابن حبان (504) - واللفظ له."],[412,"Abū Umāmah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people most deserving of closeness to Allah are those who begin by giving salām.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5197)."],[413,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one who begins with salām is free of the sin of severing ties and estrangement.”","حسن: رواه أبو نعيم في حلية الأولياء (9/25)."],[414,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not greet with the greeting of the Jews and Christians, for their greeting is by means of the hands, the head, and gestures.”","حسن: رواه النسائي في السنن الكبرى (10100)."],[415,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Which aspect of Islam is best?” He replied: “That you feed people and give salām to those whom you know and those whom you do not know.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6236)، ومسلم (39)."],[416,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rider should give salām to the one who is walking, the one who is walking to the one who is sitting, and the smaller group to the larger group.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6232-6233)، ومسلم (2160)."],[417,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The younger should give salām to the older, the one passing by to the one sitting, and the smaller group to the larger group.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6231)."],[418,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mounted person should give salām to the one walking, the one walking to the one standing, and the smaller group to the larger group.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2705)، وأحمد (23940)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (998)."],[419,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rider should give salām to the one on foot, the one on foot to the one sitting, and the smaller number to the larger number. Whoever returns the salām receives its reward, and whoever does not return it has nothing.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (15666)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (992)."],[420,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The rider should give salām to the one walking, and the one walking to the one sitting. When two people are both walking, whichever of them begins with salām is better.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (2006)، وصححه ابن حبان (498)."],[421,"Sayyār narrated: I was walking with Thābit al-Bunānī when he passed by some children and gave them salām. Thābit narrated that he had been walking with Anas when Anas passed by some children and gave them salām. Anas in turn narrated that he had been walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he passed by some children and gave them salām.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6247)، ومسلم (2168، 15)."],[422,"Anas narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me while I was playing with some boys. He gave us salām, then sent me on an errand. I was delayed in returning to my mother. When I came back, she asked: “What kept you?” I replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand.” She asked: “What was his errand?” I replied: “It is a secret.” She said: “Never disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to anyone.” Anas said: “By Allah, if I were ever going to tell it to anyone, I would have told you, O Thābit.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2482، 145)."],[423,"Sahl narrated: “We used to rejoice on Fridays.” I asked: “Why?” He replied: There was an elderly woman among us who would send someone to Buḍāʿah—an area of date palms in Madinah, as Ibn Maslamah explained—and she would take the roots of chard, place them in a pot, and add crushed grains of barley. After we had prayed Jumuʿah, we would leave, give her salām, and she would serve it to us. We used to rejoice because of that. We would not take our midday nap or eat lunch until after Jumuʿah.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6248)، ومسلم (859)."],[424,"Asmāʾ bint Yazīd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by us while we were a group of women, and he gave us salām.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5204)، وابن ماجه (3701)، وأحمد (27561)."],[425,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you meets his brother, let him give him salām. If a tree, wall, or rock comes between them and then he meets him again, let him give him salām again.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5600)، وأبو يعلى (6351)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (2072)."],[426,"Anas narrated: “When we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and a tree came between us so that we became separated, then when we met again we would give salām to one another.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (7983)."],[427,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you comes to a gathering, let him give salām. When he wishes to get up and leave, let him give salām. The first greeting is no more deserving than the latter.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5208)، والترمذي (2706)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1007، 1008)."],[428,"ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Peace be upon you.” The Prophet ﷺ returned his greeting, and the man sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Ten.” Then another man came and said: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ returned his greeting, and the man sat down. He said: “Twenty.” Then another man came and said: “Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.” The Prophet ﷺ returned his greeting, and the man sat down. He said: “Thirty.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5195)، والترمذي (2689)، وأحمد (19948)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (337)."],[429,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting in a gathering and said: “Peace be upon you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Ten good deeds.” Another man passed and said: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.” He said: “Twenty good deeds.” Then another man passed and said: “Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.” He said: “Thirty good deeds.” Then a man got up from the gathering and left without giving salām. The Prophet ﷺ said: “How quickly your companion forgot! When one of you comes to a gathering, let him give salām. If he then wishes to sit, let him sit. And when he gets up to leave, let him give salām. The first greeting is no more deserving than the latter.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (986)، وصححه ابن حبان (493)."],[430,"Abū Jurayy Jābir ibn Sulaym narrated: I saw a man whose judgment the people followed. He would not say anything except that they acted upon it. I asked: “Who is this?” They replied: “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said twice: “Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do not say, ‘Upon you be peace,’ for ‘upon you be peace’ is the greeting of the dead. Rather say: ‘Peace be upon you.’” I asked: “Are you the Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “I am the Messenger of Allah. He is the One whom, if harm afflicts you and you call upon Him, He removes it from you; and if a year of drought afflicts you and you call upon Him, He causes the earth to grow for you; and if you are in a barren land—or wilderness—and your riding animal becomes lost, then you call upon Him and He returns it to you.” I said: “Give me some instruction.” He said: “Never insult anyone.” Jābir said: “After that I never insulted a free person, a slave, a camel, or a sheep.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not belittle any good deed, even speaking to your brother while your face is cheerful toward him, for that is part of goodness. Raise your lower garment to the middle of your shin; if you refuse, then at least to the ankles. Beware of letting the lower garment trail beneath the ankles, for that is from arrogance, and Allah does not love arrogance. If a man insults you and shames you for something he knows about you, do not shame him for something you know about him, for the burden of that will fall upon him.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4084) - واللفظ له -، والترمذي (2722)، والبيهقي في الشعب (5730)."],[431,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in one part of it. The man prayed, then came and greeted him with salām. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “And upon you be peace. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” So the man went back and prayed, then came and greeted him again. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “And upon you be peace. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.” On the second occasion—or a later one—the man said: “Teach me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “When you stand for prayer, perform your wuḍūʾ thoroughly. Then face the qiblah and say the takbīr. Then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur’an. Then bow until you are at rest in bowing. Then rise until you are standing upright. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then rise until you are at rest while sitting. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then rise until you are at rest while sitting. Then do that throughout your entire prayer.” Abū Usāmah said that in the final wording it says: “Until you are standing upright.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6251)، ومسلم (397)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[432,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥasan ibn Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated from his father, from his grandfather: It was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, if a group comes to a house and one of them seeks permission, is that sufficient for all of them?” He replied: “Yes.” It was asked: “If one man from the people of the house responds, is that sufficient on behalf of all of them?” He replied: “Yes.” It was asked: “If a group passes by and one of them gives salām, is that sufficient on behalf of all of them?” He replied: “Yes.” It was asked: “If one person from the other group returns the salām, is that sufficient for all of them?” He replied: “Yes.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (2730)."],[433,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿĀ’ishah, this is Jibrīl sending you salām.” She said: “And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah. You see what we do not see.” She meant the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6249)، ومسلم (2447، 91)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[434,"Jābir narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “So-and-so has a date-palm cluster in my garden, and its location has caused me harm and hardship.” The Prophet ﷺ sent for the owner and said: “Sell me your date-palm cluster that is in so-and-so’s garden.” He replied: “No.” He said: “Then give it to me as a gift.” He replied: “No.” He said: “Then sell it to me in exchange for a date-palm cluster in Paradise.” He replied: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ then said: “I have not seen anyone more miserly than you except the one who is miserly with salām.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (14517)."],[435,"Al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad narrated: Two companions and I came in such a state of exhaustion and hunger that our hearing and sight had been affected. We began presenting ourselves to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but none of them was able to take us in. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he took us to his household. There were three goats there. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Milk them and divide the milk among us.” So we would milk them. Each of us would drink his own share, and we would set aside the share of the Prophet ﷺ for him. He would come during the night and give salām in such a manner that he would not awaken a sleeping person, while one who was awake could hear him. Then he would go to the mosque and pray, after which he would come to his drink and drink it. One night, after I had drunk my own share, Satan came to me and said: “Muḥammad goes to the Anṣār, and they give him gifts and food. He has no need for this little drink.” So I went to his portion and drank it. Once it had settled in my stomach and I knew there was no way to return it, Satan made me regret what I had done. He said: “Woe to you! What have you done? You drank Muḥammad’s drink! He will come and not find it, then he will supplicate against you and you will be destroyed, losing both your worldly life and your Hereafter.” I had only a small cloak. When I covered my feet with it, my head was exposed, and when I covered my head, my feet were exposed. Sleep would not come to me. As for my two companions, they slept because they had not done what I had done. Then the Prophet ﷺ came and gave salām just as he normally did. He went to the mosque and prayed, then came to his drink and uncovered it, but found nothing there. He raised his head toward the sky. I thought: “Now he will supplicate against me and I will be destroyed.” But he said: “O Allah, feed whoever feeds me, and give drink to whoever gives me drink.” I immediately took my cloak and tied it tightly around myself, picked up a knife, and went toward the goats to find the fattest one so that I could slaughter it for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. But I found one of them with a full udder, and in fact all of them had full udders. So I took a vessel belonging to the household of Muḥammad ﷺ, one which they would never have expected to fill with milk, and I milked into it until foam rose over its top. Then I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He asked: “Have you drunk your share tonight?” I replied: “O Messenger of Allah, drink.” So he drank and handed the vessel back to me. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, drink.” He drank again and handed it back to me. When I realized that the Prophet ﷺ had drunk his fill and that I had received the benefit of his supplication, I began laughing until I fell to the ground. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This must be one of your mischievous acts, O Miqdād.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is what happened to me, and I did such-and-such.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “This was nothing but a mercy from Allah. Why did you not inform me so that we could wake our two companions and they too could have some of it?” I replied: “By the One who sent you with the truth, once you and I have received it together, I do not care who else among the people receives it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2055)."],[436,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: A man passed by while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was urinating and gave him salām, but the Prophet ﷺ did not return his greeting.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (370)."],[437,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not initiate the Jews or Christians with salām. If you meet one of them on a road, then make him take its narrower side.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2167)."],[438,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: A group of Jews entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Al-sāmu ʿalaykum” — meaning, “Death be upon you.” I understood what they had said, so I replied: “And upon you be death and the curse.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gently, O ʿĀ’ishah. Indeed, Allah loves gentleness in every matter.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not hear what they said?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “I already said: ‘And upon you.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6256)، ومسلم (2165)."],[439,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of the Jews greets you, he may only be saying, ‘Death be upon you,’ so say: ‘And upon you.’”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (3)، والبخاري (6257)، ومسلم (2164)."],[440,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: Some Jews greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: “Death be upon you, O Abū al-Qāsim.” He replied: “And upon you.” ʿĀ’ishah became angry and said: “Did you not hear what they said?” He replied: “Yes, I heard them and returned it upon them. Our supplication against them is answered, while their supplication against us is not answered.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2166)."],[441,"Abū Baṣrah al-Ghifārī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them one day: “I am going to ride to the Jews. Whoever comes with me, if they greet you, then say: ‘And upon you.’” So we went with him. When we came to them, they greeted us, and we replied: “And upon you.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (27235) - واللفظ له -، والنسائي في الكبرى (10148)."],[442,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When the People of the Book greet you, say: ‘And upon you.’” In another wording of Muslim, the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: “The People of the Book greet us. How should we respond to them?” He replied: “Say: ‘And upon you.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6258)، ومسلم (2163، 6). ورواه مسلم (2163، 7) باللفظ الثاني."],[443,"Anas narrated: A Jewish man passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Death be upon you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “And upon you.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Do you know what he said? He said: ‘Death be upon you.’” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill him?” He replied: “No. When the People of the Book greet you, say: ‘And upon you.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6926)."],[444,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Some Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Death be upon you, O Abū al-Qāsim.” He replied: “And upon you.” ʿĀ’ishah said: “Rather, upon you be death and disgrace.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿĀ’ishah, do not be obscene in speech.” She replied: “Did you not hear what they said?” He said: “Did I not return upon them what they said? I said: ‘And upon you.’” In another narration, ʿĀ’ishah understood what they meant and insulted them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Enough, O ʿĀ’ishah. Indeed, Allah does not love obscenity or deliberately obscene speech.” The narration adds that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “And when they come to you, they greet you with that by which Allah has not greeted you…” [Sūrat al-Mujādilah 58:8] to the end of the verse.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2165، 11)."],[445,"Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ mounted a donkey which had a saddle upon it, beneath which was a Fadakī cloak. He seated Usāmah ibn Zayd behind him and went to visit Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah among Banū al-Ḥārith ibn al-Khazraj. This was before the Battle of Badr. He passed by a gathering containing a mixture of Muslims, polytheists who worshipped idols, and Jews. Among them was ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl, and ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah was also in the gathering. When the dust raised by the animal reached the gathering, ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy covered his nose with his cloak and said: “Do not cover us with dust.” The Prophet ﷺ gave them salām, then stopped and dismounted. He called them to Allah and recited the Qur’an to them. ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl said: “O man, there is nothing better than this if what you say is true, but do not disturb us with it in our gatherings. Return to your own place, and whoever comes to you from among us, tell it to him.” ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah said: “Rather, come to us in our gatherings, for we love that.” The Muslims, polytheists, and Jews then began insulting one another until they nearly came to blows. The Prophet ﷺ continued calming them until they settled down. Then he mounted his animal and went to Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah. He said: “O Saʿd, did you not hear what Abū Ḥubāb said?” meaning ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy. He then told him what he had said. Saʿd replied: “Pardon him, O Messenger of Allah, and overlook it. By Allah, Allah has given you what He has given you. The people of this settlement had agreed to crown him and bind the royal turban upon him. But when Allah prevented that through the truth He gave you, he choked with resentment over it. That is what caused him to behave as you saw.” So the Prophet ﷺ pardoned him.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6254)، ومسلم (1798)."],[446,"Qatādah narrated: I asked Anas: “Was handshaking practiced among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?” He replied: “Yes.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6263)."],[447,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of Yemen have come to you. Their hearts are softer than yours.” And they were the first to introduce handshaking.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5213)، وأحمد (13212)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (967)."],[448,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tomorrow, people will come to you whose hearts are softer toward Islam than yours.” Then the Ashʿarīs arrived, among them Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī. As they drew near to Madinah, they began chanting: “Tomorrow we shall meet the beloved ones— Muḥammad and his party.” When they arrived, they shook hands with one another, and they were the first to establish the practice of handshaking.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (12582)، وصححه ابن حبان (7193)."],[449,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No two Muslims meet and shake hands except that they are forgiven before they part.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5212)، والترمذي (2727)، وابن ماجه (3703)، وأحمد (18547)."],[450,"Umaymah bint Ruqayqah narrated: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of women who pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we pledge allegiance to you that we will not associate anything with Allah, we will not steal, we will not commit zinā, we will not kill our children, we will not fabricate a false accusation between our hands and feet, and we will not disobey you in what is right.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “According to what you are able and capable of.” She said: We replied: “Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. Come, O Messenger of Allah, let us pledge allegiance to you by hand.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I do not shake hands with women. My statement to one hundred women is the same as my statement to one woman—or like my statement to a single woman.”","صحيح: رواه مالك (2)، ورواه الترمذي (1597)، والنسائي (4181)، وابن ماجه (2874)."],[451,"Asmāʾ bint Yazīd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the believing women to pledge allegiance. Asmāʾ said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not extend your hand to us?” He replied: “I do not shake hands with women.”","حسن: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه كما في المطالب (2109) - واللفظ له."],[452,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Hishām narrated: “We were with the Prophet ﷺ while he was holding the hand of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6264)."],[453,"Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him and said: “O Ḥudhayfah, give me your hand.” Ḥudhayfah withheld his hand. The Prophet ﷺ asked him a second time, then a third time, and said: “What is preventing you?” Ḥudhayfah replied: “I am in a state of janābah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “When a believer meets another believer and takes him by the hand, their sins fall away just as the leaves of a tree fall away.”","حسن: رواه ابن وهب في الجامع (250)."],[454,"Salmān al-Fārisī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When a Muslim meets his Muslim brother and takes him by the hand, their sins fall away from them just as leaves fall from a dry tree on a day of strong wind; otherwise, they are forgiven even if their sins are like the foam of the sea.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (6150)، والبيهقي في الشعب (8549)."],[455,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No two Muslims meet and one takes the hand of the other except that it becomes a right upon Allah to answer their supplication, and He does not let their hands separate until He has forgiven them.”","حسن: رواه البزار (6463)، وأبو يعلى (4139)."],[456,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the tashahhud while my hand was between his two hands, just as he would teach me a sūrah from the Qur’an.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6265)، ومسلم (402، 59)."],[457,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bid farewell to a man, he would take his hand and would not release it until the man himself released the hand of the Prophet ﷺ. He would say: “I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the conclusion of your deeds.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (3442، 3443)، وأبو داود (2600)، وابن ماجه (2826)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2531)."],[458,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: No one would take the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and have the Prophet ﷺ pull his hand away first; rather, the other man would be the one to release it. Nor would his knees—or his knee—be seen protruding beyond the knees of the person sitting beside him. Whenever someone shook his hand, he would turn his face fully toward him and would not turn away until the man had finished speaking.","حسن: رواه البزار في مسنده (8548)، والطبراني في الأوسط (8688)."],[459,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: “I never saw a man place his mouth close to the ear of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak privately with him and have the Prophet ﷺ move his head away first; rather, the man himself would be the one to move away. And I never saw a man take his hand and have the Prophet ﷺ release it first; rather, the man himself would be the one to let go.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4794)، والترمذي (2490)، وابن ماجه (3716)، وابن حبان (6435)."],[460,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I entered with Abū Bakr upon his family and found his daughter ʿĀ’ishah lying down with a fever. I saw her father kiss her cheek and say: “How are you, my daughter?”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (3918)."],[461,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī while al-Aqraʿ ibn Ḥābis al-Tamīmī was sitting with him. Al-Aqraʿ said: “I have ten children and I have never kissed any of them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5997)، ومسلم (2318)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[462,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Some Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked: “Do you kiss your children?” They replied: “Yes.” The Bedouins said: “By Allah, we do not kiss ours.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What can I do if Allah has removed mercy from you?” In another wording: “…removed mercy from your heart?”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5998)، ومسلم (2317)."],[463,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Then he—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—said: “Rejoice, O ʿĀ’ishah, for Allah has revealed your vindication.” He then recited the Qur’an to her. Her parents said: “Get up and kiss the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She replied: “I praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, not the two of you.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5219)، ومن طريقه البيهقي (13579)."],[464,"ʿĀ’ishah, the Mother of the Believers, narrated: “I never saw anyone more closely resemble the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in demeanor, manner, and conduct—in her standing and sitting—than Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said: When Fāṭimah entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would stand up for her, kiss her, and seat her in his own place. And when the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her, she would stand from her place, kiss him, and seat him in her own place… to the end of the hadith.","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3872)، وابن المقرئ في الرخصة في تقبيل اليد (26)، والحاكم (7715)."],[465,"Usāmah ibn Sharīk narrated: “We stood up to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and kissed his hand.”","حسن: رواه المحاملي في أماليه (247)، وأبو بكر بن المقرئ في الرخصة في تقبيل اليد (2)، والخطيب في الجامع لأخلاق الراوي (314)."],[466,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā narrated from his father: Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr was a righteous, cheerful, pleasant man. While he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ speaking to the people and making them laugh, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poked him in the side. Usayd said: “You hurt me.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Take your retaliation.” Usayd said: “O Messenger of Allah, you are wearing a shirt, while I was not wearing one.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted his shirt. Usayd embraced him and began kissing his side. He said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. This is what I wanted.”","حسن: رواه الحاكم (5262)، وعنه البيهقي (16021)."],[467,"Abū Juḥayfah Wahb ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Suwāʾī narrated: When Jaʿfar returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed him between the eyes and then said: “I do not know which makes me happier: the arrival of Jaʿfar or the conquest of Khaybar.”","حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (364)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 244)."],[468,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Razīn narrated: We passed through al-Rabadhah and were told: “Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ is here.” So we went to him and gave him salām. He extended his two hands and said: “With these two hands I pledged allegiance to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ.” He had a large palm, as though it were the palm of a camel. So we rose toward it and kissed it.","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (16551)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (973)."],[469,"Jābir narrated: The Prophet ﷺ would place two of those martyred at Uḥud together in one grave, then ask: “Which of these two had taken in more of the Qur’an?” When one of them was pointed out, he would place him first in the burial niche.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (1343)."],[470,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, part of honoring Allah is honoring an elderly Muslim, honoring a bearer of the Qur’an who neither goes to excess concerning it nor neglects it, and honoring a just ruler.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4843)."],[471,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: When the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Welcome to the delegation who have come neither disgraced nor regretful…” to the end of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6176)، ومسلم (17، 24)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[472,"Abū Murrah, the freedman of Umm Hāniʾ bint Abī Ṭālib, narrated that he heard Umm Hāniʾ bint Abī Ṭālib say: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Year of the Conquest and found him bathing while his daughter Fāṭimah was screening him. I gave him salām. He asked: “Who is this?” I replied: “I am Umm Hāniʾ bint Abī Ṭālib.” He said: “Welcome, Umm Hāniʾ.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (357)، ومسلم (336، 82)."],[473,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmrah al-Anṣārī narrated: Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī was informed of a funeral. It seems that he was delayed until the people had already taken their seats. Then he arrived. When the people saw him, they quickly made room for him, and some of them stood up so that he could sit in their places. He said: “No. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The best gatherings are the most spacious.’” Then he moved aside and sat in a spacious place.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4820)، وأحمد (11137)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1136)."],[474,"Abū Wāqid al-Laythī narrated: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque with the people around him, three men approached. Two of them came toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while one went away. When the two stood at the gathering of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they gave salām. One of them saw an open space in the circle and sat there. The other sat behind the people. As for the third, he turned away and left. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished, he said: “Shall I tell you about the three men? One of them sought refuge with Allah, so Allah gave him refuge. The second felt shy, so Allah showed modesty toward him. As for the third, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (4)، والبخاري (66)، ومسلم (2176)."],[475,"Jābir ibn Samurah narrated: “When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, each one of us would sit wherever the gathering ended.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4825)، والترمذي (2725)، وأحمد (20855)، وصححه ابن حبان (6432)."],[477,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man should not make another man get up from his seat and then sit in his place. Rather, make room and spread out.” Another narration adds: “He disliked that a man should get up from his seat so that another person could sit in his place.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6270)، ومسلم (2177، 28). واللفظ للبخاري، والزيادة للبخاري أيضا."],[478,"Jābir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should make his brother get up from his place on Friday and then move into his seat and sit there. Rather, he should say: ‘Make room.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2178)."],[479,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A man should not make another man leave his place and then sit there himself. Rather, make room, and Allah will make room for you.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (10776)."],[480,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a man to separate two people who are sitting together except with their permission.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4845)، والترمذي (2752)، وأحمد (6999)."],[481,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man should not sit between another man and his son.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (3051)، وعلي بن الجعد في مسنده (2947)."],[482,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you gets up from his seat and then returns to it, he has more right to it.” In another wording: “Whoever gets up from his seat and then returns to it has more right to it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2179)."],[483,"Wahb ibn Ḥudhayfah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If a man gets up from his place and then returns to it, he has more right to it. Even if he gets up to attend to some need and then returns, he has more right to it.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2751)، وأحمد (15484)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (1277)."],[484,"Abū Rifāʿah narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, a stranger has come asking about his religion, for he does not know what his religion is.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward me and left the sermon until he came to me. A chair was brought for him, and I thought its legs were made of iron. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on it and began teaching me from what Allah had taught him. Then he returned to his sermon and completed its remaining portion.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (876)."],[485,"Buraydah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited sitting in a place that is partly shaded and partly exposed to the sun.","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3722)."],[486,"A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited sitting between direct sunlight and shade, and said: “It is the sitting place of Satan.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (15421)."],[487,"Al-Sharīd ibn Suwayd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was sitting like this: I had placed my left hand behind my back and was leaning on the fleshy base of my palm. He said: “Are you sitting in the manner of those upon whom wrath has been incurred?”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4848)، وأحمد (19454)، وصححه ابن حبان (5674)، والحاكم (4/269)."],[488,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the courtyard of the Kaʿbah, sitting in the iḥtibāʾ posture while holding his legs with his hands, like this.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6272)."],[489,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said three times: “Shall I inform you of the greatest of the major sins?” They replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Associating partners with Allah and disobedience to parents.” Then he sat upright after having been reclining and said: “And indeed, false speech!” He continued repeating it until we thought: “If only he would stop.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2654)، ومسلم (87)."],[490,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was informed about my fasting, so he entered upon me. I placed a leather cushion for him stuffed with palm fiber, but he sat on the ground, leaving the cushion between me and him… Then he mentioned the remainder of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6277)، ومسلم (1159، 191)."],[491,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jaḥsh, he invited the people. They ate and then remained sitting, talking. He began acting as though he were preparing to get up, but they did not leave. When he saw that, he stood up. When he stood, some of the people stood and left with him, while three remained behind. The Prophet ﷺ later came back intending to enter, but those people were still sitting there. Eventually, they got up and left. Anas said: I went and informed the Prophet ﷺ that they had departed. He came and entered. I went to enter after him, but he lowered the curtain between me and him. Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed: “O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you…” until His saying: “…Indeed, that would be, in the sight of Allah, an enormous matter.” [Sūrat al-Aḥzāb 33:53]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6271)، ومسلم (1428، 92)."],[492,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man tells another person something and then looks around, it is a trust.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4868)، والترمذي (1959)، وأحمد (14474)."],[493,"ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah narrated: I was a young boy under the care of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my hand used to wander around the dish. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Young boy, mention the Name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is nearest to you.” That remained my manner of eating thereafter.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5376)، ومسلم (2022، 108)."],[494,"Ḥudhayfah narrated: Whenever we attended a meal with the Prophet ﷺ, we would not put our hands into the food until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began and placed his hand in it. On one occasion we were present with him at a meal when a young girl came rushing as though she were being pushed. She went to put her hand into the food, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of her hand. Then a Bedouin came rushing as though he too were being pushed, so the Prophet ﷺ took hold of his hand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Satan considers food lawful for himself when the Name of Allah is not mentioned over it. He brought this girl so that he might make the food lawful through her, but I took hold of her hand. Then he brought this Bedouin so that he might make it lawful through him, but I took hold of his hand. By the One in whose hand is my soul, his hand is in my hand along with hers.” Another narration adds: Then he mentioned the Name of Allah and ate.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2017، 102)."],[495,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When a man enters his house and mentions Allah when entering and when eating, Satan says: ‘You have no lodging here tonight and no dinner.’ But if he enters without mentioning Allah upon entering, Satan says: ‘You have obtained lodging.’ And if he does not mention Allah when eating, Satan says: ‘You have obtained both lodging and dinner.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2018)."],[496,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever forgets to mention Allah at the beginning of his meal should say when he remembers: ‘In the Name of Allah at its beginning and its end.’ He thereby begins his meal anew, and the wicked one is prevented from what he had been taking from it.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (5213)، وابن السني (460)، والطبراني في الكبير (10354)."],[497,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.”","صحيح: رواه مالك (1931 - موطأ برواية أبي مصعب الزهري)، ورواه مسلم (2020، 105)."],[498,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.”","حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة في المصنف (24439)، وأحمد (13097)، وأبو يعلى (4772-4774)."],[499,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Let one of you eat with his right hand, drink with his right hand, take with his right hand, and give with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand, drinks with his left hand, gives with his left hand, and takes with his left hand.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3266)."],[500,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2019)."],[501,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should eat with his left hand or drink with it, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2020، 106)."],[502,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from eating with his left hand, walking while wearing only one sandal, wrapping himself in the ṣammāʾ manner, and sitting in the iḥtibāʾ posture in a single garment while exposing his private parts.","صحيح: رواه مالك (5)، ورواه مسلم (2099، 70)."],[503,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ narrated: A man ate with his left hand in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to him: “Eat with your right hand.” The man replied: “I cannot.” He said: “May you never be able to.” Nothing prevented him except arrogance. Salamah said: “After that, he was never able to raise that hand to his mouth.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2021)."],[504,"ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah narrated: One day I ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began taking meat from different parts around the dish. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Eat from what is nearest to you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5377)، ومسلم (2022، 109)."],[505,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was brought a bowl of tharīd and said: “Eat from around its edges and do not eat from its middle, for blessing descends upon its middle.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3772)، وأحمد (3190) - والسياق له."],[506,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr al-Māzinī narrated: My father sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to invite him to a meal. He came with me. When I drew near to the house, I hurried ahead and informed my parents. They came out to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, welcomed him, and laid out for him a woolly cloak we had. He sat upon it. My father then said to my mother: “Bring your food.” She brought a bowl containing flour that she had mixed and thickened with water and salt and placed it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “In the Name of Allah, eat from around its edges and leave its top, for the blessing is in it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate, and we ate with him, yet some food remained. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive them, have mercy on them, bless them, and expand their provision.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (17678)، وابن حبان (5299)."],[507,"Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ narrated: I was among the people of al-Ṣuffah. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a round loaf of bread. He broke it into a bowl, poured hot water over it, added fat, mixed it thoroughly, blended it together, and prepared it. Then he said: “Go and bring me ten people, with you as the tenth.” So I brought them. He said: “Eat, and eat from its lower sides, and do not eat from its top, for blessing descends from its top.” They ate from it until they were full.","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (16006)."],[508,"Salmā narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that food be taken from its top.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (24/ح 754)."],[509,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A tailor invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a meal he had prepared. Anas said: I went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to that meal. The tailor brought him barley bread and a broth containing gourd. Anas said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ searching for pieces of gourd around the dish, and from that day onward I continued to love gourd.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (51)، والبخاري (2092)، ومسلم (2041، 144)، وزاد فيه: “دباء وقديد”."],[510,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: No lunch or dinner consisting of bread and meat was ever gathered for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except upon ḍafaf.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (13859)، والترمذي في الشمائل (138)، وأبو يعلى (3108)، وابن حبان في صحيحه (6359)."],[511,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food most beloved to Allah is that over which the greatest number of hands gather.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (2046)، والطبراني في الأوسط (7313)."],[512,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ sitting in the iqʿāʾ posture while eating dates.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2044، 148)."],[513,"Anas narrated: Dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ began distributing them while sitting in a raised, ready-to-move posture, eating them quickly. In another narration: “Eating them hurriedly.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2044، 149)."],[514,"Abū Juḥayfah narrated: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he said to a man who was with him: “I do not eat while reclining.” In another wording: “I do not eat reclining.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5399)، واللفظ الآخر bukhari(5398)."],[515,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen eating while reclining, nor would two men walk directly behind his heels.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3770)، وابن ماجه (244)، وأحمد (6549)."],[516,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr narrated: A sheep was presented to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knelt upon his knees and began eating. A Bedouin asked: “What kind of sitting posture is this?” He replied: “Allah has made me a noble servant and has not made me an arrogant, stubborn tyrant.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3263)، وأبو داود (3773)."],[517,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Satan attends one of you in every matter of his, even at his food. If a morsel falls from one of you, let him remove whatever dirt has gotten onto it, then eat it and not leave it for Satan. When he finishes, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2033، 135)."],[518,"Anas narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate food, he would lick his three fingers. He also said: “If a morsel belonging to one of you falls, let him remove the dirt from it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan.” He also commanded us to wipe the dish clean, saying: “For you do not know in which part of your food the blessing lies.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2034)."],[519,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you eats food, he should not wipe his hand until he has licked it himself or had someone else lick it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5456)، ومسلم (2031، 129)."],[520,"Jābir narrated: The Prophet ﷺ commanded that the fingers and the dish be licked clean and said: “You do not know in which part of it the blessing lies.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2033، 133)."],[521,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2035)."],[522,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ licking his three fingers after eating.” In another narration: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat with three fingers and would lick his hand before wiping it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2032، 131)."],[523,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you eats food, he should not wipe his hand until he has licked it himself or had someone else lick it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5456)، ومسلم (2031، 129)."],[524,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh was asked about performing wuḍūʾ after eating food touched by fire. He replied: “No. During the time of the Prophet ﷺ, we rarely found such food. When we did find it, we had no napkins except our palms, forearms, and feet. Then we would pray without performing wuḍūʾ.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5457)."],[525,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a morsel belonging to one of you falls, let him pick it up, remove whatever dirt is upon it, and eat it. He should not leave it for Satan. And he should not wipe his hand with a napkin until he has licked his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2033، 134)."],[526,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came out after relieving himself and food was brought to him. Wuḍūʾ was mentioned to him, so he said: “Am I intending to pray so that I should perform wuḍūʾ?”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (374)."],[527,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever goes to sleep while food grease or residue remains on his hand and he does not wash it, then something happens to him, let him blame no one but himself.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3852)، وابن ماجه (3297)، وأحمد (7569)."],[528,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever goes to sleep with food residue on his hand before washing it, and then some harm befalls him, let him blame no one but himself.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (1219)، وعبد الرزاق (19840)."],[529,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ never criticized any food. If he desired it, he ate it, and if he disliked it, he left it.” In another narration: “If he desired it, he ate it, and if he did not desire it, he remained silent.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5409)، ومسلم (2064، 187)."],[530,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of two is sufficient for three, and the food of three is sufficient for four.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (20)، والبخاري (5392)، ومسلم (2058)."],[531,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The food of one is sufficient for two, the food of two is sufficient for four, and the food of four is sufficient for eight.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2059، 179)."],[532,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Muslim eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (9)، والبخاري (5396)، ومسلم (2060)."],[533,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man used to eat a great deal. Then he embraced Islam and began eating only a little. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5397)."],[534,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hosted a disbelieving guest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a sheep be milked for him, and the man drank all of its milk. Then another was milked and he drank its milk, then another, until he had drunk the milk of seven sheep. The next morning he embraced Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked for him, but he could not finish it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer drinks with one intestine, while the disbeliever drinks with seven intestines.”","صحيح: رواه مالك (10)، ومسلم (2063، 186)."],[535,"Nāfiʿ narrated: Ibn ʿUmar would not eat until a poor person was brought to eat with him. I once brought a man to eat with him, and the man ate a great deal. Ibn ʿUmar said: “O Nāfiʿ, do not bring this man to me again. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5393)، ومسلم (2060، 183)."],[536,"ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated: Abū Nuhayk was a man who ate a great deal. Ibn ʿUmar said to him: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The disbeliever eats with seven intestines.’” Abū Nuhayk replied: “But I believe in Allah and His Messenger.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5395)."],[537,"Jābir and Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2061، 184)."],[538,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The believer eats with one intestine, while the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2062، 185)."],[539,"A man from Juhaynah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The disbeliever drinks with seven intestines, while the believer drinks with one intestine.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23135)."],[540,"Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The disbeliever eats with seven intestines, while the believer eats with one intestine.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (26845)."],[541,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: Abū Ṭalḥah said to Umm Sulaym: “I have heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sounding weak, and I can recognize hunger in it. Do you have anything?” She replied: “Yes.” She brought out some barley loaves, then took a veil of hers, wrapped some of the bread in part of it, tucked it under my arm, wrapped the rest of the cloth around me, and sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I took it to him and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting in the mosque with some people. I stood before them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Did Abū Ṭalḥah send you?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “For food?” I replied: “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to those with him: “Get up.” So he set out, and I went ahead of them until I reached Abū Ṭalḥah and informed him. Abū Ṭalḥah said: “O Umm Sulaym, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come with the people, but we do not have enough food to feed them.” She replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” Abū Ṭalḥah went out to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with him until they entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring what you have, O Umm Sulaym.” She brought the bread. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that it be crumbled, and Umm Sulaym squeezed some fat from a leather container over it to season it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whatever Allah willed him to say, and then said: “Give permission to ten.” Ten were admitted and ate until they were full, then they left. He then said: “Give permission to ten.” Another ten entered and ate until they were full, then left. He continued doing this until all of the people had eaten and become full. There were seventy or eighty men.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (19)، والبخاري (5381)، ومسلم (2040، 142)."],[542,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr narrated: We were with the Prophet ﷺ, one hundred and thirty of us. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Does any one of you have food?” A man had approximately one ṣāʿ of food, so it was kneaded. Then a tall, disheveled polytheist came driving some sheep. The Prophet ﷺ asked him: “Are they for sale or a gift?” —or he said: “A donation?” The man replied: “No, they are for sale.” So the Prophet ﷺ purchased a sheep from him, and it was prepared. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ ordered that the dark meat from the abdomen be roasted. By Allah, not one of the one hundred and thirty people was left without receiving a piece of it. If a person was present, he gave him his share; if he was absent, he kept it for him. Then the food was placed into two large bowls. We all ate and became full, and some food still remained in the two bowls. I loaded what remained onto the camel—or words to that effect.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5382)، ومسلم (2056)."],[543,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ passed away at a time when we had begun to eat our fill of the two dark things: dates and water.” In another wording: “when the people had begun to eat their fill.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5383)، ومسلم (2875، 30)."],[544,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day—or one night—and came across Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. He asked them: “What brought the two of you out of your homes at this hour?” They replied: “Hunger, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “And by the One in whose hand is my soul, the same thing that brought you out brought me out as well. Get up.” So they went with him. He came to the house of a man from the Anṣār, but the man was not at home. When the man’s wife saw the Prophet ﷺ, she said: “Welcome and greetings.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: “Where is so-and-so?” She replied: “He has gone to bring us fresh, sweet water.” Then the Anṣārī man arrived. When he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his two companions, he said: “Praise be to Allah! No one today has more honored guests than I do.” He went and brought them a cluster containing unripe or partly ripe dates, dried ripe dates, and fresh ripe dates and said: “Eat from these.” Then he took a knife. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not slaughter a milk-producing sheep.” So he slaughtered a sheep for them. They ate from the sheep and from the date cluster and drank. When they had eaten their fill and quenched their thirst, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abū Bakr and ʿUmar: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will certainly be questioned about this blessing on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger brought you out of your homes, and you did not return until you had received this blessing.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2038)."],[545,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If dinner is placed before one of you and the prayer is commenced, begin with dinner, and do not hurry until you have finished eating.” Food would be placed before Ibn ʿUmar and the prayer would begin, yet he would not go to it until he had finished, even though he could hear the imam reciting.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (673)، ومسلم (559)."],[546,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When dinner is served, begin with it before praying Maghrib, and do not rush away from your dinner.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (672)، ومسلم (557)."],[547,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When dinner has been served and the prayer is commenced, begin with dinner.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (671)، ومسلم (558)."],[548,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from a mountain pass after relieving himself. We had dates in front of us placed upon a shield or similar object. We invited him to eat, so he ate with us without touching water.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3762)، وأحمد (15272)، وصححه ابن حبان (1160)."],[550,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: Two roasted lizards were brought to the Prophet ﷺ while we were in the house of Maymūnah.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5400)، ومسلم (1945)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[551,"Abū Qatādah al-Sulamī narrated: One day I was sitting with some men from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ at a stopping place on the road to Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had camped ahead of us. The people were in iḥrām, while I was not. They saw a wild donkey while I was busy repairing my sandal. They did not alert me to it, although they wished that I would notice it myself. I turned and saw it, so I went to my horse, saddled it, and mounted. I had forgotten my whip and spear. I said to them: “Hand me the whip and spear.” They replied: “No, by Allah, we will not assist you in any way with it.” I became angry, dismounted, took them myself, then mounted again. I pursued the wild donkey and struck it down. I brought it back after it had died, and they began eating from it. Then they became uncertain about whether they were permitted to eat it while they were in iḥrām. We continued traveling, and I kept the foreleg with me. When we reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we asked him about it. He said: “Do you have any of it with you?” I handed him the foreleg, and he ate from it, gnawing the meat from the bone while he was in iḥrām.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5407)، ومسلم (1194، 63)."],[552,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ took a meat-covered bone out of a cooking pot, ate from it, then prayed without performing wuḍūʾ.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5404-5405)، ومسلم (354)."],[553,"ʿAmr ibn Umayyah narrated: He saw the Prophet ﷺ cutting meat from a sheep’s shoulder that he was holding in his hand. Then he was called to prayer. He put down the shoulder and the knife with which he had been cutting it, stood up, and prayed without performing wuḍūʾ.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5408)، ومسلم (355، 92)."],[554,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated: I was the guest of the Prophet ﷺ one night. He ordered that a side of meat be roasted, then took a knife and began cutting pieces from it for me.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (188)، والترمذي في الشمائل (168)، وأحمد (18212)."],[555,"ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated: “We ate roasted meat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي في الشمائل (167)."],[556,"Abū Dharr narrated: The Prophet ﷺ, my beloved, advised me: “When you cook broth, increase its water, then look to a household among your neighbors and give them some of it in a good manner.” In another wording: “O Abū Dharr, when you cook broth, increase its water and remember your neighbors.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2625، 143)، ورواه مسلم أيضا (2625، 142) باللفظ الثاني."],[557,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should belittle any good deed. If he finds nothing to give, then let him meet his brother with a cheerful face. And if you buy meat or prepare a pot of food, increase its broth and give some of it to your neighbor.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3362)، وابن حبان (523)."],[558,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you cook meat, increase the broth or water, for that makes it more plentiful—or more sufficient—for the neighbors.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (15030)."],[559,"Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr used to cover tharīd for a short time after preparing it until its intense heat subsided. Then she would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “That is greater in blessing.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (26958، 26959)."],[560,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: We were with the Prophet ﷺ at a meal to which he had been invited. A foreleg was presented to him, and he liked that part of the meat. He bit a piece of meat from it.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3340)، ومسلم (194)."],[561,"Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Bite the meat directly from the bone, for that is more wholesome and more pleasant.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (1835)، وأحمد (15300)."],[562,"ʿAmr ibn Umayyah narrated: He saw the Prophet ﷺ cutting meat from a sheep’s shoulder that he was holding in his hand. Then he was called to prayer. He put down the shoulder and the knife with which he had been cutting it, stood up, and prayed without performing wuḍūʾ.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5408)، ومسلم (355)."],[563,"Jabalah ibn Suḥaym narrated: Ibn al-Zubayr used to provide us with dates. The people were suffering hardship at that time, and while we were eating, Ibn ʿUmar would pass by us and say: “Do not take two dates together at once, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited taking dates in pairs, unless a man seeks the permission of his companion.” Shuʿbah said: “I think the words concerning seeking permission are from Ibn ʿUmar himself.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5446)، ومسلم (2045، 150)."],[564,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Busr narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with my father. We brought him food and waṭbah, and he ate from it. Then dates were brought to him. He would eat them and place the pits between his fingers, joining his index and middle fingers together. Shuʿbah said: “I think that is how it was narrated—and Allah willing, it is indeed in the hadith—that he placed the pits between the two fingers.” Then a drink was brought to him. He drank from it and then handed it to the person on his right. My father took hold of the bridle of his riding animal and said: “Supplicate to Allah for us.” He said: “O Allah, bless them in what You have provided for them, forgive them, and have mercy on them.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2042)."],[565,"Anas narrated: “As far as I know, the Prophet ﷺ never ate from a sukkurrajah, never had thin refined bread prepared for him, and never ate upon a khuwān.” Qatādah was asked: “Then what did they eat upon?” He replied: “Upon dining cloths.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5386)."],[566,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ stayed in order to consummate his marriage with Ṣafiyyah. I invited the Muslims to his wedding feast. He ordered that leather mats be spread out, and dates, dried curd, and clarified butter were placed upon them.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5387، 371)، ومسلم (1365، 84)."],[567,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: Umm Ḥufayd bint al-Ḥārith ibn Ḥazn, the maternal aunt of Ibn ʿAbbās, presented the Prophet ﷺ with clarified butter, dried curd, and desert lizards. They were brought forward and eaten upon his table, while the Prophet ﷺ refrained from eating the lizards because he found them distasteful. Had they been forbidden, they would not have been eaten upon the table of the Prophet ﷺ, nor would he have instructed that they be eaten.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5389)، ومسلم (1947)."],[568,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited a man from drinking while standing. Qatādah said: “We asked: What about eating?” He replied: “That is worse—or more objectionable.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2024، 113)."],[569,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited drinking while standing.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2025، 115)."],[570,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should drink while standing. Whoever forgets and does so should make himself vomit.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2026)."],[571,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If the one who drinks while standing knew what was in his stomach, he would make himself vomit.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (7808، 7809)."],[572,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ saw a man drinking while standing and said to him: “Vomit it.” The man asked: “Why?” He said: “Would you be pleased if a cat drank together with you?” The man replied: “No.” He said: “Then one worse than a cat has drunk with you: Satan.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (8003)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (2896)."],[573,"Al-Jārūd ibn al-Muʿallā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited drinking while standing.","حسن: رواه الترمذي (1881)."],[574,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: “I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ water from Zamzam, and he drank it while standing.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5617)، ومسلم (2027، 117)."],[575,"ʿAlī prayed Ẓuhr, then remained attending to the people’s needs in the courtyard of Kūfah until the time for ʿAṣr arrived. Water was brought to him. He drank from it and washed his face and hands, and the narration also mentions his head and feet. Then he stood and drank the remaining water while standing. He said: “Some people dislike drinking while standing, but the Prophet ﷺ did exactly what you have seen me do.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5616)."],[576,"Al-Nazzāl narrated: ʿAlī came to the gate of the courtyard and drank while standing. He said: “Some people dislike drinking while standing, but I saw the Prophet ﷺ do just as you have seen me do.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5615)."],[577,"Zādhān narrated: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib drank while standing. The people looked at him as though they disapproved. He said: “Why are you looking at me? If I drink while standing, I have seen the Prophet ﷺ drink while standing; and if I drink while sitting, I have seen the Prophet ﷺ drink while sitting.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (795)."],[578,"Umm al-Faḍl bint al-Ḥārith sent a cup of milk to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing on the evening of ʿArafah. He took it in his hand and drank it.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5618)، ومسلم (1123)."],[579,"Kabshah al-Anṣāriyyah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and drank while standing directly from the mouth of a hanging waterskin. I then went to the mouth of the waterskin and cut it off.","صحيح: رواه الترمذي في الجامع (1892)، وفي الشمائل (214)، وأحمد (27448)، وصححه ابن حبان (5318)."],[580,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: “During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to eat while walking and drink while standing.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1880)، وابن ماجه (3301)، وأحمد (5874)، وصححه ابن حبان (5322)."],[581,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink both while standing and while sitting.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي في الجامع (1883)، وفي الشمائل (209)، وأبو داود (653)، وابن ماجه (931)، وأحمد (6660)."],[582,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drink while standing and while sitting, pray while wearing sandals and while barefoot, and turn away after prayer both to his right and to his left.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (1235)."],[583,"Anas narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take three breaths while drinking and would say: “It is more thirst-quenching, healthier, and more pleasant.” Anas said: “So I also take three breaths when drinking.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2028، 123)."],[584,"Anas narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to breathe three times while drinking.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5631)، ومسلم (2028، 122)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[585,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to drink in three breaths. Whenever he brought the vessel to his mouth, he would mention the Name of Allah, and whenever he moved it away, he would praise Allah. He would do this three times.","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (4141)، والخرائطي في فضيلة الشكر (24)."],[586,"Abū al-Muthannā al-Juhanī narrated: I was with Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam when Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī entered upon him. Marwān asked him: “Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he prohibited blowing into a drink?” Abū Saʿīd replied: “Yes.” A man had said: “O Messenger of Allah, I do not become fully quenched from a single breath.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then remove the cup from your mouth and breathe.” The man said: “I see a speck of dirt in it.” He replied: “Then pour it out.”","حسن: رواه مالك (12)، والترمذي (1887)، وابن حبان (5327)، والحاكم (7208)."],[587,"Abū Qatādah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you drinks, he should not breathe into the vessel. When one of you urinates, he should not wipe his private part with his right hand. And when one of you cleans himself after relieving himself, he should not do so with his right hand.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5630)، ومسلم (267، 63)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[588,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you drinks, he should not breathe into the vessel. If he wishes to drink again, let him move the vessel away, then return to it if he wishes.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3427)، وابن أبي شيبة (24169)، وأبو يعلى (6677)، والحاكم (4/139)."],[589,"Abū al-Muthannā al-Juhanī narrated: I was with Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam when Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī entered upon him. Marwān asked: “Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he prohibited blowing into a drink?” Abū Saʿīd replied: “Yes.” A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I do not become fully quenched from one breath.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then remove the cup from your mouth and breathe.” The man said: “I see a speck of dirt in it.” He said: “Then pour it out.”","حسن: رواه مالك (12)، والترمذي (1887)، وابن حبان (5327)، والحاكم (7208)."],[590,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited breathing into a vessel or blowing into it.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3728)، والترمذي (1888)، وابن ماجه (3429)، وأحمد (1907)."],[591,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: “It was prohibited to drink from the broken or chipped edge of a cup.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (4131)، وأبو نعيم في حلية الأولياء (9/38)."],[592,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon a man from the Anṣār together with one of his companions. The Prophet ﷺ and his companion gave salām, and the man returned the greeting. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. It is a very hot time of day.” The man was directing water through his garden. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If you have water that has remained overnight in a waterskin, then give us some. Otherwise, we will drink directly.” The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have water that has remained overnight in a waterskin.” He went to the shelter, poured water into a cup, then milked some milk from a domestic animal into it. The Prophet ﷺ drank. The man then prepared another serving, and the companion who had come with the Prophet ﷺ drank.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5621)."],[593,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited ikhtināth of waterskins, meaning bending or turning their mouths so as to drink directly from them. In another narration: “He prohibited drinking from their mouths.” And in another: “Ikhtināth means turning the mouth of the waterskin over and then drinking from it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5625). والرواية الثانية: البخاري (5626)، ومسلم (2023، 111). والرواية الثالثة لمسلم."],[594,"ʿIkrimah said: “Shall I tell you some short reports that Abū Hurayrah narrated to us?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin or water container, and prohibited a person from preventing his neighbor from inserting his timber into his wall.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5627)."],[595,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ prohibited drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5629)."],[596,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited animals killed by being used as targets, the milk of animals that habitually feed on filth, and drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3786)، والترمذي (1827)، والنسائي (4448)، وأحمد (1989، 2161)."],[597,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin. The report adds: “because that causes it to become foul-smelling.”","صحيح: رواه الحاكم (7211)، إلا قوله: ((لأن ذلك ينتنه)) فهو شاذ."],[598,"Kabshah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and drank while standing from the mouth of a hanging waterskin. I then went to its mouth and cut it off.","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1892)، وابن ماجه (3423)، وصححه ابن حبان (5318)."],[599,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon a woman from the Anṣār. There was a hanging waterskin in the house, so he bent its mouth and drank from it while standing.","حسن: رواه أحمد (25279)."],[600,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ served drink, he would say: “Begin with the elder.” Or he said: “Begin with the elders.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (2425)، والطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (4137)."],[601,"Anas narrated: A domestic sheep was milked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of Anas ibn Mālik. Its milk was mixed with water from the well in Anas’s house. The cup was given to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he drank from it. When he removed the cup from his mouth, Abū Bakr was on his left and a Bedouin was on his right. ʿUmar, fearing that the Prophet ﷺ would give it to the Bedouin first, said: “Give it to Abū Bakr, O Messenger of Allah, who is beside you.” But the Prophet ﷺ gave it to the Bedouin on his right and said: “The one on the right, then the one on the right.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2352)، ومسلم (2029)."],[602,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty. My mothers used to encourage me to serve him. He entered our home, so we milked a domestic sheep for him and mixed the milk with water from a well in the house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank. ʿUmar said to him, while Abū Bakr was on his left: “O Messenger of Allah, give it to Abū Bakr.” But he gave it to a Bedouin who was on his right and said: “The one on the right, then the one on the right.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5612)، ومسلم (2029، 125)."],[603,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in our home and asked for something to drink. We milked a sheep for him and mixed its milk with water from this well of mine. I handed it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he drank. Abū Bakr was on his left, ʿUmar was facing him, and a Bedouin was on his right. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished drinking, ʿUmar said: “Here is Abū Bakr, O Messenger of Allah,” pointing him out. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the vessel to the Bedouin and passed over Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Those on the right, those on the right, those on the right.” Anas said: “This is the Sunnah. This is the Sunnah. This is the Sunnah.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2029، 126)."],[604,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Anṣārī narrated: A drink was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he drank from it. A young boy was on his right, while some elderly men were on his left. He said to the boy: “Will you give me permission to give it to these men first?” The boy replied: “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. I will not give preference to anyone over myself regarding my share from you.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed the vessel in his hand.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (18)، والبخاري (5620)، ومسلم (2030، 127)."],[605,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought milk mixed with water from a well. A Bedouin was on his right and Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq was on his left. He drank and then gave the vessel to the Bedouin, saying: “The one on the right, then the one on the right.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (17)، والبخاري (5619)، ومسلم (2029، 124)."],[606,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon a man from the Anṣār together with one of his companions. The Prophet ﷺ and his companion gave salām, and the man returned it. The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. It is a very hot hour.” He was directing water through his garden. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If you have water that has remained overnight in a waterskin, give us some; otherwise, we will drink directly.” The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have water that has remained overnight in a waterskin.” He went to the shelter, poured water into a cup, and milked some milk from one of his domestic animals into it. The Prophet ﷺ drank. He then prepared another serving, and the man who had come with the Prophet ﷺ drank.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5621)."],[608,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: On the night the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, while at Īliyāʾ, he was brought two vessels: one containing wine and the other milk. He looked at them and chose the milk. Jibrīl, peace be upon him, said: “Praise be to Allah who guided you to the natural disposition. Had you chosen the wine, your nation would have gone astray.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5603)، ومسلم (168، 92)."],[609,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Burāq was brought to me. It was a tall white riding animal, larger than a donkey but smaller than a mule, and it placed its hoof at the furthest point its sight could reach. I rode it until I reached Bayt al-Maqdis. I tied it to the ring to which the Prophets used to tie their mounts. Then I entered the mosque and prayed two rakʿahs there. Afterward I came out, and Jibrīl, peace be upon him, brought me a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk. I chose the milk. Jibrīl said: ‘You have chosen the natural disposition.’ Then we were taken up into the heaven…” to the end of the hadith.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (162، 259)."],[610,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ drank milk, then called for water and rinsed his mouth. He said: “It contains fat.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5609)، ومسلم (358)."],[611,"Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī narrated: I brought the Prophet ﷺ a cup of milk from al-Naqīʿ that was uncovered. He said: “Why did you not cover it, even if only by placing a stick across it?” Abū Ḥumayd said: “The command concerning waterskins being tied and doors being closed applies at night.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2010)."],[612,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: Abū Ḥumayd brought a cup of milk from al-Naqīʿ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Why did you not cover it, even if only by placing a stick across it?”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5605)، ومسلم (2011، 95)."],[613,"ʿAlqamah narrated: I asked Ibn Masʿūd: “Did any of you accompany the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn?” He replied: “No. But one night we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and suddenly lost sight of him. We searched for him in the valleys and mountain paths and said: ‘Perhaps he has been carried away, or perhaps he has been assassinated!’ We spent the worst night that any people could spend.” When morning came, he approached us from the direction of Ḥirāʾ. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, we lost you and searched for you but could not find you. We spent the worst night that any people could spend.” He said: “A caller from among the jinn came to me, so I went with him and recited the Qur’an to them.” Then he took us and showed us their footprints and the traces of their fires. They had asked him for provisions, so he said: “Every bone over which the Name of Allah has been mentioned that falls into your hands will be restored with as much meat upon it as possible, and every piece of dung is fodder for your animals.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Therefore, do not use either of them for cleaning yourselves after relieving yourselves, for they are the food of your brothers.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (450)."],[614,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that he used to carry a small water vessel for the Prophet ﷺ for his wuḍūʾ and personal needs. While Abū Hurayrah was following him carrying it, the Prophet ﷺ asked: “Who is this?” He replied: “It is Abū Hurayrah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bring me some stones with which I may clean myself, and do not bring me a bone or dung.” So I brought him stones carried in the edge of my garment and placed them beside him, then went away. When he had finished, I walked with him and asked: “What is the matter with bones and dung?” He replied: “They are among the food of the jinn. A delegation of the jinn of Naṣībīn came to me—and what excellent jinn they were—and they asked me for provisions. So I supplicated to Allah for them that whenever they pass by a bone or a piece of dung, they will find food upon it.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (3860)."],[615,"Abū Qatādah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us in a lengthy sermon. At its conclusion, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who serves drink to the people should be the last of them to drink.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (681، 311)."],[616,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The one serving drink to the people should be the last of them to drink.” In another wording, he said: We were on a journey and could not find water. Later we came upon water, and they began serving the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Each time they brought him a drink, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one serving the people is the last of them.” He said this three times, until all of them had drunk.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3725)، وأحمد (19121). واللفظ الأول لأبي داود، واللفظ الثاني لأحمد."],[617,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “Pleasant, fresh water used to be brought for the Prophet ﷺ from al-Suqyā.” Qutaybah said: “It was a spring two days’ journey from Madinah.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3735)، وأحمد (24693، 24770)، وصححه ابن حبان (5332)، والحاكم (4/138)."],[618,"Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who drinks from a silver vessel is only gurgling the Fire of Hell into his stomach.” In another wording: “Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or silver is only gurgling fire from Hell into his stomach.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (11)، والبخاري (5634)، ومسلم (2065). واللفظ الثاني رواه مسلم."],[619,"Anas narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited eating and drinking from vessels of gold and silver.”","حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (6598)."],[620,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Take a midday nap, for Satan does not take a midday nap.”","حسن: رواه أبو نعيم في أخبار أصبهان (371)."],[621,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day must not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6136)، ومسلم (47، 75)."],[622,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should maintain his ties of kinship. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.” In another wording: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6138)، ومسلم (47، 74)."],[624,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I am suffering from severe hunger.” The Prophet ﷺ sent to one of his wives, but she replied: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing except water.” He sent to another, and she gave the same reply, until all of them said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I have nothing except water.” The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Who will host this man tonight? May Allah have mercy on him.” A man from the Anṣār stood and said: “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” He took the guest home and asked his wife: “Do you have anything?” She replied: “Nothing except the food of my children.” He said: “Distract them with something. When our guest comes in, extinguish the lamp and make him think that we are eating. When he reaches for the food, go to the lamp and extinguish it.” So they sat down, and the guest ate. The next morning, the man went to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Allah was amazed at what the two of you did for your guest last night.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3798)، ومسلم (2054، 172)، واللفظ له. والرجل هو أبو طلحة."],[625,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no good in one who does not offer hospitality.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (17419)، والروياني في مسنده (176)."],[626,"Abū Shurayḥ al-Kaʿbī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. His special hospitality is for one day and one night, while general hospitality is for three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity. And it is not lawful for the guest to remain with him until he causes him hardship.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (22)، والبخاري (6019، 6135)، ومسلم (48، 14)."],[627,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days. Whatever comes after that is charity.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (11615)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (1931-1932)."],[628,"Zayd ibn Khālid narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Hospitality is for three days, and whatever exceeds that is charity.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1925)."],[629,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days, and anything beyond that is charity.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3749)، وأحمد (8645)."],[630,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days, and whatever exceeds that is charity.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (11325) عن عبد الرزاق، وهو في مصنفه (20528)."],[631,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days. Whatever exceeds that is charity, and every good deed is charity.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1928)."],[632,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Hospitality is for three days, and whatever exceeds that is charity.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1929)."],[633,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated: We said: “O Messenger of Allah, you send us out and we stay with people who do not offer us hospitality. What do you say about that?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “If you stay with people and they provide you with what is appropriate for a guest, then accept it. If they do not, then take from them the guest’s due right that they ought to provide.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6137)، ومسلم (1727)."],[634,"Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdī Karib, Abū Karīmah, narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “One night of hospitality is a duty upon every Muslim. If a guest spends the morning at his courtyard having been deprived of hospitality, it becomes a debt owed to him. If he wishes, he may claim it, and if he wishes, he may leave it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3750)، وابن ماجه (3677)، وأحمد (17172) - واللفظ له."],[635,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Any guest who stays with a people and reaches the morning having been deprived may take an amount equal to the hospitality due to him, and there is no blame upon him.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (8948)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (2816، 2817)."],[636,"Mālik ibn Naḍlah al-Jushamī narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, suppose I pass by a man and he neither offers me hospitality nor hosts me, then later he passes by me. Should I repay him in the same way?” He replied: “No. Offer him hospitality.” He then saw that my clothes were worn and asked: “Do you possess wealth?” I replied: “I possess all kinds of wealth. Allah has given me camels and sheep.” He said: “Then let its effects be seen upon you.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (2006)، وأبو داود (4063)، والنسائي (5223)، وأحمد (15888)."],[637,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said: “Have I not been informed that you stand in prayer throughout the night and fast during the day?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “Do not do that. Stand in prayer and sleep; fast and break your fast. Your body has a right over you, your eyes have a right over you, your guest has a right over you, and your wife has a right over you. Perhaps you will live a long life. It is sufficient for you to fast three days of every month, for every good deed is rewarded tenfold, and that is equivalent to fasting the entire year.” I insisted upon more, so he made the ruling stricter for me. I said: “I am capable of more than that.” He said: “Then fast three days each week.” I continued to insist, so he made it stricter for me. I said: “I am capable of more.” He said: “Then observe the fast of the Prophet of Allah Dāwūd.” I asked: “What was the fast of the Prophet of Allah Dāwūd?” He replied: “Half of all time.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6134)، ومسلم (1159، 183)."],[638,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you is invited to a meal, let him accept the invitation. If he wishes, he may eat, and if he wishes, he may refrain.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1430، 105)."],[639,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you is invited, let him accept. If he is fasting, let him supplicate, and if he is not fasting, let him eat.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1431)."],[640,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Free the captive, respond to the invitation, and visit the sick.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5174)."],[641,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If I were invited to a meal consisting only of a sheep’s lower leg, I would accept the invitation; and if a sheep’s lower leg were given to me as a gift, I would accept it.”","صحيح: أخرجه البخاري (5178)."],[642,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you are invited even to a meal of a sheep’s lower leg, then accept the invitation.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1429، 104)."],[643,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A tailor invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a meal he had prepared. Anas said: I went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to that meal. The tailor served him barley bread and broth containing gourd. Anas said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ searching for pieces of gourd around the dish, and from that day onward I continued to love gourd.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (51)، والبخاري (2092)، ومسلم (2041، 144)."],[644,"A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If two people invite you at the same time, accept the invitation of the one whose door is closer, for the one whose door is closer is the nearer neighbor. If one of them invited you first, then accept the invitation of the one who invited you first.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3756)، وأحمد (23466)."],[645,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited eating the food of two people who compete with one another in lavish hospitality.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3754)، وصححه الحاكم (7170)."],[646,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The invitations of two people competing with each other in ostentation are not to be accepted, nor is their food to be eaten.”","حسن: رواه ابن السماك في جزئه كما في الصحيحة (626)، والبيهقي في الشعب (5667)."],[647,"Anas narrated: We were with ʿUmar when he said: “We were prohibited from unnecessary affectation and burdening ourselves.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (7293)."],[648,"Shaqīq ibn Salamah narrated: A companion and I went to Salmān al-Fārisī. Salmān said: “Were it not that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us from burdening ourselves unnecessarily, I would have gone to extra effort for you.” Then he brought bread and meat. My companion said: “If only we had some thyme with our salt.” Salmān sent his water vessel to be pawned and obtained thyme. After we had eaten, my companion said: “Praise be to Allah who has made us content with what He has provided us.” Salmān replied: “Had you truly been content with what Allah provided you, my water vessel would not now be pawned.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (6085)."],[649,"Laqīṭ ibn Ṣabirah narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he slaughtered a sheep for us. He said: “Do not think that we slaughtered it specifically because of you. Rather, we own sheep, and whenever their number reaches one hundred, we slaughter one.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (16382)."],[651,"Abū Juḥayfah Wahb al-Suwāʾī narrated: The Prophet ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between Salmān and Abū al-Dardāʾ. Salmān visited Abū al-Dardāʾ and saw Umm al-Dardāʾ dressed in a neglected manner. He asked her: “What is the matter with you?” She replied: “Your brother Abū al-Dardāʾ has no interest in worldly life.” Then Abū al-Dardāʾ arrived and prepared food for Salmān. He said: “Eat, for I am fasting.” Salmān replied: “I will not eat until you eat.” So Abū al-Dardāʾ ate. When night came, Abū al-Dardāʾ got up to pray. Salmān told him: “Sleep.” So he slept. Later he tried to get up again, and Salmān said: “Sleep.” When the final part of the night came, Salmān said: “Get up now.” So the two of them prayed. Then Salmān said to him: “Your Lord has a right over you, your own self has a right over you, and your family has a right over you. So give everyone who has a right his due.” Abū al-Dardāʾ went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what had happened. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Salmān has spoken the truth.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6139)."],[652,"Abū Mūsā narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ride a donkey, wear wool, personally restrain a sheep, and attend to the needs of his guest.","صحيح: رواه أبو الشيخ في أخلاق النبي ﷺ (315)، والحاكم (205)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (4188)."],[653,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The first person to offer hospitality to a guest was Ibrāhīm, peace be upon him.”","حسن: رواه ابن أبي الدنيا في قرى الضيف، ومن طريقه البيهقي في الشعب (917)."],[654,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: There were three legal rulings connected to Barīrah. She was given the choice regarding her husband when she was emancipated. Some meat was given to her in charity. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while a cooking pot was over the fire. He asked for food, and bread with a household condiment was brought to him. He said: “Did I not see a pot over the fire containing meat?” They replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but that is meat which was given in charity to Barīrah, and we disliked giving you some of it.” He said: “It was charity for her, but from her it is a gift to us.” The Prophet ﷺ also said concerning her: “The right of walāʾ belongs only to the one who emancipates the slave.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5430)، ومسلم (1504، 14)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[655,"Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī narrated: There was a man from the Anṣār known as Abū Shuʿayb who had a servant who worked as a butcher. He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and recognized signs of hunger on his face. He said to his servant: “Prepare food for five people, for I want to invite the Prophet ﷺ as one of five.” The servant prepared the food. Abū Shuʿayb then went to the Prophet ﷺ and invited him as one of five people. Another man followed them without having been invited. When they reached the door, the Prophet ﷺ said: “This man followed us. If you wish, you may give him permission, and if you wish, he may return.” The host replied: “No, rather I give him permission, O Messenger of Allah.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5434)، ومسلم (2036، 138)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[656,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A Persian neighbor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was skilled at preparing broth. He prepared some food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and came to invite him. The Prophet ﷺ asked, referring to ʿĀ’ishah: “And her?” The man replied: “No.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then no.” The man returned and invited him again. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “And her?” He replied: “No.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ again said: “Then no.” The man returned a third time and invited him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “And her?” This time the man replied: “Yes.” So the Prophet ﷺ and ʿĀ’ishah got up and hurried together until they reached his house.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2037)."],[657,"Anas narrated: I was a young boy walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a servant of his who was a tailor. The tailor brought him a bowl containing food with gourd in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began seeking out the pieces of gourd. When I saw that, I began gathering the pieces of gourd and placing them in front of him. Meanwhile, the tailor returned to his work. Anas said: “I have continued to love gourd ever since I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do what he did.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5435)، ومسلم (2041)."],[658,"Anas narrated: My mother, Umm Sulaym, took a mudd of barley, ground it, and prepared a thick dish from it. She also squeezed some fat from a leather container she had. Then she sent me to the Prophet ﷺ. I found him among his Companions and invited him. He asked: “And those who are with me?” I returned and said: “He is asking, ‘And those who are with me?’” Abū Ṭalḥah went out to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is only a little food prepared by Umm Sulaym.” The Prophet ﷺ entered, and the food was brought. He said: “Admit ten people to me.” Ten entered and ate until they were full. Then he said: “Admit ten more.” Another ten entered and ate until they were full. Then he again said: “Admit ten.” This continued until forty had been counted. Then the Prophet ﷺ ate and stood up. Anas said: “I kept looking at the food to see whether any of it had diminished.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5450)، ومسلم (2040)."],[659,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr narrated: Abū Bakr hosted a group of guests and said to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: “Take care of your guests, for I am going to the Prophet ﷺ. Finish serving them before I return.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān brought them whatever food was available and said: “Eat.” They asked: “Where is the master of the house?” He replied: “Eat.” They said: “We will not eat until the master of the house comes.” He said: “Please accept your hospitality from us. If he returns and you have not eaten, I will surely face trouble from him.” But they refused. I realized that Abū Bakr would be angry with me. When he returned, I moved away from him. He asked: “What did you do?” The guests told him what had happened. He called: “O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān!” I remained silent. He called again: “O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān!” I remained silent. Then he said: “O foolish fellow! I adjure you, if you can hear my voice, come here!” So I came out and said: “Ask your guests.” They said: “He is telling the truth. He brought us the food.” Abū Bakr said: “So you were only waiting for me? By Allah, I will not eat it tonight.” The guests replied: “By Allah, we will not eat until you eat.” Abū Bakr said: “I have never seen a night as troublesome as this! Woe to you, what is wrong with you? Why will you not accept our hospitality? Bring the food.” The food was brought. He placed his hand into it and said: “In the Name of Allah. My first oath was from Satan.” Then he ate, and they ate with him. Muslim adds: The next morning Abū Bakr went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, they fulfilled their oath while I broke mine.” He told him what had happened. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Rather, you were the most righteous and the best of them.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: “No expiation for an oath reached me in connection with this incident.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6140)، ومسلم (2057، 177)."],[660,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr narrated: Abū Bakr brought home a guest—or some guests—then remained with the Prophet ﷺ until evening. When he returned, my mother said to him: “You remained away from your guest—or your guests—tonight.” He asked: “Did you not give them dinner?” She replied: “We offered it to him—or to them—but he refused—or they refused.” Abū Bakr became angry, rebuked and scolded, and swore that he would not eat the food. I hid myself. He called out: “O foolish fellow!” His wife then swore that she would not eat until he ate, and the guest—or guests—swore that he would not eat—or they would not eat—until Abū Bakr ate. Abū Bakr said: “This seems to be from Satan.” He called for the food, then ate, and they ate with him. Whenever they lifted a morsel, more food than it had been would grow underneath it. Abū Bakr said: “O sister of Banū Firās, what is this?” She replied: “By the delight of my eye, it is now more than it was before we began eating.” They ate from it, and some of it was sent to the Prophet ﷺ. It was mentioned that he also ate from it.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6141، 602)، ومسلم (2057، 176)."],[661,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: “If you enter upon your Muslim brother and he gives you food, then eat and do not question him about it. And if he gives you something to drink, then drink and do not question him about it.”","حسن: رواه الحاكم (7161)."],[662,"Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not keep close companionship except with a believer, and let none but a God-fearing person eat your food.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4832)، والترمذي (2395)، وأحمد (11337)، والدارمي (554)، والحاكم (7169)."],[663,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hosted a disbelieving guest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a sheep be milked for him, and he drank all of its milk. Then another was milked and he drank its milk, then another, until he had drunk the milk of seven sheep. The next morning he embraced Islam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a sheep be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked for him, but he could not finish it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer drinks with one intestine, while the disbeliever drinks with seven intestines.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (10)، ومسلم (2063، 186)، والبخاري (5396)."],[664,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr narrated: The people of al-Ṣuffah were poor people. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever has food sufficient for two should take a third person with him, and whoever has food for four should take a fifth or a sixth.” Abū Bakr brought three people home, while the Prophet ﷺ took ten. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: The household consisted of me, my father, and my mother—and I do not know whether he also mentioned my wife and a servant shared between our household and the household of Abū Bakr. Abū Bakr ate dinner with the Prophet ﷺ, then remained until after the ʿIshāʾ prayer. He stayed until the Prophet ﷺ became drowsy, then returned after as much of the night had passed as Allah willed. His wife asked him: “What kept you from your guests—or your guest?” He replied: “Did you not serve them dinner?” She said: “They refused to eat until you came. Food was offered to them, but they refused.” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I went and hid myself. Abū Bakr called: “O foolish fellow!” He rebuked and insulted me, then said to the guests: “Eat, though may it bring you no enjoyment!” Then he said: “By Allah, I will never eat it.” By Allah, whenever we took a morsel from the food, more than that amount grew beneath it, until everyone became full. The food became greater in quantity than it had been before. Abū Bakr looked at it and saw that it was still as much as before, or even more. He said to his wife: “O sister of Banū Firās, what is this?” She replied: “By the delight of my eye, it is now three times as much as it was before.” Abū Bakr then ate from it and said: “That oath of mine was only from Satan.” Then he ate a morsel and carried the food to the Prophet ﷺ, where it remained until morning. There was a treaty between us and another people, and when its term expired, we divided ourselves into twelve groups, each man accompanied by a number of people—Allah knows how many were with each one—and they all ate from that food. Or words to that effect.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (602)، ومسلم (2057، 176)."],[665,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: I never knew my parents except that they both followed the religion of Islam. Not a day passed without the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming to us at both ends of the day, morning and evening. One day, while we were sitting in the house of Abū Bakr at the height of midday, someone said: “Here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming at an hour when he does not normally come.” Abū Bakr said: “Nothing but an important matter could have brought him at this hour.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I have been given permission to depart.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6079)."],[666,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a household from the Anṣār and ate food with them. When he intended to leave, he instructed that an area of the house be prepared. Water was sprinkled upon a mat for him, and he prayed upon it and supplicated for them.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6080)."],[667,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: Umm Sulaym used to spread a leather mat for the Prophet ﷺ, and he would take his midday nap upon it in her home. When the Prophet ﷺ slept, she would collect some of his perspiration and hair and place them in a bottle, then mix them into perfume. When the time of Anas ibn Mālik’s death approached, he instructed that some of that perfume be placed in the aromatic mixture used for his burial. So it was placed in his burial perfume.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6281)، ومسلم (2331)."],[668,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you dress and when you perform wuḍūʾ, begin with your right sides.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4141)، والترمذي (1766)، وابن ماجه (402)، وأحمد (8652)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (178)، وابن حبان (1090)."],[669,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you puts on his footwear, let him begin with the right foot. When he removes it, let him begin with the left. Let the right foot be the first to be shod and the last to be uncovered.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (15)، والبخاري (5855)، ومسلم (2097)."],[670,"The Mother of the Believers ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ liked to begin with the right side when putting on his footwear, combing his hair, purifying himself, and in all his affairs.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (168)، ومسلم (268)."],[671,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from putting on his footwear while standing.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3618)."],[672,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ prohibited a man from putting on his footwear while standing.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3619)."],[673,"Jābir narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from putting on his footwear while standing.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4135)."],[674,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should walk wearing only one sandal. Either wear both of them or leave both feet bare.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (14)، والبخاري (5856)، ومسلم (2097، 68)."],[675,"Abū Razīn narrated: Abū Hurayrah came out to us and struck his forehead with his hand, saying: “Do you claim that I lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that you may be guided while I go astray? I testify that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘If the strap of one of your sandals breaks, he should not walk in the other sandal until he repairs it.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2098)."],[676,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited walking in only one sandal and said: “Indeed, Satan walks wearing one sandal.”","صحيح: رواه الطحاوي في شرح مشكل الآثار (1358)."],[677,"Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said—or he said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say”: “If the strap of one of your sandals breaks, do not walk in only one sandal until you repair its strap. Do not walk in only one leather sock, do not eat with your left hand, do not sit in the iḥtibāʾ posture while wrapped in a single garment, and do not wrap yourself in the ṣammāʾ manner.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2099، 71)."],[678,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: “I used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was menstruating.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (102)، والبخاري (5925)، ومسلم (297، 9)."],[679,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated concerning the Prophet ﷺ: “He liked to begin with the right side whenever possible when combing his hair and performing wuḍūʾ.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5926)، ومسلم (268، 67)."],[680,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has hair should honor and care for it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4163)، والبيهقي في الشعب (6455)، وفي الآداب (695)."],[681,"Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated: Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh asked me: “What is istabraq?” I replied: “It is thick, coarse brocade.” He said: I heard ʿAbdullāh say: ʿUmar saw a man wearing a garment of istabraq. He brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, buy this and wear it when delegations come to you.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Silk is only worn by one who has no share in the Hereafter.” Some time passed, then the Prophet ﷺ sent ʿUmar a garment. ʿUmar brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “You sent this to me even though you said what you said concerning a garment like it?” He replied: “I only sent it to you so that you might obtain some wealth through it.” Because of this hadith, Ibn ʿUmar disliked decorative silk stripes in clothing.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6081)، ومسلم (2068، 90)."],[682,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: A man from among us had a son and named him al-Qāsim. We said to him: “We will not give you the kunyah Abū al-Qāsim, nor will we honor you with it.” This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Name your son ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6186)، ومسلم (2133، 7)."],[683,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved of your names to Allah are ʿAbdullāh and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2132)."],[684,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated: When I came to Najrān, they questioned me and said: “You recite, ‘O sister of Hārūn,’ yet Mūsā lived such-and-such a long time before ʿĪsā.” When I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I asked him about this. He said: “They used to name people after the Prophets and righteous people who came before them.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2135)."],[685,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: A son was born to me, so I brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He named him Ibrāhīm, performed taḥnīk for him with a date, supplicated for blessing for him, and handed him back to me. He was the eldest son of Abū Mūsā.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6198)، ومسلم (2145)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[686,"Yūsuf ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me in his lap, stroked my head, and named me Yūsuf.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (16407)، والطبراني (22/285)."],[687,"Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm narrated from his father: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb gathered every boy who bore the name of a Prophet and brought them into a house, intending to change their names. Their fathers then testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself had given them those names. He said: “My father, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, was among them.”","حسن: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه كما في المطالب (2796)."],[688,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated: The Prophet ﷺ did not regard anything as an evil omen. When he appointed a man to a task, he would ask his name. If he liked the man’s name, he would be pleased by it and signs of happiness would be visible on his face. If he disliked the name, signs of dislike would be visible on his face. Likewise, when he entered a town or village, he would ask its name. If he liked its name, he would be pleased and signs of happiness would be visible on his face. If he disliked its name, signs of dislike would be visible on his face.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3920)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8771)، وأحمد (22946)، وابن حبان (5827)."],[689,"Yaʿīsh al-Ghifārī narrated: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a she-camel and asked: “Who will milk her?” A man said: “I will.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is your name?” He replied: “Murrah.” He said: “Sit down.” Another man stood. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is your name?” He replied: “Jamrah.” He said: “Sit down.” Then Yaʿīsh stood. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is your name?” He replied: “Yaʿīsh.” He said: “Milk her.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 710)."],[690,"Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān narrated, each confirming the other’s account: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out at the time of al-Ḥudaybiyyah… to the end of the lengthy hadith. It includes the statement of Maʿmar: Ayyūb informed me, from ʿIkrimah, that when Suhayl ibn ʿAmr arrived, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Your matter has now been made easy for you.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2731)."],[691,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed through a land called Ghadirah, so he renamed it Khaḍirah.","صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (4556)، والطبراني في الأوسط (652)، وابن حبان (5821)."],[692,"Anas narrated: A man called out to another man in al-Baqīʿ: “O Abū al-Qāsim!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward him. The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I did not mean you. I was calling so-and-so.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2121)، ومسلم (2131)."],[693,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated: A man from among us had a son and named him al-Qāsim. The Anṣār said to him: “We will not give you the kunyah Abū al-Qāsim, nor will we grant you the pleasure of being called by it.” He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, a son was born to me and I named him al-Qāsim. The Anṣār said, ‘We will not give you the kunyah Abū al-Qāsim, nor will we grant you that pleasure.’” The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Anṣār have done well. Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah, for I am the one who distributes.” Another wording adds: “I distribute among you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3115)، ومسلم (2133، 5)."],[694,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (12770)."],[695,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah. Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot assume my form. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6197)، ومسلم (2134، 2266، 3)."],[696,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ said: “Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6188)، ومسلم (2134)."],[697,"Jābir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is named with my name should not take my kunyah, and whoever takes my kunyah should not be named with my name.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4966)، وأحمد (14357)."],[698,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited anyone from combining his name and kunyah by being named Muḥammad and also taking the kunyah Abū al-Qāsim.","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2841)، وأحمد (9598)، وابن حبان (5814)."],[699,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAmrah narrated from his paternal uncle that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not combine my name and my kunyah.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23081)."],[700,"ʿAlī narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, if a son is born to me after you, may I name him with your name and give him your kunyah?” He replied: “Yes.” Another wording adds: “That was a special permission for me.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4967)، والترمذي (2843)، وأحمد (730)، والحاكم (7737)."],[701,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: Zaynab had originally been named Barrah. It was said: “She is declaring herself righteous.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ renamed her Zaynab.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6192)، ومسلم (2141)."],[702,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed the name ʿĀṣiyah and said: “You are Jamīlah.” In another narration: A daughter of ʿUmar used to be called ʿĀṣiyah… to the end of the hadith.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2139، 14)."],[703,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: Juwayriyyah’s original name was Barrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed her name to Juwayriyyah. He disliked that someone should say: “He has just left the presence of Barrah.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2140)."],[704,"Zaynab bint Umm Salamah narrated: “My name was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Zaynab.” She said: Zaynab bint Jaḥsh also entered upon him, and her name had been Barrah, so he named her Zaynab.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2142، 18)."],[705,"Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated: I named my daughter Barrah. Zaynab bint Abī Salamah said to me: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited this name. I myself had been named Barrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Do not declare yourselves pure or righteous. Allah knows best which of you are truly righteous.’” They asked: “Then what should we name her?” He replied: “Name her Zaynab.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2142، 19)."],[706,"Muṭīʿ ibn al-Aswad narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the day of the Conquest of Makkah: “No Qurashī will be killed in captivity after this day until the Day of Resurrection.” Another narration adds: Of the men of Quraysh named al-ʿĀṣī, none had embraced Islam except Muṭīʿ. His name had been al-ʿĀṣī, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ renamed him Muṭīʿ.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1782)."],[707,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: Al-Mundhir ibn Abī Usayd was brought to the Prophet ﷺ when he was born, and the Prophet ﷺ placed him upon his thigh while Abū Usayd was sitting nearby. The Prophet ﷺ then became occupied with something before him, so Abū Usayd ordered that his son be taken away from the thigh of the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ became attentive again, he asked: “Where is the child?” Abū Usayd replied: “We sent him back, O Messenger of Allah.” He asked: “What is his name?” He replied: “So-and-so.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Rather, his name is al-Mundhir.” So he named him al-Mundhir that day.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6191)، ومسلم (2149)."],[708,"Al-Musayyib ibn Ḥazn narrated that his father came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is your name?” He replied: “Ḥazn.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You are Sahl.” He replied: “I will not change a name that my father gave me.” Ibn al-Musayyib said: “Harshness continued to remain among us afterward.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6190)."],[709,"Usāmah ibn Akhdarī narrated: A man named Aṣram was among a group who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: “What is your name?” He replied: “I am Aṣram.” He said: “Rather, you are Zurʿah.” In another wording, he said: “You are Zurʿah. What do you want?” He replied: “A name for this boy.” He said: “He is ʿĀṣim.” Then he closed his hand.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4954)، والزيادة رواها الحاكم (7729)."],[710,"Bashīr, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, had been named Zaḥm ibn Maʿbad during the pre-Islamic period. When he emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is your name?” He replied: “Zaḥm.” He said: “Rather, you are Bashīr.” …to the end of the hadith.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3230)، والنسائي (2048)، وابن ماجه (1568)، وصححه ابن حبان (3170). وله طريق آخر عند أحمد (21956)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (830)."],[711,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who was called al-Muḍṭajiʿ and renamed him al-Munbaʿith.","حسن: رواه أبو داود في الكنى كما في الإصابة (3/458)."],[712,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ heard a man asking another: “What is your name?” He replied: “Shihāb.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You are Hishām.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (24465)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (825)، والطبراني في الأوسط (2408)، وابن حبان (5823)، والحاكم (4/276-277)."],[713,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: When al-Ḥasan was born, I named him Ḥamzah. When al-Ḥusayn was born, I named him after his paternal uncle Jaʿfar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then called me and said: “I have been commanded to change the names of these two.” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” So he named them Ḥasan and Ḥusayn.","حسن: رواه أحمد (1370) - واللفظ له -، والبزار (657)، وأبو يعلى (498)، والطبراني في الكبير (3/102)."],[714,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated: “My name during the pre-Islamic period was ʿAbd ʿAmr, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.”","صحيح: رواه الحاكم (7731)، والضياء في المختارة (904)."],[715,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A female slave belonging to ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, had a foreign name, so ʿUmar renamed her Jamīlah. She said to ʿUmar: “Let the Prophet ﷺ judge between you and me.” So they went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to her: “You are Jamīlah.” ʿUmar then said: “Take it, despite yourself.”","صحيح: رواه ابن أبي عمر العدني في مسنده كما في المطالب العالية (2801)، وصحح إسناده البوصيري في إتحاف المهرة (7424)."],[716,"Hāniʾ ibn Shurayḥ narrated: He came as part of a delegation from his people to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ heard them calling a man ʿAbd al-Ḥajar. He asked him: “What is your name?” The man replied: “ʿAbd al-Ḥajar.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rather, you are ʿAbdullāh.”","حسن: رواه ابن أبي شيبة (26421)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (811)."],[717,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: An elderly woman came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was with me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: “Who are you?” She replied: “I am Jathāmah al-Muzaniyyah.” He said: “Rather, you are Ḥassānah al-Muzaniyyah. How are you all? How is your condition? How have you been since we last saw you?” She replied: “We are well. May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah.” When she left, I said: “O Messenger of Allah, you showed this old woman such special attention?” He replied: “She used to visit us during the time of Khadījah, and indeed, faithfully maintaining old relationships is part of faith.”","حسن: رواه الحاكم (40)، والبيهقي في الشعب (8701)."],[718,"ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbd al-Sulamī narrated: When a man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a name that he did not like, he would change it. Nine of us from Banū Sulaym came to him, the eldest of us being al-ʿIrbāḍ ibn Sāriyah, and we all pledged allegiance to him together.","حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (1365)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 293)."],[719,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The most degrading name in the sight of Allah is that of a man who calls himself ‘King of Kings.’ There is no true Sovereign except Allah, Mighty and Majestic.” In another wording: “The vilest of names in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection is that of a man who calls himself ‘King of Kings.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6206)، ومسلم (2143، 20)، والرواية الثانية للبخاري bukhari(6205)."],[720,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The man most detested by Allah on the Day of Resurrection, the vilest of them and the most hateful to Him, is a man who used to call himself ‘King of Kings.’ There is no King except Allah.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2143، 21)."],[721,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us from naming our slaves with four names: Aflah, Rabāḥ, Yasār, and Nāfiʿ.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2136، 10)."],[722,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved words to Allah are four: Subḥān Allah, al-ḥamdu lillāh, lā ilāha illa Allah, and Allahu akbar. It does not matter with which of them you begin. And do not name your servant Yasār, Rabāḥ, Najīḥ, or Aflah, for you might ask, ‘Is he there?’ and he will not be there, so someone will answer, ‘No.’ They are only four, so do not add to them on my authority.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2137)."],[723,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ intended to prohibit the names Yaʿlā, Barakah, Aflah, Yasār, Nāfiʿ, and similar names. Then I later saw that he remained silent concerning them and said nothing further. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away without prohibiting them. Later, ʿUmar intended to prohibit them, but then left the matter.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2138)."],[724,"Hāniʾ narrated: When he came as part of a delegation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his people, the Prophet ﷺ heard them calling him by the kunyah Abū al-Ḥakam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: “Indeed, Allah is al-Ḥakam—the Judge—and judgment belongs to Him. Why are you called Abū al-Ḥakam?” He replied: “Whenever my people disagree about something, they come to me, and I judge between them, and both sides are satisfied.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How excellent this is. What children do you have?” He replied: “I have Shurayḥ, Muslim, and ʿAbdullāh.” He asked: “Which of them is the eldest?” I replied: “Shurayḥ.” He said: “Then you are Abū Shurayḥ.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4955)، والنسائي (5387)، وصححه ابن حبان (504)، ورواه الحاكم (4/279)."],[725,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the best of people in character. I had a little brother who was called Abū ʿUmayr. I think he had already been weaned. Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and saw him, he would say: “O Abū ʿUmayr, what happened to the little nughayr?” The child used to play with that small bird.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6203)، ومسلم (2150)."],[726,"Umm Khālid bint Khālid narrated: Some garments were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, among them a small black patterned cloak. He asked: “Who do you think we should dress in this?” The people remained silent. He said: “Bring me Umm Khālid.” She was brought while being carried. The Prophet ﷺ took the cloak in his hand, dressed her in it, and said: “Wear it until it becomes worn out.” The garment had a green or yellow design on it. He said: “O Umm Khālid, this is sanāh.” In the Abyssinian language, sanāh means “beautiful.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5823)."],[727,"ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿĀ’ish, this is Jibrīl conveying salām to you.” I replied: “And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah.” She said: “He sees what we do not see.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6201)، ومسلم (2447، 91)."],[728,"Anas narrated: Umm Sulaym was among the women traveling with the caravan, and Anjashah, a servant of the Prophet ﷺ, was driving their camels. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Anjash, be gentle in driving the glass vessels.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6202)، ومسلم (2323، 71)، واللفظ للبخاري، ولفظ مسلم: «يا أنجشة»."],[729,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: Of all the names by which ʿAlī was called, the one most beloved to him was Abū Turāb, and he would be happy when he was called by it. No one gave him the name Abū Turāb except the Prophet ﷺ. One day, there was some disagreement between him and Fāṭimah, so he went out and lay down beside a wall near the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ came looking for him and was told: “There he is, lying beside the wall.” The Prophet ﷺ came to him and found that his back had become covered with dust. He began wiping the dust from his back and saying: “Sit up, O Abū Turāb.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6204)، ومسلم (2409)."],[730,"ʿĀ’ishah said: “O Messenger of Allah, all of my companions have kunyahs.” He said: “Then take the kunyah from your son ʿAbdullāh.” He meant her sister’s son, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr. So she became known by the kunyah Umm ʿAbdullāh.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4970)، وأحمد (24756)."],[731,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I brought Ibn al-Zubayr to the Prophet ﷺ. He performed taḥnīk for him with a date and said: “This is ʿAbdullāh, and you are Umm ʿAbdullāh.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (24619)، والحاكم (4/278)."],[732,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him the kunyah Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, even though no child had yet been born to him.","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (8405)، والحاكم (5364)."],[733,"Ḥamzah ibn Ṣuhayb narrated: ʿUmar said to Ṣuhayb: “Why do you take the kunyah Abū Yaḥyā when you have no child?” Ṣuhayb replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunyah Abū Yaḥyā.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3738)، وأحمد (23926)."],[734,"Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rode a donkey upon which was a Fadakī cloak, with Usāmah riding behind him, on his way to visit Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah among Banū al-Ḥārith ibn al-Khazraj before the Battle of Badr. They passed by a gathering in which ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl was present, before he had outwardly accepted Islam. The gathering contained a mixture of Muslims, idol-worshipping polytheists, and Jews. Among the Muslims was ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah. When the dust raised by the animal reached the gathering, Ibn Ubayy covered his nose with his cloak and said: “Do not cover us with dust.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them salām, stopped, dismounted, called them to Allah, and recited the Qur’an to them. ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl said: “O man, nothing could be better than what you say if it is true. But do not disturb us with it in our gatherings. Whoever comes to you, tell it to him.” ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah said: “Rather, O Messenger of Allah, come to us in our gatherings, for we love that.” The Muslims, polytheists, and Jews then began insulting one another until they almost came to blows. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued calming them until they fell silent. Then he mounted his animal and went to Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Saʿd, did you not hear what Abū Ḥubāb said?” meaning ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy. Then he mentioned what he had said. …to the end of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6207)، ومسلم (1798)."],[735,"Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from his father: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb disciplined one of his sons who had taken the kunyah Abū ʿĪsā. Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah also used the kunyah Abū ʿĪsā. ʿUmar said to him: “Is it not enough for you to take the kunyah Abū ʿAbdullāh?” Al-Mughīrah replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me that kunyah.” ʿUmar said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had his past and future sins forgiven, while we remain in our uncertain condition.” Al-Mughīrah continued to be called Abū ʿAbdullāh until he died.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4963)، والضياء في المختارة (86)، والحاكم (3/477) مختصرا."],[736,"Abū Jubayrah ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk narrated: This verse was revealed concerning us, Banū Salamah: “And do not insult one another by offensive nicknames. How evil it is to be called by a sinful name after having faith.” [Sūrat al-Ḥujurāt 49:11] He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, there was hardly a man among us who did not have two or three names. The Prophet ﷺ would call someone: “O so-and-so.” The people would say: “Stop, O Messenger of Allah. He becomes angry when called by that name.” So this verse was revealed: “And do not call one another by offensive nicknames.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4962)، والترمذي (3268)، وابن ماجه (3741)، وأحمد (18288)، والحاكم (7755)."],[737,"Ḥudhayfah narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: “Count for me how many people profess Islam.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us when we are between six hundred and seven hundred?” He replied: “You do not know. Perhaps you will be tested.” Ḥudhayfah said: “And indeed we were tested, until a man among us could only pray secretly.” In another wording: “We recorded for him the names of one thousand five hundred men, and we said: ‘Should we still fear when we are one thousand five hundred?’”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (149، 235)، والبخاري (3060)."],[738,"Abū Dharr narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No man knowingly claims another man as his father except that he has committed an act of kufr. Whoever claims what does not belong to him is not from us, and let him take his seat in the Fire. And whoever calls another man a disbeliever or says, ‘Enemy of Allah,’ when he is not such, then that accusation returns upon him.” In al-Bukhārī’s wording: “Whoever claims to belong to a people when he is not one of them, let him take his seat in the Fire.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (61)، والبخاري (3508، 6045)."],[739,"Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the greatest fabrications is for a man to claim lineage to someone other than his father, to claim that his eyes saw what they did not see, or to attribute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ something that he did not say.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (3509)."],[740,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever attributes his allegiance to patrons other than his true patrons has removed the bond of faith from his neck.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (14562)."],[741,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “My son.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2151)."],[742,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated: No one asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more questions about the Dajjāl than I did. He said to me: “My son, why are you so troubled by him? He will not harm you.” I said: “They claim that he will have rivers of water and mountains of bread with him.” He replied: “He is far more insignificant to Allah than that.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2152)."],[744,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When Allah gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a banner will be raised for every betrayer, and it will be said: ‘This is the betrayal of so-and-so, son of so-and-so.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6177)، ومسلم (1735، 9)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[746,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant may utter a word without considering what it contains, and because of it he falls into the Fire farther than the distance between the east and the west.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6477)، ومسلم (2988)، واللفظ لمسلم، ولم يذكر البخاري: «والمغرب»."],[747,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “A servant may utter a word that pleases Allah, giving it little thought, and Allah raises him by it many degrees. And a servant may utter a word that angers Allah, giving it little thought, and because of it he falls into Hell.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6478)."],[748,"Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever guarantees for me what is between his two jaws and what is between his two legs, I guarantee Paradise for him.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6474)."],[749,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah protects from the evil of what is between his two jaws and the evil of what is between his two legs will enter Paradise.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2409)، وصححه ابن حبان (5703)."],[750,"Abū Mūsā narrated: Abū al-Dardāʾ and I were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: “Whoever guards what is between his two jaws and what is between his two legs will enter Paradise.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (7275)، والحاكم (8063)، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (5371)."],[751,"Zayd ibn Aslam narrated from his father: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, took hold of his tongue and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah, Mighty and Majestic, protects from the evil of what is between his two jaws and what is between his two legs will enter Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه ابن أبي الدنيا في الصمت (20)."],[752,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “What most often causes people to enter Paradise?” He replied: “Taqwā of Allah and good character.” He was asked: “What most often causes people to enter the Fire?” He replied: “The mouth and the private parts.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2004)، وابن حبان (476)، والحاكم (7919)."],[753,"ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A person’s good fortune and bad fortune lie in what is between his two jaws.” Wahb said: “He means his tongue.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (5717)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/ح 198)."],[754,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever remains silent is saved.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2501)، وابن المبارك في الزهد (385)، وعبد الله بن وهب في الجامع (302)."],[755,"Sufyān ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Thaqafī narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me something to which I may firmly hold.” He said: “Say: ‘My Lord is Allah,’ then remain steadfast.” I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you fear most for me?” He took hold of his own tongue and said: “This.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2410)، وابن ماجه (3972)، وصححه ابن حبان (5699)، والحاكم (7874)."],[756,"Bilāl ibn al-Ḥārith al-Muzanī, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “One of you may utter a word pleasing to Allah, not realizing how far its effect will reach, and because of it Allah records His pleasure for him until the day he meets Him. And one of you may utter a word angering Allah, not realizing how far its effect will reach, and because of it Allah records His anger against him until the day he meets Him.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2319)، وابن ماجه (2669)، وصححه ابن حبان (280)، والحاكم (140)، والبيهقي في الشعب (4606)."],[757,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī said: “The limbs humble themselves before the tongue and say: ‘Fear Allah concerning us, for if you remain upright, we remain upright; and if you become crooked, we become crooked.’”","حسن: رواه أبو داود الطيالسي (2323)."],[758,"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no part of the body except that it complains of the tongue because of the sharpness of its speech.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (5)، وعنه ابن السني في عمل اليوم والليلة (7)، وابن أبي الدنيا في الصمت (13)، والبيهقي في الشعب (4596)."],[759,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not speak excessively without the remembrance of Allah, for excessive speech without the remembrance of Allah hardens the heart, and the person farthest from Allah is the one with a hard heart.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2411)، والبيهقي في الشعب (4600)."],[760,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd climbed al-Ṣafā and took hold of his tongue. He said: “O tongue, speak good and you will profit; remain silent from evil and you will be safe, before you come to regret.” Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Most of the sins of the son of Adam are committed by his tongue.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (10446)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (901)."],[761,"Aswad ibn Aṣram al-Muḥāribī came to Madinah with some very fat camels during a time of drought and barrenness. When the people of Madinah saw them, they were amazed at how fat they were. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent for the camels. They were brought, and he went out and looked at them. He asked: “Why have you brought these camels?” Aswad replied: “I want to exchange them for a servant.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who has a servant?” ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, said: “I do, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Bring her.” ʿUthmān brought her. When Aswad saw her, he said: “This is the kind I want.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “She is yours, so take her.” Aswad took her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received his camels. Aswad then said: “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He said: “Can you control your tongue?” Aswad replied: “What could I control if I cannot control my tongue?” He said: “Can you control your hand?” Aswad replied: “What could I control if I cannot control my hand?” He said: “Then say nothing with your tongue except what is good, and extend your hand only toward what is good.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (813)، والبيهقي في الشعب (4583)."],[762,"ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrated: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out riding his mount, with his Companions traveling with him. Muʿādh ibn Jabal said: “O Prophet of Allah, will you permit me, if you are pleased, to come closer to you?” He replied: “Yes.” Muʿādh came near him, and they traveled together. Muʿādh said: “May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. I ask Allah to make our day of death come before yours. If something should happen—and we hope, Allah willing, that nothing will—what deeds should we perform after you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, then said: “Jihād in the path of Allah.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jihād is indeed an excellent thing, but something more within people’s ability than that is fasting and charity.” He said: “Fasting and charity are excellent things.” Muʿādh then mentioned every kind of good deed that the son of Adam performs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is something even better for people than that.” Muʿādh asked: “What could be better than that, O Prophet of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointed toward his mouth and said: “Silence, except when speaking good.” Muʿādh asked: “Will we really be held accountable for what our tongues say?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck Muʿādh’s thigh and said: “O Muʿādh, may your mother lose you—or whatever expression Allah willed him to say—what else throws people onto their faces in Hell except what their tongues have uttered? Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent from evil. Speak good and you will profit; remain silent from evil and you will be safe.”","صحيح: رواه الحاكم (7774) والسياق له، والطبراني في الكبير كما في جامع المسانيد لابن كثير (4914)."],[763,"Abū Shurayḥ al-Kaʿbī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. His special hospitality is for one day and one night, and hospitality is for three days. Whatever comes after that is charity. And it is not lawful for the guest to remain with him until he causes him hardship.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (22)، والبخاري (6135). ورواه البخاري (6019)، ومسلم (48، 14) عقب الحديث (1726)."],[764,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said three times: “May Allah have mercy on a person who speaks and thereby gains, or remains silent and thereby remains safe.”","حسن: رواه البيهقي في الشعب (4589)، وابن أبي الدنيا في الصمت (41)."],[765,"ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Fire, sought refuge from it, and turned his face away three times. Then he said: “Protect yourselves from the Fire even with half a date. If you cannot find even that, then with a good word.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6023)، ومسلم (1016، 68)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[766,"Ṣuhayb narrated: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed ʿAṣr, he would speak softly.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3340)."],[767,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates the overly eloquent man who twists and rolls his tongue in speech as a cow rolls its tongue.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5005)، والترمذي (2853)، وأحمد (6543)."],[768,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: Two men came from the east and delivered speeches, and the people were amazed by their eloquence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some eloquence is like magic.” Or: “Indeed, some forms of eloquence are like magic.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5767)."],[769,"Abū Wā’il narrated: ʿAmmār delivered a sermon to us that was brief yet eloquent. When he stepped down, we said: “O Abū al-Yaqẓān, you spoke eloquently and concisely. If only you had spoken a little longer!” He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The length of a man’s prayer and the brevity of his sermon are signs of his understanding. So lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon, and indeed some eloquence is like magic.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (869)."],[770,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, some eloquence is like magic. Among the worst of people are those who will be alive when the Hour comes, and those who take graves as places of worship.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (4342)."],[771,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6145)."],[772,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom.”","صحيح: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (2101، 2102)."],[773,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and began speaking. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, some eloquence is like magic, and some poetry contains wisdom.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5011)، والترمذي (2845)، وابن ماجه (3756)، وابن حبان (5778)، واللفظ لأبي داود."],[774,"Al-Sharīd narrated: One day I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he asked: “Do you know any of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abī al-Ṣalt?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “Go on.” So I recited a verse. He said: “Go on.” I recited another verse. He continued saying: “Go on,” until I had recited one hundred verses to him. Another narration adds: “He almost embraced Islam through his poetry.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2255)."],[775,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The truest statement ever spoken by a poet is the statement of Labīd: ‘Indeed, everything apart from Allah is false.’ And Umayyah ibn Abī al-Ṣalt almost embraced Islam.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6147)، ومسلم (2256)، وأكثر مسلم من ذكر طرقه وألفاظه."],[776,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came upon his wives while a camel-driver named Anjashah was driving their mounts. He said: “Careful, O Anjashah. Drive gently with the glass vessels.” Abū Qilābah said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke a phrase which, if one of you were to use it, you would make fun of him for it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6149)، ومسلم (2323، 71)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[777,"Umm Sulaym narrated: She was with the wives of the Prophet ﷺ while a camel-driver was driving their mounts. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Anjashah, drive gently with the glass vessels.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (27116)، والنسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (530)، والطبراني (25/121)."],[778,"Al-Haytham ibn Abī Sinān narrated that he heard Abū Hurayrah, while narrating stories, mention that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Your brother does not speak obscenely.” He meant ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah. He recited: Among us is the Messenger of Allah, reciting His Book, when the well-known light of dawn breaks forth. He showed us guidance after blindness, so our hearts are certain that whatever he says will come to pass. He spends the night keeping his side away from his bed, while the sleeping places weigh heavily upon the disbelievers.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6151)."],[779,"Jundub ibn Sufyān narrated: The finger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wounded and bled during one of the campaigns. He said: “You are only a finger that has bled, and whatever you have suffered is in the path of Allah.” In another narration: While the Prophet ﷺ was walking, a stone struck him, causing him to stumble and injure his finger. He said: “You are only a finger that has bled, and whatever you have suffered is in the path of Allah.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2802)، ومسلم (1796، 112). والرواية الثانية أخرجها البخاري (6146)، ومسلم (1796، 113)، واللفظ للبخاري، ولم يسق مسلم لفظه."],[780,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ narrated: We went out with the Prophet ﷺ toward Khaybar and traveled by night. A man from the group said to ʿĀmir: “O ʿĀmir, will you not let us hear some of your chants?” ʿĀmir was skilled in camel-driving chants, so he began chanting to the people: O Allah, were it not for You, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So forgive us; may we be sacrificed for You for what we have preserved, and make our feet firm when we meet the enemy. And send tranquility down upon us; when they cry out against us, we refuse to flee, and with cries they have called others against us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who is this driver?” They replied: “ʿĀmir ibn al-Akwaʿ.” He said: “May Allah have mercy on him.” A man from the group said: “It has become certain, O Prophet of Allah. If only you had allowed us to enjoy his company longer!” The narration continues: When the battle lines met, ʿĀmir’s sword was short.\nHe struck at the leg of a Jewish fighter, but the blade rebounded and struck ʿĀmir himself on the knee, causing his death. When they returned, Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me and took my hand. He asked: “What is wrong with you?” I replied: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. They claim that ʿĀmir’s deeds were nullified.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever said that has lied. He has two rewards.” He joined two of his fingers together and said: “He was indeed one who strove and fought hard. Few Arabs have ever walked the earth like him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4196)، ومسلم (1802، 123)، واللفظ للبخاري، والحديث مذكور بطوله في غزوة خيبر."],[781,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has revealed concerning poetry what He has revealed.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “The believer strives with his sword and with his tongue. By the One in whose hand is my soul, what you hurl at them with your poetry is like the shooting of arrows.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (15785، 27174)، والطبراني في الكبير (19/75)، وصححه ابن حبان (5786)."],[782,"Shurayḥ ibn Hāniʾ al-Ḥārithī narrated: ʿĀ’ishah was asked: “Did the Prophet ﷺ ever quote lines of poetry?” She replied: “He used to quote the poetry of Ibn Rawāḥah, and he would say: ‘News will be brought to you by one whom you did not provision.’”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2848) واللفظ له، وأحمد (25071)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (867)."],[783,"Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated: I asked Jābir ibn Samurah: “Did you used to sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He replied: “Yes, very often. He would not rise from the place where he had prayed Ṣubḥ until the sun had risen. Once the sun rose, he would get up. His Companions would converse and mention events from the pre-Islamic period, and they would laugh while the Prophet ﷺ would smile.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2322، 69)."],[784,"Simāk narrated: I asked Jābir ibn Samurah: “Did you used to sit with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He replied: “Yes. He was often silent and laughed little. His Companions would recite poetry in his presence and speak about various matters among themselves. They would laugh, and sometimes he would smile.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (20810) - واللفظ له -، والترمذي (2850)، وصححه ابن حبان (5781)."],[785,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah during the ʿUmrat al-Qaḍāʾ, while ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah walked before him reciting: Make way, O sons of the disbelievers, from his path; today we strike you for its revelation, with blows that remove heads from their resting places and cause a close friend to forget his friend. ʿUmar said to him: “O Ibn Rawāḥah, are you reciting poetry in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and within the Sacred Sanctuary of Allah, Mighty and Majestic?”\nThe Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Leave him, for it strikes them more swiftly than the shooting of arrows.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2847)، والنسائي (2873)، وابن خزيمة (2680)، وابن حبان (5788)."],[786,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about poetry. He replied: “It is speech. What is good in it is good, and what is ugly in it is ugly.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (4760)."],[787,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For a man’s body cavity to be filled with pus that corrupts it is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6155)، ومسلم (2257)."],[788,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “For the inside of one of you to be filled with pus is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6154)."],[789,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “For the inside of one of you to be filled with pus that corrupts it is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2258)."],[790,"Nawfal ibn Abī ʿAqrab narrated: I asked ʿĀ’ishah: “Was poetry recited and listened to in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” She replied: “It was the type of speech most disliked by him.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (25020، 25150)، وإسحاق بن راهويه (1687)."],[791,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-ʿArj, a poet appeared reciting poetry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take hold of Satan,” or, “Restrain Satan. For a man’s inside to be filled with pus is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2259)."],[792,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ḥassān ibn Thābit: “Satirize them—or respond to their satire—and Jibrīl is with you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6153)، ومسلم (2486)."],[793,"Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated: He heard Ḥassān ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī call upon Abū Hurayrah as a witness, saying: “O Abū Hurayrah, I ask you by Allah: did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘O Ḥassān, respond in defense of the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit.’?” Abū Hurayrah replied: “Yes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6152)، ومسلم (2485، 152)."],[794,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Ḥassān ibn Thābit sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to satirize the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “But what about my lineage?” Ḥassān replied: “I will draw you out from among them as a hair is drawn out of dough.” ʿUrwah said: I began speaking badly about Ḥassān in the presence of ʿĀ’ishah. She said: “Do not insult him, for he used to defend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6150)، ومسلم (2489)."],[795,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: ʿUmar passed by Ḥassān while he was reciting poetry in the mosque and looked at him disapprovingly. Ḥassān said: “I used to recite poetry in this mosque when someone better than you was present.” Then he turned to Abū Hurayrah and said: “I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Respond in defense of me. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit.’?” Abū Hurayrah replied: “By Allah, yes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3212)، ومسلم (2485)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[796,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the people guilty of the greatest falsehood is a man who satirizes another man and then reviles his entire tribe, and a man who disowns his own father and thereby accuses his mother of fornication.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3761) والسياق له، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (874)، وصححه ابن حبان (5785)."],[798,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If there are three people, two of them should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (14)، والبخاري (6288)، ومسلم (2183)."],[799,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you are three people, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the other until you mingle with other people, because that may cause him sadness.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6290)، ومسلم (2184، 37)."],[800,"Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated: I saw Ibn ʿUmar speaking privately with a man. Another man came and inserted himself between them, so Ibn ʿUmar struck him on the chest and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When two people are speaking privately, a third person should not enter between them except with their permission.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (6225)، والدارقطني في العلل (13/177)، وأبو نعيم في حلية الأولياء (8/198)."],[801,"ʿĀ’ishah, the Mother of the Believers, narrated: All the wives of the Prophet ﷺ were with him, and not one of them was absent. Fāṭimah came walking, and her manner of walking was almost exactly like that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he saw her, he welcomed her and said: “Welcome, my daughter.” Then he seated her on his right or his left and spoke privately to her. She began to weep intensely. When he saw her distress, he spoke privately to her a second time, and she laughed. I said to her: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ singled you out from among all his wives for private conversation, and yet you are crying?” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up, I asked her: “What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?” She replied: “I would never disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I said to her: “I insist upon you, by the right I have over you, that you tell me what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to you.” She replied: “Now, yes.” She said: The first time he spoke privately to me, he informed me that Jibrīl used to review the Qur’an with him once—or twice—each year, but that this year he had reviewed it with him twice. He said: “I do not think this means anything except that my appointed time has drawn near. So fear Allah and be patient, for I am an excellent predecessor for you.” She said: That is why I wept as you saw. When he saw my distress, he spoke privately to me again and said: “O Fāṭimah, would you not be pleased to be the leader of the believing women—or the leader of the women of this Ummah?” She said: That is why I laughed as you saw.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6285)، ومسلم (2450، 98)، والسياق لمسلم."],[802,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: One day the Prophet ﷺ distributed something. A man from the Anṣār said: “By Allah, this is a distribution in which the Face of Allah was not intended.” I said: “By Allah, I will certainly tell the Prophet ﷺ.” I went to him while he was among a group of people and spoke to him privately. He became angry until his face turned red, then said: “May Allah have mercy on Mūsā. He was harmed with more than this, yet he remained patient.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6291)، ومسلم (1062، 141)."],[803,"Anas narrated: The prayer had been called to begin, while a man was speaking privately with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The man continued speaking privately with him for so long that the Companions fell asleep. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood and prayed.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6292)، ومسلم (376، 124)."],[804,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ entrusted me with a secret, and I never told anyone about it afterward. Even Umm Sulaym asked me about it, but I did not tell her.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6289)، ومسلم (2482، 146)."],[805,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: Allah, the Exalted, said: “The son of Adam offends Me by cursing time, while I am the One who controls time. The command is in My hand; I alternate the night and the day.” In another wording, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: “The son of Adam offends Me by saying, ‘What a wretched time!’ None of you should say, ‘What a wretched time,’ for I am the One who controls time. I alternate its night and day, and whenever I will, I take them away.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7491)، ومسلم (2246، 2)."],[806,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not curse time, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: ‘I am the One who controls time. The days and nights belong to Me. I renew them and cause them to pass away, and I bring kings after kings.’”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (10438)."],[807,"Abū Qatādah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not curse time, for Allah is the One who controls time.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (22552)."],[808,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not call grapes ‘karm,’ for true nobility is in the heart of the believer.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6183)، ومسلم (2247، 7)."],[809,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should curse time, for Allah is the One who controls time. And none of you should call grapes ‘karm,’ for the truly noble one is the Muslim man.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2247، 6)."],[810,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not call grapes ‘karm,’ and do not say, ‘What a wretched time,’ for Allah is the One who controls time.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6182)."],[811,"Wā’il ibn Ḥujr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not call it al-karm. Rather, call it grapes or al-ḥabalah.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2248، 12)."],[812,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you hear a man saying, ‘The people are ruined,’ then he is the most ruined of them.”","صحيح: رواه مالك (2)، ومسلم (2623)."],[813,"Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ related: A man said: “By Allah, Allah will never forgive so-and-so.” Allah, the Exalted, said: “Who is this who swears concerning Me that I will not forgive so-and-so? I have forgiven so-and-so and rendered your deeds worthless.” Or words to that effect.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2621، 137)."],[814,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There were two men among the Children of Israel who were like brothers. One of them used to commit sins, while the other was devoted to worship. Whenever the worshipper saw the other committing a sin, he would say, ‘Stop.’ One day he found him committing a sin and said, ‘Stop.’ The sinner replied, ‘Leave me to my Lord. Have you been appointed as a watcher over me?’ The worshipper said, ‘By Allah, Allah will never forgive you,’ or, ‘Allah will never admit you into Paradise.’ Then their souls were taken, and they were brought together before the Lord of the worlds. Allah said to the worshipper: ‘Did you possess knowledge of Me? Or did you have power over what is in My hand?’ Then He said to the sinner: ‘Go and enter Paradise by My mercy.’ And He said concerning the other: ‘Take him to the Fire.’” Abū Hurayrah said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, he uttered a single word that ruined both his worldly life and his Hereafter.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4901)، وأحمد (8749)، وابن حبان (5712)."],[815,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘Feed your lord,’ ‘Help your lord perform wuḍūʾ,’ or ‘Give your lord something to drink.’ Rather, let him say, ‘My master’ or ‘my patron.’ And none of you should say, ‘My male slave’ or ‘my female slave.’ Rather, let him say, ‘My young man,’ ‘my young woman,’ or ‘my servant.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2552)، ومسلم (2249، 15)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[816,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My male slave’ or ‘my female slave.’ All of you are servants of Allah, and all of your women are female servants of Allah. Rather, let him say, ‘My servant,’ ‘my maid,’ ‘my young man,’ or ‘my young woman.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2249، 13)."],[817,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My slave,’ for all of you are servants of Allah. Rather, let him say, ‘My young man.’ And a servant should not say, ‘My lord,’ but should say, ‘My master.’” In another wording: “A servant should not say to his master, ‘My patron,’ for your true Patron is Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2249، 14)."],[818,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My soul has become foul.’ Rather, let him say, ‘My soul feels unsettled.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6179)، ومسلم (2250)."],[819,"Sahl ibn Ḥunayf narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should say, ‘My soul has become foul.’ Rather, let him say, ‘My soul feels unsettled.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6180)، ومسلم (2251)."],[820,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever among you swears and says in his oath, ‘By al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā,’ should say, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah.’ And whoever says to his companion, ‘Come, let me gamble with you,’ should give charity.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6301)، ومسلم (1647، 5)."],[821,"Umm Salamah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ awoke and said: “Subḥān Allah! How many treasures have been sent down, and how many trials have been sent down! Who will awaken the women of these chambers” —meaning his wives, so that they might pray— “Many a woman clothed in this world will be naked in the Hereafter.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6218)."],[822,"Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: She came to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was observing iʿtikāf in the mosque during the last ten nights of Ramaḍān. She spoke with him for part of the evening, then got up to return home. The Prophet ﷺ stood and accompanied her. When she reached the mosque door near the residence of Umm Salamah, two men from the Anṣār passed by them. They greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and continued on. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: “Take it easy. This is only Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy.” They said: “Subḥān Allah, O Messenger of Allah!” They were distressed that he felt any need to explain himself. He said: “Satan flows through the son of Adam like blood, and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6219)، ومسلم (2175)."],[823,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib came out from the presence of the Prophet ﷺ during the illness from which he died. The people asked: “O Abū al-Ḥasan, how is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ this morning?” He replied: “By the praise of Allah, he is feeling better this morning.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6266)."],[824,"Muʿādh ibn Jabal narrated: I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, with nothing between me and him except the rear part of the saddle. He said: “O Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and gladly responding to you.” He traveled for a while, then said: “O Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and gladly responding to you.” After traveling a while longer, he again said: “O Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and gladly responding to you.” He asked: “Do you know what right Allah has over His servants?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “The right of Allah over His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he traveled for a while and said: “O Muʿādh ibn Jabal.” I replied: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and gladly responding to you.” He asked: “Do you know what right the servants have with Allah if they do that?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That He will not punish them.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6267)، ومسلم (30، 48)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[825,"Abū Dharr narrated: I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ one evening through the lava plain of Madinah when Mount Uḥud appeared before us. He said: “O Abū Dharr, I would not like to have gold equal to Mount Uḥud and then have a night—or three nights—pass while even one dinar of it remained with me, except something I had set aside to repay a debt, unless I distributed it among the servants of Allah like this, and this, and this.” He gestured with his hand in different directions. Then he said: “O Abū Dharr.” I replied: “At your service and gladly responding to you, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Those who possess the most will be those who possess the least…” to the end of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6268)، ومسلم (94، 32)."],[826,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: He and Abū Ṭalḥah were returning with the Prophet ﷺ, and Ṣafiyyah was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on his mount. At one point along the road, the she-camel stumbled, causing the Prophet ﷺ and Ṣafiyyah to fall. Abū Ṭalḥah—I think the narrator said—jumped down from his camel and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom! Have you been hurt?” He replied: “No, but attend to the woman.” Abū Ṭalḥah covered his own face with his garment and went toward her. He placed his garment over her, and she stood up. Then he secured their riding animal for them, and they mounted again. When they reached the outskirts of Madinah—or came within sight of Madinah—the Prophet ﷺ said: “We return, repenting, worshipping, and praising our Lord.” He continued saying this until he entered Madinah.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6185)، ومسلم (1345)."],[827,"Abū Dharr narrated: The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Abū Dharr.” I replied: “At your service and gladly responding to you, O Messenger of Allah, and may I be your ransom.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5226)."],[828,"ʿAlī narrated: “I never heard the Prophet ﷺ combine mention of both his parents as a ransom for anyone except Saʿd ibn Mālik. I heard him say on the Day of Uḥud: ‘O Saʿd, shoot! May my father and mother be your ransom.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4059)، ومسلم (2411)."],[829,"Abū Qatādah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and the people became thirsty. Those who were quick went ahead, while I remained close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ throughout that night. He said to me: “May Allah protect you because of the way you protected His Prophet.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (681)."],[830,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Some people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about soothsayers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They are nothing.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, sometimes they tell us something that turns out to be true.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “That is a word of truth which a jinn snatches and then repeats into the ear of his ally like the clucking of a hen, after which they mix more than a hundred lies into it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6213)، ومسلم (2228، 123)."],[831,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, accompanied by a black servant of his named Anjashah who was chanting to drive the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Easy, O Anjashah! Be gentle with the glass vessels.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6161)، ومسلم (2323، 70)."],[832,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man leading a sacrificial camel. He said to him: “Ride it.” The man replied: “O Messenger of Allah, it is a sacrificial camel.” He said: “Ride it, woe to you!” This was on the second or third time.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (144)، والبخاري (6160)، ومسلم (1322، 371)."],[833,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ saw a man leading a sacrificial camel. He said: “Ride it.” The man replied: “It is a sacrificial camel.” He said: “Ride it.” The man repeated: “It is a sacrificial camel.” He said: “Ride it, woe to you!”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6159)، ومسلم (1323)."],[834,"Anas narrated: A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour occur?” He replied: “Woe to you! What have you prepared for it?” The man said: “I have prepared nothing for it except that I love Allah and His Messenger.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You will be with those whom you love.” We asked: “And are we likewise?” He replied: “Yes.” Anas said: We were extremely happy that day. Then a young servant of al-Mughīrah passed by, who was around my age. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If this boy lives, old age will not overtake him before your Hour comes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6167)، ومسلم (2953، 139)."],[835,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Aflaḥ, the brother of Abū al-Quʿays, sought permission to enter upon me after the verse of ḥijāb had been revealed. I said: “By Allah, I will not give him permission until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, because the brother of Abū al-Quʿays was not the one who nursed me; rather, it was the wife of Abū al-Quʿays who nursed me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and I said: “O Messenger of Allah, this man did not nurse me; rather, it was his brother’s wife who nursed me.” He said: “Give him permission, for he is your paternal uncle through breastfeeding. May your right hand be dusty!” ʿUrwah said: Because of this, ʿĀ’ishah used to say: “Consider unlawful through breastfeeding whatever is unlawful through blood relationship.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6156)، ومسلم (1444)."],[836,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ intended to depart, but he saw Ṣafiyyah standing at the entrance of her tent, distressed and saddened because she had begun menstruating. He said: “ʿAqrā ḥalqā!” —an expression used in the dialect of Quraysh— “Are you going to hold us back?” Then he asked: “Did you perform the ṭawāf of ifāḍah on the Day of Sacrifice?” meaning the ṭawāf. She replied: “Yes.” He said: “Then depart.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6157)، ومسلم (1211، 387) عقب الحديث (1328)."],[837,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Ṣayyād: “I have hidden something for you. What is it?” He replied: “Al-dukh.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Be gone!”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6172)."],[840,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The strong believer is better and more beloved to Allah than the weak believer, though there is good in both. Be eager for what benefits you, seek Allah’s help, and do not give up. If something befalls you, do not say, ‘If only I had done such-and-such, then such-and-such would have happened.’ Rather say, ‘Allah decreed, and whatever He willed, He did,’ for ‘if only’ opens the door to the work of Satan.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2664)."],[841,"Al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād said: The couple who had invoked mutual curses were mentioned in the presence of Ibn ʿAbbās. Ibn Shaddād asked: “Were they the two concerning whom the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned her’?” Ibn ʿAbbās replied: “No. That was another woman who openly displayed suspicious conduct.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7238)، ومسلم (1497، 13)."],[842,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would cause hardship for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk.” Al-Bukhārī adds: “with every prayer.” Muslim’s wording is: “at every prayer.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (145)، والبخاري (887)، ومسلم (252)."],[843,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ continued fasting without breaking it at night toward the end of the month, and some people also continued fasting. When this reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Had the month been extended for me, I would have continued such uninterrupted fasting that those who go to extremes would have abandoned their extremism. I am not like you; my Lord continually provides me with nourishment and drink.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7241)، ومسلم (1104، 60)."],[844,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Had I known at the beginning what I came to know later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animals, and I would have exited iḥrām with the people when they exited it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7229)، ومسلم (1211، 130)."],[845,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If I had gold equal to Mount Uḥud, I would love that three days not pass while a single dinar remained with me—except something I had reserved for a debt—so long as I could find someone to accept it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7228)، ومسلم (991)."],[846,"Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: On the Day of al-Aḥzāb, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was carrying earth with us, until the dust covered the whiteness of his stomach. He was saying: “By Allah, were it not for You, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So send tranquility down upon us; indeed, these people have rebelled against us.” He said that he would sometimes say: “Indeed, the people have rebelled against us; whenever they seek to subject us to trial, we refuse.” He would raise his voice while chanting it.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7236)، ومسلم (1803)."],[847,"Abū Mūsā narrated: I was with the Prophet ﷺ while he was staying at al-Jiʿrānah between Makkah and Madinah, and Bilāl was with him. A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Will you not fulfill what you promised me?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Receive glad tidings.” The man replied: “You have said ‘receive glad tidings’ to me too many times.” The Prophet ﷺ turned toward Abū Mūsā and Bilāl with the appearance of someone displeased and said: “He has rejected the glad tidings, so you two accept them.” They said: “We accept them.” He then called for a cup containing water, washed his hands and face in it, and spat lightly into it. Then he said: “Drink from it, pour some over your faces and chests, and rejoice.” They took the cup and did so. Umm Salamah called from behind the curtain: “Leave some for your mother.” So they left some of it for her.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4328)، ومسلم (2497)."],[848,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: One night the Prophet ﷺ was unable to sleep and said: “If only a righteous man from among my Companions would guard me tonight.” Then we heard the sound of weapons. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Who is this?” It was said: “Saʿd, O Messenger of Allah. I have come to guard you.” The Prophet ﷺ then slept until we could hear him breathing deeply in sleep.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7231)، ومسلم (2410، 39)."],[849,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I wish that I could fight in the path of Allah and be killed, then be brought back to life and killed again, then be brought back to life and killed again.” Abū Hurayrah would repeat these words three times and say: “I testify by Allah.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (27)، والبخاري (7227)، ومسلم (1876، 106)."],[850,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no permissible envy except in two cases: a man whom Allah has taught the Qur’an, so he recites it throughout the hours of the night and the day, and a neighbor hears him and says, ‘If only I had been given what so-and-so has been given, so that I could do as he does’; and a man whom Allah has given wealth, and he spends it in what is right, so another man says, ‘If only I had been given what so-and-so has been given, so that I could do as he does.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5026)."],[851,"Anas narrated: “Had I not heard the Prophet ﷺ say, ‘Do not wish for death,’ I would have wished for it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7233)، ومسلم (2680، 11)."],[852,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should wish for death because of a hardship that has afflicted him. If he absolutely must say something, then let him say: ‘O Allah, keep me alive for as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die when death is better for me.’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5671)، ومسلم (2680)."],[853,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should wish for death. If he is a doer of good, perhaps he will increase in goodness; and if he is a wrongdoer, perhaps he will seek Allah’s pleasure and repent.”\nIn another wording: “None of you should wish for death or pray for it before it comes to him. When one of you dies, his deeds come to an end, and an increase in the lifespan of a believer only increases him in good.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7235)، ومسلم (2682)."],[854,"Sālim Abū al-Naḍr, the freedman of ʿUmar ibn ʿUbaydullāh and his secretary, narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā wrote to him, and I read the letter. It contained the statement that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for safety and well-being.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7237)، ومسلم (1742، 20)."],[855,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibrīl and says, ‘Indeed, I love so-and-so, so love him.’ Jibrīl then loves him. Then Jibrīl announces in the heavens, ‘Indeed, Allah loves so-and-so, so love him,’ and the inhabitants of the heavens love him. Then acceptance is placed for him on earth. And when Allah hates a servant, He calls Jibrīl and says, ‘Indeed, I hate so-and-so, so hate him.’ Jibrīl then hates him. Then he announces among the inhabitants of the heavens, ‘Indeed, Allah hates so-and-so, so hate him,’ and they hate him. Then hatred for him is placed on earth.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2637، 157)، والبخاري (7485)."],[856,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no servant except that he has a reputation in the heavens. If his reputation in the heavens is good, a good reputation is placed for him on earth; and if his reputation in the heavens is bad, a bad reputation is placed for him on earth.”","حسن: رواه البزار (9202)، والبيهقي في الزهد الكبير (820)."],[857,"Anas narrated: A funeral procession passed by, and the people praised the deceased. The Prophet ﷺ said: “It has become certain.” Then another funeral procession passed by, and the people spoke badly of the deceased. He again said: “It has become certain.” ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb asked: “What has become certain?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “You praised this one, so Paradise has become certain for him. You spoke badly of the other, so the Fire has become certain for him. You are Allah’s witnesses on earth.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1367)، ومسلم (949)."],[858,"Abū Bakr ibn Abī Zuhayr al-Thaqafī narrated from his father: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us at al-Nabāwah—or al-Banāwah—which is in al-Ṭā’if, and said: “Soon you will be able to recognize the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.” They asked: “How is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “By good praise and bad praise. You are Allah’s witnesses over one another.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (4221)، وأحمد (15439)، وابن حبان (7384)، والحاكم (8345)."],[859,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ at al-Nabāwah—or al-Nabāʾah—say: “Soon you will recognize the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, by what?” He replied: “By good praise and bad praise.”","حسن: رواه البزار (1134)."],[860,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, direct me to an action which, if I follow it, will admit me into Paradise, but do not give me too much.” He said: “Do not become angry.” Another man came and said: “O Prophet of Allah, direct me to an action which, if I perform it, will admit me into Paradise.” He said: “Be a doer of good.” The man asked: “How will I know that I am a doer of good?” He replied: “Ask your neighbors. If they say that you are a doer of good, then you are a doer of good; and if they say that you are an evildoer, then you are an evildoer.”","صحيح: رواه البزار (9245)، والنسائي في جزء إملائه (16، 17)، والحاكم (1399)."],[861,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “How can I know when I have done good and when I have done wrong?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “If you hear your neighbors saying, ‘You have done good,’ then you have done good. And if you hear them saying, ‘You have done wrong,’ then you have done wrong.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (4223)، وأحمد (3808)، وابن حبان (525، 526)."],[862,"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Qays narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When a man comes to a people and they say, ‘Welcome,’ then welcome is for him until the day he meets his Lord. And when a man comes to a people and they say, ‘Qahṭan’—a word of hardship and deprivation—then hardship is for him on the Day of Resurrection.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (8136)، وصححه الحاكم (6235)."],[863,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the people of Paradise is the one whose ears Allah fills with people’s good praise while he hears it. And among the people of the Fire is the one whose ears Allah fills with people’s evil praise while he hears it.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (4224)، والطبراني في الكبير (12787)."],[864,"Abū Mūsā narrated: The Prophet ﷺ heard a man praising another man and exaggerating in his praise. He said: “You have destroyed the man,” or: “You have broken the man’s back.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6060)، ومسلم (3001)."],[865,"Hammām ibn al-Ḥārith narrated: A man began praising ʿUthmān excessively. Al-Miqdād went forward, knelt on his knees—he was a large man—and began throwing pebbly dust toward the man’s face. ʿUthmān asked: “What is the matter with you?” Al-Miqdād replied: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see those who excessively praise others, throw dust in their faces.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (3002، 69)."],[866,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Throw dust into the mouths of excessive flatterers.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (5769)، والبزار (5413-5414)، والطبراني في مسند الشاميين (275)."],[867,"Maʿbad al-Juhanī narrated: Muʿāwiyah rarely narrated anything from the Prophet ﷺ. Yet he would hardly allow a Friday to pass without narrating these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding of the religion. This wealth is sweet and attractive, and whoever takes it by right will be blessed in it. Beware of excessive mutual praise, for it is slaughter.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (16837، 16846)، وابن ماجه (3743)."],[868,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned what he mentioned concerning allowing one’s lower garment to hang down, Abū Bakr said: “O Messenger of Allah, one side of my garment sometimes slips down.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “You are not one of those people.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6062)."],[869,"Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “What about a man who does a good deed and people praise him for it?” He replied: “That is the believer’s immediate glad tidings.” In another wording: “and people love him because of it” instead of: “and people praise him for it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2642، 166)."],[870,"Abū Bakrah narrated: A man praised another man in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said repeatedly: “Woe to you! You have cut your companion’s neck! You have cut your companion’s neck!” Then he said: “If one of you absolutely must praise his companion, let him say: ‘I consider so-and-so to be such-and-such, and Allah is his Reckoner. I do not declare anyone pure before Allah. I consider him—if he truly knows this about him—to be such-and-such.’”\nIn another wording: A man was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and another man said: “O Messenger of Allah, there is no man after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ better than him in such-and-such matters.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said words to the same effect.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6162)، ومسلم (3000، 65)."],[871,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Baṭn Buwāṭ while he was seeking al-Majdī ibn ʿAmr al-Juhanī. Five, six, or seven of us would take turns riding a single water-carrying camel. When the turn of a man from the Anṣār came, he made his camel kneel, mounted it, and urged it forward. The camel hesitated somewhat, so he said to it: “Move! May Allah curse you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who is this cursing his camel?” The man replied: “It is I, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Get down from it, for a cursed animal must not accompany us. Do not supplicate against yourselves, do not supplicate against your children, and do not supplicate against your wealth, lest you happen upon an hour in which Allah is asked for something and He responds to you.” to the end of the hadith.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (3009)."],[872,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that Abū Sufyān ibn Ḥarb informed him: Heraclius sent for him while he was among a group of Quraysh who were trading in al-Shām. They came to him—and he narrated the hadith. Then Heraclius called for the letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and it was read aloud. It contained: “In the Name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Especially Merciful. From Muḥammad, the servant of Allah and His Messenger, to Heraclius, the ruler of the Romans. Peace be upon whoever follows guidance. To proceed…”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6260)، ومسلم (1773)."],[873,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, al-Zubayr, and al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad and said: “Proceed until you reach Rawḍat Khākh. There you will find a woman traveling in a litter who is carrying a letter. Take it from her.” We set out, our horses racing with us, until we reached the place. We found the woman and said: “Bring out the letter.” She replied: “I have no letter.” We said: “You will either bring out the letter or we will remove your garments to search for it.” She then brought it out from the braids of her hair. We took it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was a letter from Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah to some of the polytheists of Makkah, informing them of some of the plans of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ… to the end of the hadith.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3007)، ومسلم (2494)."],[874,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My example and the example of the Prophets before me is like that of a man who built a house and made it excellent and beautiful except for the place of one brick in a corner. People began walking around it, admiring it, and saying, ‘If only this brick were put in place!’ I am that brick, and I am the Seal of the Prophets.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3535)، ومسلم (2286، 22)."],[875,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “My example and the example of the Prophets is like a man who built a house, completed it, and made it beautiful except for the place of one brick. People would enter it, marvel at it, and say, ‘If only the place of this brick were completed.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the place of that brick. I came and sealed the line of the Prophets.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3534)، ومسلم (2287)."],[876,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My example among the Prophets is like that of a man who built a house and made it excellent, complete, and beautiful, but left the place of one brick unfinished. People walk around the building, admire it, and say, ‘If only the place of that brick were completed.’ Among the Prophets, I am in the position of that brick.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (3613)، وأحمد (21243)."],[877,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The example of the believer who recites the Qur’an is like the citron: its taste is pleasant and its fragrance is pleasant. The believer who does not recite it is like a date: its taste is pleasant but it has no fragrance. The example of the wicked person who recites the Qur’an is like basil: its fragrance is pleasant but its taste is bitter. And the example of the wicked person who does not recite the Qur’an is like the colocynth: its taste is bitter and it has no fragrance.” In Muslim’s wording, “the hypocrite” appears instead of “the wicked person.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (502)، ومسلم (797، 243)."],[878,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Tell me: if there were a river at the door of one of you in which he bathed five times every day, would any dirt remain upon him?” They replied: “No dirt would remain upon him.” He said: “That is the example of the five daily prayers. Through them Allah erases sins.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري واللفظ له (528)، ومسلم (667)."],[879,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of the five daily prayers is like a deep, flowing river at the door of one of you in which he bathes five times every day.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (668)."],[880,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of the believer is like a crop that the wind continually bends. The believer likewise continues to be afflicted by trials. The example of the hypocrite is like a cedar tree that remains rigid until it is cut down all at once.” In another wording: “The example of the believer is like a tender plant. From whichever direction the wind comes, it bends it; and when it straightens, another trial bends it. But the wicked person is like a rigid, upright cedar tree until Allah breaks it whenever He wills.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2809، 58)، والبخاري (5644)."],[881,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of the believer is like a tender plant: the wind bends it at one time and straightens it at another. The example of the hypocrite is like a rigid cedar tree that remains standing until it is uprooted all at once.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5643)، ومسلم (2810، 59)."],[882,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the trees is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is like the Muslim. Tell me which tree it is.” The people began thinking of the trees of the desert. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: “It occurred to me that it was the date palm, but I felt shy to speak.” They then said: “Tell us what it is, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “It is the date palm.” In another narration, he said: “Tell me of a tree whose example is like that of the Muslim: it gives its fruit at all times by the permission of its Lord, and its leaves do not fall.” I thought: “It is the date palm.” But I disliked speaking while Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were present. When neither of them spoke, the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is the date palm.” When I later went out with my father, I said: “My father, it occurred to me that it was the date palm.”\nHe asked: “What prevented you from saying it? Had you said it, that would have been more beloved to me than such-and-such.” I replied: “Nothing prevented me except that neither you nor Abū Bakr spoke, so I disliked speaking ahead of you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (61)، ومسلم (2811)."],[883,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Your example, and that of the Jews and Christians, is like a man who hired workers and said, ‘Who will work for me until midday for one qīrāṭ each?’ The Jews worked for one qīrāṭ each. Then the Christians worked for one qīrāṭ each. Then you are the ones who work from the ʿAṣr prayer until sunset for two qīrāṭs each. The Jews and Christians became angry and said, ‘We did more work but received less.’ He said, ‘Have I wronged you in any part of what was due to you?’ They replied, ‘No.’ He said, ‘Then that is My bounty, which I give to whomever I will.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2269)."],[884,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “My example and the example of the people is like that of a man who kindled a fire. When it illuminated what was around him, moths and other creatures that fall into fire began falling into it. He tried to pull them away, but they overpowered him and plunged into it. I am holding you back by your waistbands from the Fire, while you are rushing headlong into it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6483)، ومسلم (2284، 17)."],[885,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People are like one hundred camels; you can hardly find among them one suitable riding camel.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6498)، ومسلم (2547، 232)."],[886,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of my Ummah is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2869)، وأحمد (12327)، والبزار (6896)."],[887,"ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of my Ummah is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.”","حسن: رواه البزار (1412)، وابن حبان (7226)."],[889,"Al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The example of those who uphold the limits of Allah and those who fall into violating them is like a group of people who drew lots for places on a ship. Some of them received the upper part and others the lower part. Those in the lower part, whenever they needed water, had to pass by those above them. So they said, ‘If only we made a hole in our own section so that we would not disturb those above us.’ If the others leave them to do what they intend, they will all perish. But if they restrain them, they themselves will be saved and all of them will be saved.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2493)."],[890,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand. If he is unable to do so, then with his tongue. If he is unable to do so, then with his heart, and that is the weakest level of faith.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (49). فقال: قد ترك ما هنالك."],[891,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There was no Prophet whom Allah sent to a nation before me except that he had disciples and Companions from among his nation who followed his Sunnah and obeyed his commands. Then generations came after them who said what they did not do and did what they had not been commanded to do. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer; whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer; and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer. Beyond that there is not even a mustard seed’s weight of faith.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (50)."],[892,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥaḍramī narrated: Someone who heard the Prophet ﷺ informed me that he said: “Among my Ummah will be people who are given rewards like those of its earliest generations because they condemn wrongdoing.” In another wording: “At the end of this Ummah there will be people who will have rewards like those of its earliest generations. They will enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and fight the people of tribulation.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (16592)، ويعقوب بن سفيان الفسوي في المعرفة والتاريخ (1/535)."],[893,"Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated: Abū Bakr stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “O people, you recite this verse: ‘O you who believe, take care of yourselves. Those who go astray cannot harm you when you yourselves are guided.’ [Sūrat al-Māʾidah 5:105] Yet we heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When people see wrongdoing and do not change it, Allah may soon encompass them all with His punishment.’”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4338)، والترمذي (2168)، وابن ماجه (4005)، والنسائي في الكبرى (11092)، وأحمد (1)، وصححه ابن حبان (304)."],[894,"Al-ʿUrs ibn ʿUmayrah al-Kindī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When a sin is committed on earth, whoever witnesses it and hates it—or, in another wording, condemns it—is like one who was absent from it. And whoever was absent from it but approves of it is like one who witnessed it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4345)، والطبراني في الكبير (17/139). وإسناده حسن، وقد روي مرسلا عند أبي داود (4346)، والحكم لمن وصل."],[895,"Abū al-Bakhtarī narrated: Someone who heard it directly from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me that he said: “The people will not be destroyed until they leave no excuse for themselves.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4347)، وأحمد (18289)."],[896,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What will your condition be when a time soon comes in which people are sifted thoroughly, leaving only the dregs of mankind, whose covenants and trusts have become confused and corrupted, so that they differ and become like this?” He interlaced his fingers. They asked: “What should we do, O Messenger of Allah, when that happens?” He replied: “Hold to what you know to be right, leave what you recognize as wrong, turn your attention to those closest to you, and leave the affairs of the general masses.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4342)، وابن ماجه (3957)، وأحمد (7063)، وصححه الحاكم (8340). وقال الحاكم: «هذا حديث صحيح الإسناد»، وهو كما قال."],[897,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: While we were gathered around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he mentioned tribulation and said: “When you see that people’s covenants have become confused and corrupted, their trusts have become weak, and they have become like this…” He interlaced his fingers. I stood up and asked: “What should I do at that time? May Allah make me your ransom.” He replied: “Remain in your home, restrain your tongue, hold to what you know to be right, leave what you recognize as wrong, concern yourself with your own private affairs, and leave the affairs of the general public.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4343)، وأحمد (6987)، والحاكم (7758). وإسناده حسن من أجل يونس بن أبي إسحاق وهلال بن خباب، فإنهما حسنا الحديث. وقال الحاكم: «هذا حديث صحيح الإسناد»."],[898,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What will you do, O ʿAbdullāh, when you remain among the dregs of mankind?” He asked: “What will they be like, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “That will be when their trusts and covenants become confused and corrupted, and they become like this.” He interlaced his fingers. He asked: “Then what should I do, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Act upon what you know to be right, leave what you recognize as wrong, concern yourself with your own affairs, and leave the general masses.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان (5950-5951)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (1182-1183)، والطبراني في الأوسط (2797). وإسناده حسن من أجل العلاء بن عبد الرحمن، فإنه حسن الحديث."],[899,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, and I could tell from his face that something serious had occurred. He performed wuḍūʾ without speaking to anyone, then went out. I pressed myself close to the chamber so that I could hear what he was saying. He sat upon the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: “O people, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to you: Enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong before you call upon Me and I do not answer you, before you ask Me and I do not give you, and before you seek My help and I do not help you.” He added nothing beyond these words before descending.","حسن: رواه أحمد (25255)، وابن حبان (290)، وابن ماجه (4004)، والسياق لابن حبان. وسياق أحمد قريب منه، وعند ابن ماجه باختصار. وعاصم بن عمر بن عثمان لم يرو عنه إلا عمرو بن عثمان بن هانئ، ولذا قال المزي: «مجهول». وله طريق آخر رواه البخاري في التاريخ الكبير (6/178)، وبالإسنادين يصير الحديث حسنا."],[900,"Abū Saʿīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Fear of people should not prevent any one of you from speaking the truth when he knows it.” Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī then said: “Trials continued to afflict us until we fell short, and indeed we reached a serious degree of wrongdoing.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (11869)، وصححه ابن حبان (278). وعلي بن زيد ضعيف، لكنه توبع على الفقرة المذكورة."],[901,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah will question a servant on the Day of Resurrection until He says, ‘What prevented you, when you saw wrongdoing, from condemning it?’ Then, if Allah grants a servant his excuse, he will say, ‘My Lord, I hoped in You, but I feared the people.’”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (4017)، وأحمد (11735)، وصححه ابن حبان (7368). وإسناده حسن من أجل نهار العبدي، فإنه حسن الحديث."],[904,"Usāmah ibn Zayd was asked: “Will you not go to ʿUthmān and speak to him?” He replied: “Do you think I do not speak to him merely because I do not let you hear it? By Allah, I have spoken to him privately between myself and him, without opening a door that I would hate to be the first to open. Nor will I say of anyone who rules over me that he is the best of people, after I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ʿA man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and thrown into the Fire. His intestines will spill out, and he will circle around them as a donkey circles around a millstone. The people of the Fire will gather around him and say, “So-and-so, what happened to you? Did you not command what was right and forbid what was wrong?” He will reply, “Yes. I used to command what was right but did not do it myself, and I used to forbid what was wrong while committing it myself.”’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7098)، ومسلم (2989)."],[905,"Jundub ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Azdī, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of a scholar who teaches people goodness but forgets himself is like a lamp that gives light to people while burning itself.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (1681). وفي إسناده علي بن سليمان الكلبي، وهو غير معروف. وذكر الهيثمي أن رجاله موثقون اعتمادا على توثيق ابن حبان، ثم قال في موضع آخر: «علي بن سليمان الكلبي لم أعرفه». ويقويه ما روي موقوفا عن جندب عند أحمد في الزهد (1127) وأبي داود في الزهد (392)، وبهذين الإسنادين يرتقي الحديث إلى درجة الحسن، وقد حسنه المنذري في الترغيب والترهيب (220)."],[906,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Make things easy and do not make them difficult. Calm people and do not drive them away.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6125)، ومسلم (1734)."],[907,"Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah narrated from his father, from his grandfather: The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Muʿādh to Yemen and said: “Make things easy and do not make them difficult. Give glad tidings and do not drive people away. Cooperate with one another and do not differ.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3038)، ومسلم (1733)."],[908,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of the two, so long as it was not sinful. If it involved sin, he was the person farthest from it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never took revenge for himself concerning anything, unless one of the sacred limits of Allah was violated; then he would act for the sake of Allah.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (2)، والبخاري (6126)، ومسلم (2327، 77)."],[909,"Al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated: We were on the bank of a river at al-Ahwāz from which the water had receded. Abū Barzah al-Aslamī came riding a horse, began praying, and let go of the horse. The horse wandered away, so he left his prayer and followed it until he caught it. Then he returned and completed his prayer. Among us was a man who held a particular opinion, and he began saying: “Look at this old man! He left his prayer because of a horse!” Abū Barzah approached and said: “No one has rebuked me in this manner since I parted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He explained: “My home is far away. If I had continued praying and allowed the horse to go, I would not have reached my family until night.” He also mentioned that he had accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and had witnessed his practice of making matters easy.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6127)."],[910,"Al-Azraq ibn Qays narrated: We were at al-Ahwāz fighting the Ḥarūriyyah. While I was on the bank of a river, I saw a man praying while holding the reins of his riding animal. The animal began pulling against him, and he followed it. A man from the Khawārij began saying: “O Allah, deal with this old man!” When the old man finished, he said: “I heard what you said. I took part in six—or seven—and eight military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I witnessed how he made matters easy. I would rather interrupt and go after my animal than let it return to the place it is accustomed to and cause me hardship.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (1211)."],[911,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and the people rushed toward him to confront him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave him, and pour a bucket of water—or a large pail of water—over his urine. You were sent to make things easy; you were not sent to make things difficult.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6128)."],[912,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “Which deeds are best?” He replied: “To bring happiness to your believing Muslim brother, to pay off a debt for him, or to feed him bread.”","حسن: رواه ابن أبي الدنيا في قضاء الحوائج (112)."],[913,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came out to a group of his Companions who were laughing and talking. He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.” He then left, and the people began to weep. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to him: “O Muḥammad, why did you cause My servants to despair?” The Prophet ﷺ returned and said: “Receive glad tidings, remain on the correct course, and strive to come close to perfection.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (254)، وابن حبان (113)، والبيهقي في الشعب (1027)."],[916,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the religion is ease. No one makes the religion excessively difficult for himself except that it will overwhelm him. So remain on the correct course, come as close as you can, receive glad tidings, and seek strength through worship in the morning, the evening, and part of the night.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (39)."],[917,"Naṣr ibn ʿĀṣim al-Laythī narrated from a man of his people: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam on the condition that he would pray only two prayers, and the Prophet ﷺ accepted that from him.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (20287، 23079)، وابن أبي شيبة في مسنده (995)."],[918,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted something, but some people refrained from it out of excessive caution. When this reached the Prophet ﷺ, he became angry until the anger was visible on his face. Then he said: “What is the matter with people who turn away from something that has been permitted to me? By Allah, I know Allah better than they do, and I fear Him more intensely than they do.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6101)، ومسلم (2356، 128)."],[919,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then said: “If only we remained seated until we could pray ʿIshāʾ with him.” So we remained seated. He came out to us and asked: “Are you still here?” We replied: “O Messenger of Allah, we prayed Maghrib with you, then said that we would remain until we could pray ʿIshāʾ with you.” He said: “You have done well,” or, “You have done correctly.” Then he raised his head toward the sky, and he would often raise his head toward the sky, and said: “The stars are a safeguard for the sky. When the stars disappear, what the sky has been promised will come upon it. I am a safeguard for my Companions. When I am gone, what my Companions have been promised will come upon them. And my Companions are a safeguard for my Ummah. When my Companions are gone, what my Ummah has been promised will come upon it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2531)."],[920,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām narrated: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat and spoke, he would frequently raise his gaze toward the sky.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4837)، والباغندي في مسند عمر بن عبد العزيز (4)."],[921,"Zayd ibn Arqam narrated: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and delivered a sermon at a body of water called Khumm, between Makkah and Madinah. He praised Allah and extolled Him, admonished the people, and reminded them. Then he said: “To proceed: O people…” to the end of the hadith.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2408)."],[922,"ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim al-Ṭāʾī narrated: A man delivered a sermon in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been rightly guided, and whoever disobeys them both has gone astray.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What a poor preacher you are! Say instead: ‘Whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (870)."],[923,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not leave fire burning in your homes when you go to sleep.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6293)، ومسلم (2015)."],[924,"Abū Mūsā narrated: A house in Madinah burned down upon its occupants during the night. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed about what had happened, he said: “This fire is indeed an enemy to you. So when you go to sleep, extinguish it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6294)، ومسلم (2016)."],[925,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cover your vessels, close your doors, and extinguish your lamps, for the mouse may drag away the wick and cause the people of the house to burn.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6295)، ومسلم (2012)."],[926,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Close the door, tie the mouth of the waterskin, turn the vessel over—or cover the vessel—and extinguish the lamp. Satan does not open a closed door, untie a tied waterskin, or uncover a covered vessel. And the mouse may set the people’s house on fire.”","صحيح: رواه مالك (21)، ومسلم (2012، 96)."],[927,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When night begins—or when evening comes—keep your children indoors, for the devils spread out at that time. When an hour of the night has passed, then let them go. Close the doors and mention the Name of Allah, for Satan does not open a closed door. Tie your waterskins and mention the Name of Allah. Cover your vessels and mention the Name of Allah, even if you can only place something across them, and extinguish your lamps.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5623)، ومسلم (2012، 97)."],[928,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cover the vessel, tie the waterskin, close the door, and extinguish the lamp. Satan does not untie a waterskin, open a door, or uncover a vessel. If one of you finds nothing except a stick to place across his vessel while mentioning the Name of Allah, then let him do so, for the mouse may set the household’s home on fire.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2012، 96)."],[929,"Jābir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Cover your vessels and tie your waterskins, for during the year there is a night in which a plague descends. It does not pass by an uncovered vessel or an untied waterskin except that some of that plague descends into it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2014)."],[930,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not let your livestock or your children go out once the sun has set until the darkness of ʿIshāʾ has passed, for the devils spread out when the sun sets and remain so until the darkness of ʿIshāʾ has passed.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2013، 98)."],[931,"Abū Barzah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked sleeping before the ʿIshāʾ prayer and talking afterward.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (568)، ومسلم (647، 237)."],[932,"ʿUrwah narrated: ʿĀ’ishah heard me talking after the final ʿIshāʾ prayer and said: “O ʿUrayy, will you not give your scribe some rest? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not sleep before it, nor would he remain talking after it.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (5547)."],[933,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never slept before ʿIshāʾ, nor did he stay up conversing after it.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (702)، وأحمد (26280)، وأبو يعلى (4784)."],[934,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rebuked us for staying up talking after ʿIshāʾ.”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (703)، وأحمد (3686)، وابن خزيمة (1340)، وابن حبان (2031)، والطحاوي في شرح المعاني (4/330). وعطاء بن السائب ثقة إلا أنه اختلط في آخره، وقد رواه عنه عند الطحاوي حماد بن سلمة ممن سمع منه قبل الاختلاط، فإسناده صحيح."],[935,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There should be no staying up at night except for one engaged in prayer or a traveler.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (10/268)."],[936,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray in the middle of the bed while I was lying between him and the qiblah. Sometimes I would need to get up, but I disliked standing and passing directly in front of him, so I would quietly slip away.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6276)، ومسلم (512، 270)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[937,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One bed is for the man, one bed is for his wife, the third is for the guest, and the fourth is for Satan.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2084)."],[938,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “None of you should lie on his back and then place one leg over the other.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2099، 74)."],[939,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from lying on his back while placing one leg over the other.","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (5554)."],[940,"ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm narrated from his paternal uncle: He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lying on his back in the mosque with one leg placed over the other. Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib said: “ʿUmar and ʿUthmān used to do the same.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (93، 94)، والبخاري (475)، ومسلم (2100، 75)."],[941,"Abū Umāmah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man sleeping in the mosque while lying face down. He nudged him with his foot and said: “Get up and sit, for this is a manner of sleeping associated with Hell.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3725)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1188)."],[942,"Al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited cutting dates from the palms at night and harvesting crops at night.","حسن: رواه ابن الأعرابي في معجمه (1997)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (105)."],[943,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “I used to play with dolls in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and I had female companions who would play with me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, they would hide from him, but he would send them back to me so that they could continue playing with me.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6130)، ومسلم (2440)."],[944,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians were playing with their spears in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He screened me with his cloak so that I could watch their performance. He continued standing there for my sake until I was the one who chose to leave. So take into account the nature of a young girl who is eager for amusement.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5236)، ومسلم (892، 18)."],[945,"Anas narrated: The Abyssinians were performing rhythmic movements before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, dancing and saying: “Muḥammad is a righteous servant.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What are they saying?” They replied: “They are saying: ‘Muḥammad is a righteous servant.’”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (12540)، وابن حبان (5870)."],[946,"Al-Sā’ib ibn Yazīd narrated: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “O ʿĀ’ishah, do you know this woman?” She replied: “No, O Prophet of Allah.” He said: “She is the singing girl of such-and-such a clan. Would you like her to sing for you?” She replied: “Yes.” He then gave the woman a tray, and she sang for ʿĀ’ishah. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Satan has blown into her nostrils.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (15720)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8911)."],[947,"Nāfiʿ narrated: Ibn ʿUmar heard the sound of a wind instrument, so he placed his fingers over his ears, moved away from the road, and asked me: “O Nāfiʿ, can you still hear anything?” I replied: “No.” He then removed his fingers from his ears and said: “I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he heard something like this, and he did the same.” In Aḥmad’s narration: “He heard the sound of a shepherd’s flute and did the same.” Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī said: “I heard Abū Dāwūd say: ‘This is a rejected hadith.’”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4924)، وأحمد (4535)، وصححه ابن حبان (693)."],[948,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a dog or a bell.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2113)."],[949,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The bell is one of the musical instruments of Satan.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2114)."],[950,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that the bells be cut from the necks of the camels on the Day of Badr.","صحيح: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8758)، وأحمد (25166)، وابن حبان (4699، 4702)."],[951,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever plays nardashīr, it is as though he has dipped his hand into the flesh and blood of a pig.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2260)."],[952,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal narrated: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited throwing small stones with the fingers and said: “It does not kill game, nor does it wound the enemy. Rather, it may put out an eye and break a tooth.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6220)، ومسلم (1954، 55)."],[954,"Jābir narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Then revelation ceased for a period. While I was walking, I heard a voice from the sky, so I raised my gaze toward the sky. There was the angel who had come to me at Ḥirāʾ, seated upon a chair between the sky and the earth.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6214)، ومسلم (161، 255)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[955,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: I spent the night in the house of Maymūnah while the Prophet ﷺ was with her. When the final third of the night—or part of it—came, he sat up, looked toward the sky, and recited: “Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and day are signs for people of understanding.” [Sūrat Āl ʿImrān 3:190]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6215)، ومسلم (763، 19)."],[956,"Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated: We were with Abū Qatādah on the roof of our house when a star shot across the sky. The people looked toward it. Abū Qatādah said: “We were prohibited from following it with our eyes.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (22549) - والسياق له -، وعبد الرزاق في مصنفه (20007)."],[957,"Abū Mūsā narrated: He was with the Prophet ﷺ in one of the gardens of Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ had a stick in his hand with which he was poking at the water and mud. A man came and asked permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.” I went and found that it was Abū Bakr, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another man asked permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise.” I went and found that it was ʿUmar, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another man asked permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ had been reclining, but he sat up and said: “Open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise despite a trial that will afflict him.” I went and found that it was ʿUthmān. I opened for him, gave him glad tidings of Paradise, and informed him of what the Prophet ﷺ had said. ʿUthmān said: “Allah is the One whose help is sought.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2616)، ومسلم (2403، 28)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[958,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: We were with the Prophet ﷺ at a funeral, and he began poking the ground with a stick. He said: “There is no one among you except that his place in Paradise or the Fire has already been determined.” They asked: “Then should we not simply rely upon that?” He replied: “Act, for everyone will be facilitated.” Then he recited: “As for the one who gives and has taqwā…” [Sūrat al-Layl 92:5]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6217)، ومسلم (2647، 7)."],[959,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Faith consists of seventy-some—or sixty-some—branches. The best of them is the statement, ‘There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah,’ and the lowest of them is removing something harmful from the road. And modesty is a branch of faith.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (35، 58) واللفظ له، والبخاري (9)."],[960,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Removing something harmful from the road is charity.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2989)، ومسلم (1009)."],[961,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While a man was walking along a road, he found a thorny branch lying in the path and removed it. Allah appreciated that deed from him and forgave him.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (6)، والبخاري (2472)، ومسلم (1914، 127) عقب الحديث (2617)."],[962,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man passed by a tree branch lying across a road and said, ‘By Allah, I will remove this from the Muslims so that it does not harm them.’ Because of that, he was admitted into Paradise.” In another narration: “I saw a man enjoying himself in Paradise because of a tree he had removed from the road because it was harming people.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1914، 128) عقب الحديث (2617)."],[963,"Abū Shaybah narrated: Muʿādh was walking with another man when he removed a stone from the road. The man asked: “Why did you do that?” Muʿādh replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever removes a stone from the road has a good deed recorded for him, and whoever has a good deed recorded for him will enter Paradise.”","حسن: رواه البيهقي في شعب الإيمان (10660)، والطبراني في الكبير (20/ح 198)."],[964,"Abū Barzah narrated: I said: “O Prophet of Allah, teach me something from which I may benefit.” He said: “Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2618)."],[965,"Abū Barzah al-Aslamī narrated: Abū Barzah said: I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, I do not know; perhaps you will pass away while I remain after you. So provide me with some advice through which Allah may benefit me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do such-and-such, do such-and-such” —Abū Bakr forgot those instructions— “and remove harmful things from the road.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2618)."],[966,"Abū Dharr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The deeds of my Ummah, both good and bad, were shown to me. Among their good deeds I found the removal of harmful things from the road, and among their bad deeds I found phlegm left in the mosque without being buried.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (553)."],[967,"Buraydah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A human being has three hundred and sixty joints, and he must give an act of charity for each joint.” They asked: “Who is capable of doing that, O Prophet of Allah?” He replied: “Bury phlegm found in the mosque and remove something harmful from the road. If you cannot find anything else, then two rakʿahs of Duḥā prayer will suffice for you.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5242)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (1226)، وابن حبان (1642، 2540)."],[968,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of the two acts that bring curses.” They asked: “What are the two acts that bring curses, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Relieving oneself in the road used by people or in the places where they seek shade.”","صحيح: أخرجه مسلم (269)."],[969,"Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever harms the Muslims on their roads deserves their curse.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (3050)."],[970,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Keep your courtyards clean, for the Jews do not keep their courtyards clean.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (519)."],[971,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Beware of sitting in the roads.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we cannot do without our gathering places where we sit and talk.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you insist on sitting there, then give the road its rights.” They asked: “What are its rights?” He replied: “Lowering the gaze, refraining from causing harm, returning the greeting of salām, enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is wrong.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6229)، ومسلم (2121) عقب الحديث (2161)."],[972,"Abū Ṭalḥah narrated: We were sitting in the courtyards talking when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and stood over us. He said: “Why are you sitting in the gathering places along the roads? Avoid gathering along the roads.” We replied: “We are only sitting here for something harmless. We sit to remind one another and converse.” He said: “If you must do so, then fulfill their rights: lower the gaze, return the greeting of salām, and speak good words.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2161)."],[973,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sitting in the open areas along the roads. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are unable to avoid that.” He said: “If you must, then give those places their rights.” They asked: “What are their rights, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “Returning greetings, saying ‘May Allah have mercy on you’ to one who sneezes if he praises Allah, lowering the gaze, and directing people to the way.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4816)، وصححه ابن حبان (596)، والحاكم (7688)."],[974,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: While the Prophet ﷺ was performing ṭawāf around the Kaʿbah, he passed by a man whose hand had been tied to another man with a leather strap—or a thread, or something similar. The Prophet ﷺ cut it with his own hand and then said: “Lead him by his hand.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (1620)."],[975,"Anas narrated: “When the Prophet ﷺ walked, it was as though he were leaning forward.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4863)، والترمذي (1754)."],[976,"Abū al-Ṭufayl said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He was asked: “What was he like when you saw him?” He replied: “He was fair and handsome. When he walked, it was as though he were descending a slope.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4864)، وابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (2/242)."],[977,"ʿUqbah ibn al-Ḥārith narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ prayed ʿAṣr, then hurried and entered the house.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6275)."],[978,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: When the Prophet ﷺ passed by al-Ḥijr, he said: “Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves, lest what afflicted them should afflict you, unless you enter while weeping.” Then he covered his head and hastened his pace until he had passed through the valley.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4419)، ومسلم (2980، 39)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[979,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the people of al-Ḥijr: “Do not enter upon these people who were punished unless you are weeping. If you are not weeping, then do not enter upon them, lest something like what afflicted them should afflict you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4702)، ومسلم (2980، 38)."],[980,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: The people stopped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥijr—the land of Thamūd—and drew water from its wells and kneaded dough with it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to pour away the water they had drawn, feed the dough to the camels, and draw their water instead from the well from which the she-camel of Thamūd used to drink. Another narration adds: “They drew water from its wells and kneaded dough with it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3379)، ومسلم (2981)."],[981,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you travel during a time of abundant vegetation, give the camels their share of the land. When you travel during a time of drought, hasten your journey upon them. And when you stop to rest at night, avoid camping directly on the road, for it is a shelter for harmful creatures at night.” In another wording: “For the roads are the pathways of animals and the shelter of harmful creatures at night.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1926)."],[982,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the land is fertile, give your riding animals their share of the pasture. When the land is barren, hasten them onward while they still have their strength, traveling during the night. And you should travel during the night, for the earth is folded up at night.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي في العلل الكبير (2/874) - واللفظ له -، وابن خزيمة (2555)، والحاكم (1/445)."],[983,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: Some people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the difficulty of walking. He called them and said: “You should practice al-nasalān.” So we quickened our walking pace and found it easier upon us.","صحيح: رواه إسحاق بن راهويه (2010 - المطالب)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2537)، والحاكم (1619)."],[984,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Travel is a portion of torment. It prevents one of you from his sleep, food, and drink. So when one of you has fulfilled the purpose for which he traveled, let him hasten back to his family.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (39)، والبخاري (1804)، ومسلم (1927)."],[985,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would travel alone at night.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2998)."],[986,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited a person from being alone: that a man should spend the night alone or travel alone.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (5650)."],[987,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: A man set out on a journey, and two men followed him. Another man followed behind them, calling out: “Go back!” So the two men turned back. He then said to the traveler: “Those two were devils, and I continued confronting them until I made them turn back. When you reach the Prophet ﷺ, convey my salām to him and inform him that we are busy collecting our zakāh. If it were suitable to send it to him, we would have sent it to him.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: Following this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited being alone.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (2719)، والبزار (كشف الأستار - 2022)، وأبو يعلى (2588)، والحاكم (2494)."],[988,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A lone rider is a devil, two riders are two devils, and three are a traveling group.”","حسن: رواه مالك (36)، وأبو داود (2607)، والترمذي (1674)."],[989,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī—or Abū Hurayrah—narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When three people set out on a journey, let them appoint one of them as their leader.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (2608، 2609)."],[990,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would remain toward the rear of the traveling group. He would urge along the weak, give rides to those in need, and supplicate for them.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (2639)، والحاكم (2541)، وعنه البيهقي (10352)."],[991,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik used to say: “Rarely would the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on a journey except on a Thursday.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2949)."],[992,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ set out on a Thursday for the expedition of Tabūk, and he liked to depart on Thursdays.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2950)."],[993,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited traveling with the Qur’an into enemy territory. Another narration adds: “Out of fear that the enemy might get hold of it.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (7)، والبخاري (2990)، ومسلم (1869، 92)."],[994,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Prophet ﷺ had a camel-driver named Anjashah who had a beautiful voice. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Gently, O Anjashah. Do not break the glass vessels.” Qatādah said: “He meant the women, because of their delicateness.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6011)، ومسلم (2323، 73)."],[995,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Hishām narrated: “We were with the Prophet ﷺ while he was holding the hand of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6264)."],[996,"Anas narrated: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr while traveling, he would walk for a short distance while his she-camel was led beside him.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط - مجمع البحرين (1672)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (10338)."],[997,"Qurrah ibn Iyās narrated: A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, even when I slaughter a sheep, I feel compassion for it,” or he said: “I feel compassion for the sheep when I slaughter it.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Even if it is only a sheep, if you show mercy to it, Allah will show mercy to you. Even if it is only a sheep, if you show mercy to it, Allah will show mercy to you.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (15592)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (373)، والبزار (3319)."],[998,"Sawādah ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him for assistance, so he ordered that several camels be given to me. Then he said: “When you return home, instruct them to feed their young camels well. Tell them to trim their fingernails, and not to wound the udders of their livestock with their nails when milking them.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (15961)."],[999,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A dog was circling around a well, nearly dying of thirst, when a prostitute from among the Children of Israel saw it. She removed her leather boot, drew water for the dog with it, and gave it water to drink. Because of that, she was forgiven.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3467)، ومسلم (2245)."],[1000,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While a man was walking along a road, he became extremely thirsty. He found a well, climbed down into it, drank, and came back out. He then saw a dog panting and eating moist earth because of its severe thirst. The man said, ‘This dog has reached the same degree of thirst that I had reached.’ So he climbed back down into the well, filled his leather boot with water, held it in his mouth until he climbed back up, and gave the dog water to drink. Allah appreciated his deed and forgave him.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, is there a reward for us even in serving animals?” He replied: “There is a reward for serving every living creature with a moist liver.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (23)، والبخاري (2363)، ومسلم (2244)."],[1001,"ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from his grandfather: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I draw water into my trough until I fill it for my family, then a camel belonging to someone else comes to me and I give it water. Is there a reward for me in that?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “There is a reward for serving every living creature suffering from thirst.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (7075)."],[1002,"Surāqah ibn Juʿshum narrated: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about stray camels that come to my water troughs, which I had prepared for my own camels: “Will I receive a reward if I give them water?” He replied: “Yes. There is a reward for serving every living creature suffering from thirst.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3686)، وأحمد (17581)."],[1003,"Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ narrated that Surāqah ibn Juʿshum said: “O Messenger of Allah, a stray animal comes to my water trough. Is there a reward for me if I give it water?” He replied: “Give it water, for there is a reward in every living creature suffering from severe thirst.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (542)."],[1004,"Sahl ibn al-Ḥanẓaliyyah al-Anṣārī, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for a need and passed by a camel kneeling at the door of the mosque early in the day. Later in the day, he passed by it again and found it still in the same condition. He asked: “Where is the owner of this camel?” They searched for him but could not find him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fear Allah concerning these animals. Ride them while they are healthy, and eat them while they are well-fed…” In another wording: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a camel whose back had become so emaciated that it appeared to meet its belly. He said: “Fear Allah concerning these speechless animals, and ride them while they are in a sound condition.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (17625)، وصححه ابن حبان (545، 3394). ورواه أبو داود (2548)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2545) باللفظ الثاني، وإسناده حسن."],[1005,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated me behind him on his mount and confided something to me that I will never disclose to anyone. The thing behind which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most liked to conceal himself when relieving himself was either a raised mound of earth or a grove of date palms. He entered a garden belonging to a man from the Anṣār, and there was a camel there. When the camel saw the Prophet ﷺ, it groaned and its eyes filled with tears. The Prophet ﷺ approached it and stroked the area behind its ears, and it became quiet. Then he asked: “Who is the owner of this camel? To whom does this camel belong?” A young man from the Anṣār came and said: “It belongs to me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Will you not fear Allah concerning this animal which Allah has placed in your possession? It has complained to me that you keep it hungry and overwork it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2549)، وأحمد (1745)، والحاكم (2485)."],[1006,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you were forgiven for what you do to animals, much would indeed be forgiven for you.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (27486)، والبيهقي في الشعب (5188)."],[1007,"Anas narrated: “Whenever we stopped at a place during a journey, we would not perform voluntary prayer until the loads had first been removed from the animals.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (2551)."],[1008,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Beware of taking the backs of your riding animals as pulpits. Allah has only subjected them to you so that they may carry you to lands you could not otherwise reach except with great hardship. And He has made the earth for you, so fulfill your needs upon it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (2567)، ومن طريقه البيهقي (10335)."],[1009,"Muʿādh ibn Anas, who was a Companion, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ride these animals while they are healthy, and leave them while they are healthy. Do not use them as chairs.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (15639، 15641)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (2544)، وابن حبان (5619)."],[1010,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated: Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, the children of his household would go out to meet him. On one occasion when he returned from a journey, I was the first to reach him. He placed me in front of him on his mount. Then one of the two sons of Fāṭimah—either al-Ḥasan or al-Ḥusayn—was brought, and the Prophet ﷺ seated him behind himself. Thus we entered Madinah with three people riding on a single animal.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2428، 66)."],[1011,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: “Riding al-jallālah was prohibited.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2557)، ومن طريقه البيهقي (10330)."],[1012,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated: While the Prophet ﷺ was walking, a man came to him with a donkey and said: “O Messenger of Allah, ride.” The man then moved backward to give him the front position. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have more right to the front of your own animal unless you give that place to me.” The man replied: “I have given it to you.” So the Prophet ﷺ mounted.","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2773)، وأبو داود (2572)، وأحمد (22992)، وصححه ابن حبان (4735)."],[1013,"ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the owner of an animal has the greatest right to its front seat.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (119)."],[1014,"Ḥabīb ibn Maslamah came to Qays ibn Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah during the first fitnah while Qays was riding a horse. Qays moved backward from the front of the saddle and said: “Ride.” Ḥabīb refused. Qays ibn Saʿd said to him: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The owner of an animal has the greatest right to its front seat.’” Ḥabīb replied: “I am not unaware of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, but I am concerned for your safety.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (15478)، والطبراني في الكبير (4/25)، وفي الأوسط (1948)."],[1015,"ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn narrated: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, a woman from the Anṣār was riding a she-camel. The camel annoyed her, so she cursed it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard this and said: “Take whatever is loaded upon it and leave it, for it has been cursed.” ʿImrān said: “It is as though I can still see that she-camel now, walking among the people while no one approached it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2595)."],[1016,"Abū Barzah al-Aslamī narrated: A young woman was riding a she-camel that was carrying some of the people’s belongings. She saw the Prophet ﷺ while the mountain path had become narrow for the group, so she said to the camel: “Ḥal! O Allah, curse it.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “A she-camel that has been cursed must not accompany us.” In another wording: “No, by Allah, a riding animal upon which the curse of Allah has been invoked must not accompany us.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2596)."],[1017,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Baṭn Buwāṭ while he was seeking al-Majdī ibn ʿAmr al-Juhanī. Five, six, or seven of us would take turns riding a single water-carrying camel. When the turn of a man from the Anṣār came, he made his camel kneel, mounted it, and urged it forward. The camel hesitated somewhat, so he said: “Move! May Allah curse you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who is this cursing his camel?” The man replied: “It is I, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Get down from it, for a cursed animal must not accompany us. Do not supplicate against yourselves, do not supplicate against your children, and do not supplicate against your wealth, lest you coincide with an hour in which Allah is asked for something and He responds to you.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (3009)."],[1018,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was traveling on a journey when a man cursed a she-camel. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Where is the owner of the she-camel?” The man replied: “I am.” He said: “Move it to the rear, for your supplication concerning it has been answered.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (9522) والسياق له، والنسائي في الكبرى (8764)."],[1019,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that she was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey and cursed one of her camels. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that it be sent back and said: “Nothing that has been cursed is to accompany me.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (24434)."],[1020,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A man was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ and cursed his camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O servant of Allah, do not travel with us on a cursed camel.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (3622)، وابن أبي الدنيا في الصمت (387)، والطبراني في الدعاء (2088)."],[1021,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman entered the Fire because of a cat that belonged to her. She tied it up, neither feeding it nor releasing it to eat from the small creatures of the earth, until it died from emaciation.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2619)، والبخاري (3318)."],[1022,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman was punished because of a cat that she confined until it died, and because of it she entered the Fire. She neither fed it nor gave it water while she kept it confined, nor did she release it so that it could eat from the creatures of the earth.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3482)، ومسلم (2242، 151)."],[1023,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “An ant bit one of the Prophets, so he ordered the entire colony of ants to be burned. Allah then revealed to him: ‘Because one ant bit you, you burned an entire nation among the nations that glorify Allah?’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3019)، ومسلم (2241، 151)."],[1024,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One of the Prophets stopped beneath a tree, and an ant bit him. He ordered that his belongings be removed from beneath it, then ordered the ant colony to be burned with fire. Allah revealed to him: ‘Why not only the one ant?’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3319)، ومسلم (2241، 149)."],[1025,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited killing four creatures: the ant, the bee, the hoopoe, and the ṣurad bird.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5267)، وابن ماجه (3224)، وأحمد (3066)."],[1026,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.” He would prohibit killing them and prohibit burning food. Sufyān said: “It appears that the reference to burning food concerns food in enemy territory.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (13436)، وفي الأوسط (1575)."],[1027,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (11058)."],[1028,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān narrated: A physician asked the Prophet ﷺ about using a frog in medicine, so the Prophet ﷺ prohibited him from killing it.","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3871)، والنسائي (4355)، وأحمد (15757)، والحاكم (4/410-411)."],[1029,"Abū Zuhayr al-Numayrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill frogs, for their croaking is glorification of Allah, and do not kill bats; for when Bayt al-Maqdis was destroyed, the bat said: ‘My Lord, give me power over the sea so that I may drown them.’” In a shorter wording: “Do not kill frogs, for they are among the soldiers of Allah, the Exalted.”","حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (1440)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/297)، وفي الأوسط (9277)."],[1030,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Five harmful creatures may be killed even within the Sacred Precinct: the mouse, the scorpion, the crow, the kite, and the vicious dog.” In another narration, “the snake” appears in place of “the scorpion.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3314)، ومسلم (1198، 69)."],[1031,"ʿĀ’ishah said: “I am truly amazed at whoever eats crow, for the Prophet ﷺ permitted its killing and called it a fāsiq. By Allah, it is not among the wholesome things.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (1214)، والبيهقي (19369)."],[1032,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The snake is a harmful creature, the scorpion is a harmful creature, the mouse is a harmful creature, and the crow is a harmful creature.” Al-Qāsim was asked: “May crow be eaten?” He replied: “Who would eat it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it a fāsiq?”","صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (3249)."],[1033,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ called the gecko: “The little harmful creature.” She said: “I did not personally hear him command that it be killed, but Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ stated that the Prophet ﷺ did command its killing.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3306)، ومسلم (2239)، والسياق للبخاري."],[1034,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated: The Prophet ﷺ ordered that geckos be killed and called the gecko: “a little harmful creature.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2238)."],[1035,"Umm Sharīk narrated: The Prophet ﷺ ordered her to kill geckos. Another narration adds that he said: “It used to blow upon Ibrāhīm, peace be upon him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3307)، ومسلم (2237، 142)."],[1036,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills a gecko with the first strike will receive such-and-such a number of good deeds. Whoever kills it with the second strike will receive such-and-such a number of good deeds, fewer than the first. And whoever kills it with the third strike will receive such-and-such a number of good deeds, fewer than the second.” In another wording: “Whoever kills a gecko with the first strike will have one hundred good deeds recorded for him; for the second, less than that; and for the third, less than that.” And in another wording: “For the first strike, seventy good deeds.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2240)."],[1037,"Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī narrated: A man cursed a rooster that crowed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse it, for it calls people to prayer.” In another narration: “For it awakens people for prayer.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5101)، وعبد الرزاق (20498)، وعنه أحمد (17034)."],[1038,"Jābir narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited striking the face and branding the face.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2116)."],[1039,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Prophet ﷺ prohibited striking the face.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5541)."],[1040,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a donkey that had been branded on its face and said: “May Allah curse the one who branded it.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2117، 107)."],[1041,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who brands an animal on the face.","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (11926)."],[1042,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: Al-ʿAbbās was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ on a camel whose face he had branded with fire. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What is this brand, O ʿAbbās?” He replied: “It is a brand that we used in the pre-Islamic period.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not brand with burning.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني (11928)."],[1043,"Anas narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey that had been branded on its face and said: “May Allah curse whoever did this.”","حسن: رواه البزار (7342)، والطبراني في الأوسط (4304)."],[1044,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a brother of mine so that he could perform taḥnīk for him. The Prophet ﷺ was in an enclosure belonging to him, and I saw him branding sheep—I think he said—on their ears.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5542)، ومسلم (2119، 110)."],[1045,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a donkey that had been branded on its face and objected to it. A man said: “By Allah, I will only brand it at the part farthest from the face.” He then ordered that one of his donkeys be branded on the two fleshy areas beside the base of its tail. Thus, he was the first to brand in that location.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2118)."],[1046,"Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh narrated: A camel that had been branded on its face passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “If only the owners of this camel had kept the fire away from this animal’s face.” Ṭalḥah said: “I then said, ‘I will certainly brand only at the place farthest from its face.’” So I branded it at the coccyx, near the base of the tail.","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (651)، ومن طريقه الضياء في المختارة (838)."],[1047,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a servant who was commanded. He did not single us out over the rest of the people with anything except three matters: he commanded us to perform wuḍūʾ thoroughly, not to consume charity, and not to breed a donkey with a mare.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (1701)، وأبو داود (808) مطولا، والنسائي (141، 3581)، وابن ماجه (426)."],[1048,"ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: A mule was presented as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he rode it. ʿAlī said: “If only we bred donkeys with horses, then we too could have animals like this.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Only those who do not know do that.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2565)، والنسائي (3580)، وأحمد (785)، وصححه ابن حبان (4682)."],[1049,"Abū Bashīr al-Anṣārī narrated: He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a messenger. ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr said: “I think he said this while the people were resting at midday.” The messenger was instructed to announce: “No necklace made from a bowstring—or any such necklace—is to remain around the neck of a camel except that it must be cut off.” Yaḥyā said: “I heard Mālik say: ‘I think this was because of the evil eye.’”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (41)، والبخاري (3005)، ومسلم (2115، 105)."],[1050,"Ubayy ibn ʿAbbās ibn Sahl narrated from his father, from his grandfather: “The Prophet ﷺ had a horse in our garden called al-Luḥayf.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (2855)."],[1051,"Muʿādh ibn Jabal narrated: “I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on a donkey called ʿUfayr.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2856)، ومسلم (30، 49)."],[1052,"Anas narrated: There was a sudden alarm in Madinah, so the Prophet ﷺ borrowed a horse belonging to us called Mandūb. He later said: “We found nothing to be afraid of, and indeed we found the horse to be like a sea.” That is, extremely fast and smooth in its running.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2857)، ومسلم (2307، 49)."],[1053,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to kill dogs, to the extent that a woman would come from the desert with her dog and we would kill it. Then the Prophet ﷺ prohibited killing them and said: “You should kill the completely black dog with two spots, for it is a devil.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1572)."],[1054,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have ordered that they all be killed. So kill from among them the completely black dog.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2845)، والترمذي (1486)، والنسائي (4280)، وابن ماجه (3205)، وأحمد (6788)."],[1055,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that dogs be killed.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (14)، والبخاري (3323)، ومسلم (1570، 43)."],[1056,"Abū Rāfiʿ narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to kill dogs, so I went out killing them, and I did not see a dog except that I killed it. Then I came upon a dog circling around a house, and I went to kill it. Someone called out to me from inside the house: “O servant of Allah, what do you intend to do?” I replied: “I intend to kill this dog.” A woman said: “I am a helpless woman, and this dog drives wild beasts away from me and alerts me when someone comes.” I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, but he ordered me to kill it.","صحيح: رواه أحمد (27188)."],[1057,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave, and the verse: “By those sent forth in succession…” had just been revealed to him, and we were receiving it fresh from his mouth. Then a snake came out toward us. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Kill it.” We rushed to kill it, but it escaped us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Allah protected it from your harm just as He protected you from its harm.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4931)، ومسلم (2234)."],[1058,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a person in the state of iḥrām to kill a snake at Minā.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1235)."],[1059,"Abū al-Sā’ib, the freedman of Hishām ibn Zuhrah, narrated: I entered upon Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and found him praying. I sat waiting until he finished his prayer. Then I heard something moving beneath a bed in his house and saw that it was a snake. I stood up to kill it, but Abū Saʿīd gestured to me to sit down. When he finished his prayer, he pointed to a house in the courtyard and said: “Do you see this house?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: There was once a young man living there who had only recently married. He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the Trench. While he was there, the young man came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking permission and said: “O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go and see my family.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him permission and said: “Take your weapon with you, for I fear Banū Qurayẓah for you.” The young man went to his family and found his wife standing between the two doorposts. Jealousy overcame him, so he raised his spear to stab her. She said: “Do not be hasty. Enter and look at what is inside your house.” He entered and found a snake coiled upon his bed. He thrust his spear into it, then carried it outside and planted the spear upright in the courtyard. The snake writhed upon the spear, and the young man fell dead. It was not known which of the two died first—the young man or the snake. We mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “There are jinn in Madinah who have accepted Islam. If you see any of them, warn them for three days. If they appear to you after that, then kill them, for it is only a devil.” In another wording: “These houses have inhabitants from among the jinn. If you see any of them, warn them for three days. If it leaves, then so be it; otherwise kill it, for it is an unbeliever.” And he said to them: “Go and bury your companion.”","صحيح: رواه مالك (33)، ومسلم (2236، 139)."],[1060,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of the snake with two stripes, for it attacks the eyesight and causes miscarriage.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3309)، ومسلم (2232)."],[1061,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon from the pulpit and saying: “Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed snake, for the two of them cause blindness and cause pregnant women to miscarry.” ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: While I was once chasing a snake in order to kill it, Abū Lubābah called out to me: “Do not kill it.” I replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that snakes be killed.”\nHe said: “After that, he prohibited killing the snakes that live in houses, namely the resident snakes.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3297، 3298)، ومسلم (2233، 128)."],[1062,"Nāfiʿ narrated: Abū Lubābah spoke to Ibn ʿUmar about opening a door in his house so that he could have a shorter route to the mosque. The young servants then found the shed skin of a snake. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: “Look for it and kill it.” Abū Lubābah said: “Do not kill it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited killing the snakes that live in houses.” In another narration: Abū Lubābah ibn ʿAbd al-Mundhir al-Anṣārī used to live in Qubāʾ and later moved to Madinah. While ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar was sitting with him as a small doorway was being opened for him, they suddenly saw a snake from among the resident snakes of houses. They intended to kill it, but Abū Lubābah said: “Killing these has been prohibited,” meaning the resident snakes of houses. He added that the short-tailed snake and the one with two stripes had been ordered to be killed.\nIt was said that these are the two that cause the eyesight to flash or be harmed and cause women to miscarry.\nIn another narration: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar was one day near a building of his when he saw the gleam of a snake. He said: “Follow this snake and kill it.” Abū Lubābah al-Anṣārī said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibit killing snakes that live in houses, except the short-tailed snake and the one with two stripes, for these are the two that snatch away eyesight and cause the loss of what is in women’s wombs.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2233، 131)، والبخاري (3312-3313)."],[1063,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning snakes: “We have not made peace with them since we began fighting them. Whoever leaves any of them out of fear is not from us.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5248)، وأحمد (9588، 10741)، والطحاوي في شرح المشكل (1338)."],[1064,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning snakes: “We have not made peace with them since we began fighting them. Whoever leaves them because he fears them is not from us.”","صحيح: رواه الطحاوي في شرح المشكل (1339)."],[1065,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever leaves snakes because he fears pursuing them is not from us. We have not made peace with them since we began fighting them.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5250)، وأحمد (2037)."],[1066,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ saw a man chasing after a pigeon and said: “A devil chasing after a she-devil.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4940)، وابن ماجه (3765)، وأحمد (8543)، وصححه ابن حبان (5874)."],[1067,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no superstitious omen, and the best of it is a good sign.” He was asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is a good sign?” He replied: “A good word that one of you hears.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5754، 5755)، ومسلم (2223)."],[1068,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Superstitious belief in omens is a form of shirk.” ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd added: “There is none among us except that something of it may occur to him, but Allah removes it through reliance upon Him.” In another wording: “Superstitious omens are shirk. Superstitious omens are shirk.” He repeated it three times.","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3910)، والترمذي (1614)، وابن ماجه (3538)، وأحمد (3687، 4171)، وصححه ابن حبان (6122)، والحاكم (1/17-18). واللفظ الثاني لأبي داود، وإسناده صحيح."],[1069,"Umm Kurz narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Leave the birds in their places.”","صحيح: رواه الطيالسي (1739)، والطبراني في الكبير (25/ح 404)."],[1070,"Abū Burdah narrated: I came to ʿĀ’ishah and said: “O my mother, tell me something that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The birds move according to divine decree.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (24982)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (2161)."],[1071,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked superstitious omens and detested them.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (912) - واللفظ له -، وأبو يعلى (2496 - المطالب)."],[1072,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: “The Prophet ﷺ liked a good omen and disliked superstitious pessimism.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3536)، وأحمد (8393)، وصححه ابن حبان (6121)."],[1073,"Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If it were to be in anything, it would be in the horse, the woman, and the dwelling.” Meaning: misfortune or an evil omen.","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (22)، والبخاري (5095)، ومسلم (2226)."],[1074,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “If it were to be in anything, it would be in the dwelling, the servant, and the horse.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2227)."],[1075,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: Misfortune and evil omens were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “If misfortune were to be in anything, it would be in the house, the woman, and the horse.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5094)، ومسلم (2225، 117)."],[1076,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no contagion and no superstitious omen. Misfortune is only in three things: the horse, the woman, and the house.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5772)، ومسلم (2225، 16)."],[1077,"Saʿd ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “There is no hāmah, no contagion, and no superstitious omen. And if a superstitious omen were to exist in anything, it would be in the horse, the woman, and the house.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (3921) - واللفظ له -، وأحمد (1502)، وأبو يعلى (766)، وصححه ابن حبان (6127)."],[1078,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no superstitious omen, and its effect is upon the one who believes in it. If it were to be in anything, it would be in the house, the horse, and the woman.”","حسن: رواه الطحاوي في شرح المعاني (4/314)، وصححه ابن حبان (6123)، والضياء في المختارة (2269)."],[1079,"Abū Ḥassān narrated: Two men from Banū ʿĀmir entered upon ʿĀ’ishah and informed her that Abū Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he had said: “Superstitious misfortune is in the house, the woman, and the horse.” She became intensely angry and said: “By the One who revealed the Criterion to Muḥammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never said that. Rather, he said: ‘The people of the pre-Islamic period used to regard these things as evil omens.’” In another narration, ʿĀ’ishah then recited: “No calamity occurs on earth or within yourselves except that it is written in a Book.” [Sūrat al-Ḥadīd 57:22]","حسن: رواه أحمد (26034، 26088)، والحاكم (2/479)."],[1080,"Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we lived in a house while our numbers were many and our wealth was abundant. Then our numbers decreased and our wealth disappeared.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave it while considering it blameworthy.”","حسن: رواه مالك (23) مرسلا. وروي نحوه عن أنس موصولا عند أبي داود (3924)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (918)، والبيهقي (8/140)، والضياء في المختارة (1529)."],[1081,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is turned back from fulfilling a need because of a superstitious omen has committed shirk.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the expiation for that?” He replied: “That one of them should say: ‘O Allah, there is no good except Your good, there is no omen except what You decree, and there is no deity besides You.’”","حسن: رواه أحمد (7045)، وعبد الله بن وهب في جامعه (658)."],[1082,"Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “Whoever is turned back by a superstitious omen has fallen into shirk.”","حسن: رواه ابن وهب في جامعه (656) موقوفا على فضالة بن عبيد."],[1083,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whenever a man says to his brother, ‘O disbeliever,’ that charge returns upon one of the two.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (1)، والبخاري (6104)."],[1084,"Saʿīd ibn Zayd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not hurt a Muslim by insulting a disbeliever.”","حسن: رواه الحاكم (1420)، وعنه البيهقي في الشعب (6253)."],[1085,"Abū Dharr narrated that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No man accuses another man of wickedness or accuses him of disbelief except that the accusation returns upon him if the person accused is not actually like that.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6045)، ومسلم (61)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[1086,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no one who loves praise more than Allah; for that reason He praised Himself. And there is no one more protective of sacred honor than Allah; for that reason He prohibited obscenities and shameful deeds.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5520)، ومسلم (2760، 32)."],[1087,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah has protective jealousy, and the believer has protective jealousy. Allah’s protective jealousy is aroused when a believer commits what He has forbidden him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5223)، ومسلم (2761)."],[1088,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks, he lies; when he promises, he breaks his promise; and when he is entrusted, he betrays the trust.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6095)، ومسلم (59، 107)."],[1089,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Last night I saw two men who came to me. They said: ‘The man you saw whose side of the mouth was being torn open is a liar. He tells a lie that is carried from him until it reaches the horizons, and this will continue to be done to him until the Day of Resurrection.’”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6096)."],[1090,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. A man continues to speak the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a person of utmost truthfulness. Lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. A man continues to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a persistent liar.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6094)، ومسلم (2607)."],[1091,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: “There was no character trait more hated by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than lying. A man might tell a lie in his presence, and it would remain in the Prophet’s mind concerning him until he knew that the man had repented from it.”","صحيح: رواه ابن حبان (5736)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (20821)."],[1092,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Faith and disbelief do not come together in the heart of a person; truthfulness and lying do not come together completely; and betrayal and trustworthiness do not come together completely.”","حسن: رواه ابن وهب في الجامع (464)، والإمام أحمد (8593)."],[1093,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir narrated: One day my mother called me while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in our house. She said: “Come here, I will give you something.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: “What did you intend to give him?” She replied: “I intended to give him some dates.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you had not given him anything, a lie would have been recorded against you.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4991)، وأحمد (15702)."],[1094,"Bahz ibn Ḥakīm narrated from his father, from his grandfather: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Woe to the one who speaks to people and lies in order to make them laugh. Woe to him! Woe to him!”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4990)، والترمذي (2315)، وأحمد (20021)، والحاكم (142)."],[1095,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man may utter a word merely to make those sitting with him laugh, and because of it he falls farther than the distance of al-Thurayyā.”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن المبارك في الزهد (948)، ومن طريقه أحمد (9220)، وابن حبان (5716)."],[1096,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: A son of Abū Ṭalḥah became ill and then died while Abū Ṭalḥah was away. When his wife saw that the child had died, she prepared him and placed him to one side of the house. When Abū Ṭalḥah returned, he asked: “How is the boy?” She replied: “His soul has become calm, and I hope that he has found rest.” Abū Ṭalḥah thought she meant that the boy had recovered and was resting. He spent the night with her. When morning came, he performed ghusl. As he was preparing to leave, she informed him that the child had died. He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and then informed him of what had happened between the two of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perhaps Allah will bless the two of you in your night.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1301)، ومسلم (2144 عقب الحديث 2457)."],[1097,"Umm Kulthūm bint ʿUqbah narrated that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The person who reconciles between people is not a liar when he conveys something good or says something good.” Muslim adds: Ibn Shihāb said: “I did not hear permission being granted regarding anything that people call lying except in three matters: war, reconciliation between people, and what a man says to his wife and what a woman says to her husband.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2692)، ومسلم (2605)."],[1098,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most hated of men to Allah is the fiercely quarrelsome opponent.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2457)، ومسلم (2668)."],[1100,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not give up false speech, acting upon it, and ignorant behavior, then Allah has no need for him to give up his food and drink.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6057)."],[1101,"Abū Dharr narrated from the Prophet ﷺ, who related from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, that He said: “O My servants, I have forbidden injustice for Myself and have made it forbidden among you, so do not wrong one another. O My servants, all of you are astray except those whom I guide, so seek guidance from Me and I will guide you. O My servants, all of you are hungry except those whom I feed, so ask Me for food and I will feed you. O My servants, all of you are unclothed except those whom I clothe, so ask Me for clothing and I will clothe you. O My servants, you commit sins by night and by day, and I forgive all sins, so seek My forgiveness and I will forgive you. O My servants, you can never reach a level where you could harm Me, nor can you reach a level where you could benefit Me. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were all upon the most God-fearing heart of any one man among you, that would not increase My kingdom in the slightest. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were all upon the most wicked heart of any one man, that would not decrease My kingdom in the slightest. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were all to stand together on one plain and ask Me, and I were to give every person what he asked for, that would not diminish what I possess except as much as a needle diminishes the sea when it is dipped into it. O My servants, these are only your deeds. I enumerate them for you and then repay you for them in full. So whoever finds good, let him praise Allah; and whoever finds otherwise, let him blame no one but himself.”\nSaʿīd said: “Whenever Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī narrated this hadith, he would fall upon his knees.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2577، 55)."],[1102,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of injustice, for injustice will be layers of darkness on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of greed, for greed destroyed those who came before you. It drove them to shed one another’s blood and to treat what was sacred among them as lawful.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2578، 56)."],[1103,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, injustice will be layers of darkness on the Day of Resurrection.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2447)، ومسلم (2579، 57)."],[1104,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you know who the bankrupt person is?” They replied: “The bankrupt person among us is the one who has neither dirhams nor possessions.” He said: “The bankrupt person from my Ummah is the one who comes on the Day of Resurrection with prayer, fasting, and zakāh, but he also comes having insulted this person, falsely accused that person, consumed another person’s wealth, shed another person’s blood, and struck another person. So this person will be given from his good deeds, and that person will be given from his good deeds. If his good deeds run out before what he owes has been fully settled, some of their sins will be taken and cast upon him, and then he will be cast into the Fire.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2581، 59)."],[1105,"Abū Mūsā narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives the wrongdoer respite, but when He seizes him, He does not let him escape.” Then he recited: “Such is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are wrongdoing. Indeed, His seizure is painful and severe.” [Sūrat Hūd 11:102]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4686)، ومسلم (2583، 11)."],[1106,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that Muḥammad ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you what al-ʿaḍh is? It is tale-bearing: carrying statements between people.” And Muḥammad ﷺ also said: “A man continues to speak truthfully until he is recorded as a person of utmost truthfulness, and he continues to lie until he is recorded as a liar.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2606)."],[1107,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you know what al-ʿaḍh is?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “It is carrying statements from some people to others in order to cause corruption between them.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (424)، والبيهقي (21159)."],[1108,"Ḥudhayfah narrated: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “A tale-bearer will not enter Paradise.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6056)، ومسلم (105)، واللفظ لمسلم."],[1109,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by two graves and said: “The two of them are being punished, and they are not being punished for something they regarded as serious. As for this one, he did not protect himself from his urine; and as for the other, he used to go about spreading tales between people.” Then he called for a fresh palm stalk, split it into two pieces, planted one upon each grave, and said: “Perhaps their punishment will be lightened as long as these two do not dry out.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6052)، ومسلم (292)."],[1110,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you know what backbiting is?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “It is mentioning your brother in a way that he dislikes.” It was asked: “What if what I say about my brother is actually true?” He replied: “If what you say is true, then you have backbitten him. If it is not true, then you have slandered him.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2589)."],[1111,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: I imitated a man in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “I would not like to imitate a person even if I were given such-and-such in return.” She said: I then said: “O Messenger of Allah, Ṣafiyyah is a woman…” and she gestured with her hand, apparently indicating that Ṣafiyyah was short. He said: “You have uttered a word which, if it were mixed with the water of the sea, would contaminate it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4875)، والترمذي (2502، 2503)، وأحمد (25560)."],[1112,"Jābir narrated: A foul-smelling wind arose during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Some of the hypocrites have backbitten some of the Muslims, and this wind was sent because of that.”","صحيح: رواه عبد بن حميد (1028)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (733)، والخرائطي في مساوئ الأخلاق (187)."],[1113,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a foul wind, like the smell of a decaying corpse, arose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you know what this smell is? This is the smell of those who backbite the believers.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (14784)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (732)."],[1114,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When I was taken up, I passed by a people who had fingernails of copper with which they were scratching their faces and chests. I asked, ‘Who are these, O Jibrīl?’ He replied, ‘These are the ones who used to eat the flesh of people and attack their honor.’”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4878)، وأحمد (13340)."],[1115,"Anas narrated: The Arabs used to serve one another during journeys. Abū Bakr and ʿUmar had a man with them who served them. He fell asleep, and when they awoke they found that he had not prepared any food. They said: “This man of yours certainly sleeps a lot.” They woke him and said: “Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him: ‘Abū Bakr and ʿUmar send you salām and ask you for something to eat with their bread.’” He went to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Tell them that they have already eaten something with their bread.” They became alarmed and came to the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “O Messenger of Allah, we sent to you asking for something to eat with our bread, and you said that we had already eaten. What did we eat?” He replied: “You ate the flesh of your brother. Indeed, I can see his flesh between your teeth.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, then seek forgiveness for us.” He replied: “Let him seek forgiveness for you.”","حسن: رواه الخرائطي في مساوئ الأخلاق (186)، والضياء المقدسي في المختارة (1696، 1697)."],[1116,"Al-Mustawrid narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever gains a meal at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will feed him the like of it from Hell. Whoever is clothed with a garment at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will clothe him with the like of it from Hell. And whoever takes a stand against a man for the sake of reputation and showing off, Allah will expose him in a position of reputation and showing off on the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4881)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (240)، وأحمد (18011)، وأبو يعلى (6858)."],[1117,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man got up and left. Another man then spoke ill of him after he had gone. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Clean between your teeth.” He said: “Why should I clean between my teeth, O Messenger of Allah? Have I eaten meat?” He replied: “You have eaten the flesh of your brother.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (10092)."],[1118,"Abū Barzah al-Aslamī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O people who have believed with their tongues while faith has not entered their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims and do not search for their faults. Whoever searches for their faults, Allah will search out his faults, and whoever Allah searches out his faults, He will disgrace him even inside his own home.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4880)، وأحمد (19776)، وأبو يعلى (7423)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (21164)."],[1119,"Al-Barāʾ narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us so loudly that even the young women in their homes—or in their private chambers—could hear him. He said: “O people who have believed with their tongues, do not backbite the Muslims and do not search for their faults. Whoever searches for the fault of his brother, Allah will search for his fault, and whoever Allah searches for his fault, He will disgrace him inside his own house.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (1675)."],[1120,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and called out in a loud voice: “O people who have submitted with their tongues while faith has not reached their hearts, do not harm the Muslims, do not shame them, and do not search for their faults. Whoever searches for the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah will search for his fault, and whoever Allah searches for his fault, He will disgrace him even inside his own dwelling.” Ibn ʿUmar once looked at the House—or the Kaʿbah—and said: “How great you are, and how great your sanctity is! Yet the believer has greater sanctity with Allah than you.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2032)، وابن حبان (5763)."],[1121,"Muʿāwiyah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If you search for people’s faults, you will corrupt them—or you will nearly corrupt them.” Abū al-Dardāʾ said: “A statement Muʿāwiyah heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah, the Exalted, benefited him through it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4888)، وابن حبان (5760)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (17623)."],[1122,"Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib and Abū Umāmah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “When a ruler goes looking for reasons to suspect people, he corrupts them.”","حسن: رواه الطبراني في مسند الشاميين (1660)."],[1123,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: A man asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allow him to enter. What a bad son of his clan he is,” or: “What a bad man of his clan he is.” When the man entered, the Prophet ﷺ spoke gently to him. ʿĀ’ishah said: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, you said about him what you said, then you spoke gently to him?” He replied: “O ʿĀ’ishah, among the worst people in rank before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the one whom people leave alone or avoid because they fear his obscene and abusive speech.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6054)، ومسلم (2591، 73)."],[1124,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Defend your honor with your wealth.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how do we defend our honor with our wealth?” He replied: “By giving something to the poet and to anyone whose tongue you fear.”","حسن: رواه حمزة بن يوسف السهمي في تاريخ جرجان (ص 223)."],[1125,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the greatest of the major sins is that a man curses his own parents.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, how does a man curse his own parents?” He replied: “He insults another man’s father, so that man insults his father; and he insults his mother, so that man insults his mother.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5973)، ومسلم (90)."],[1126,"Abū al-Ṭufayl ʿĀmir ibn Wāthilah narrated: I was with ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib when a man came to him and asked: “What did the Prophet ﷺ privately confide to you?” ʿAlī became angry and said: “The Prophet ﷺ never privately told me anything that he concealed from the people, except that he did tell me four statements.” The man asked: “What are they, O Commander of the Believers?” ʿAlī replied that the Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah curse whoever curses his father. May Allah curse whoever sacrifices for other than Allah. May Allah curse whoever shelters an offender. And may Allah curse whoever alters the boundary markers of the land.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1978)."],[1127,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cursed is the one who insults his father. Cursed is the one who insults his mother. Cursed is the one who sacrifices for other than Allah. Cursed is the one who alters the boundaries of the land. Cursed is the one who deliberately misdirects a blind person from the road. Cursed is the one who has intercourse with an animal. Cursed is the one who commits the act of the people of Lūṭ.”\nIn another narration, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated the statement concerning the act of the people of Lūṭ three times.","حسن: رواه أحمد (1875، 2913، 2914، 2915)، والطبراني في الكبير (4/356)."],[1128,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the falsest of speech. Do not spy, do not seek out one another’s secrets, do not compete against one another in rivalry, do not envy one another, do not hate one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. Rather, be servants of Allah as brothers.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (15)، والبخاري (6066)، ومسلم (2563، 28)."],[1129,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not spy on one another, do not seek out one another’s hidden matters, do not engage in deceptive bidding, and be servants of Allah as brothers.” In another wording: “Do not cut one another off, do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, and do not envy one another. Be brothers as Allah has commanded you.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2563، 30)."],[1130,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not boycott one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not seek out one another’s hidden matters, and let none of you sell over the sale of another. Be servants of Allah as brothers.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2563، 29)."],[1131,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and do not compete against one another in rivalry. Be servants of Allah as brothers.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2563، 29)."],[1132,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Beware of envy, for envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes firewood—or he said: grass.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4903)، وعبد بن حميد (1430)."],[1133,"Ḍamrah ibn Thaʿlabah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People will continue to remain upon goodness so long as they do not envy one another.”","حسن: رواه أبو الشيخ في التوبيخ والتنبيه (80)، والطبراني في الكبير (8157)."],[1134,"Zayd ibn Wahb narrated: Someone came to Ibn Masʿūd and said: “So-and-so has wine dripping from his beard.” ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd replied: “We have been prohibited from spying. But if something becomes openly apparent to us, we act upon it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4890)، وعبد الرزاق في المصنف (18945)، وصححه الحاكم (4/377)."],[1135,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Seek help in accomplishing your needs by keeping them concealed, for every blessing has someone who envies it.”","حسن: رواه ابن حبان في روضة العقلاء (ص 187)، وحمزة السهمي في تاريخ جرجان (ص 223)."],[1136,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the Kaʿbah, he said: “Welcome to you, O House! How great you are, and how great your sanctity is! Yet the believer has greater sanctity with Allah than you. Allah has made one thing concerning you sacred, while He has made three things concerning the believer sacred: his blood, his wealth, and that evil suspicion be held about him.”","حسن: رواه البيهقي في الشعب (6280)."],[1137,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “I do not think that so-and-so and so-and-so know anything of our religion.” Al-Layth said: “They were two men from among the hypocrites.” In another wording, ʿĀ’ishah said: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me one day and said: “O ʿĀ’ishah, I do not think that so-and-so and so-and-so understand the religion upon which we are.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6067)."],[1138,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday, and every Muslim servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is hostility. It is said: ‘Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile. Delay these two until they reconcile.’”","صحيح: رواه مالك (17)، ومسلم (2565، 35)."],[1139,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. Be servants of Allah as brothers. It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three nights.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (14)، والبخاري (6076)، ومسلم (2559، 23)."],[1140,"Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three nights. They meet, and this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of the two is the one who begins with the greeting of salām.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (13)، والبخاري (6077)، ومسلم (2560، 25)."],[1141,"ʿAwf ibn Mālik ibn al-Ṭufayl—who was the maternal nephew of ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ—narrated that ʿĀ’ishah related: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr said concerning some sale or gift that ʿĀ’ishah had made: “By Allah, ʿĀ’ishah must stop doing this, or I will have her legally restricted from disposing of her wealth.” ʿĀ’ishah asked: “Did he really say that?” They replied: “Yes.” She said: “By Allah, I make a vow never to speak to Ibn al-Zubayr again.” When the estrangement lasted for a long time, Ibn al-Zubayr sought people to intercede for him with her. She said: “No, by Allah, I will never accept intercession for him, nor will I break my vow.” When this became difficult for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad ibn ʿAbd Yaghūth, both from Banū Zuhrah. He said to them: “I adjure you by Allah to get me into the presence of ʿĀ’ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever relations with me.” Al-Miswar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān brought him with them, wrapped in their cloaks, and sought permission to enter upon ʿĀ’ishah. They said: “Peace, mercy, and blessings of Allah be upon you. May we enter?” ʿĀ’ishah replied: “Enter.” They asked: “All of us?” She replied: “Yes, all of you may enter,” not knowing that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr went behind the curtain, embraced ʿĀ’ishah, and began pleading with her and weeping. Al-Miswar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān also continued pleading with her to speak to him and accept his apology. They reminded her: “The Prophet ﷺ prohibited the kind of estrangement that you know about, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three nights.” When they repeatedly reminded her and pressed her strongly, ʿĀ’ishah began reminding them of her vow while weeping and saying: “I made a vow, and a vow is a serious matter.” They continued until she finally spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr. As expiation connected to that vow, she freed forty slaves. Afterward, whenever she remembered her vow, she would weep until her tears soaked her head covering.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6073، 6074، 6075)."],[1142,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a believer to boycott his brother for more than three days.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2561)."],[1143,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is to be no estrangement after three days.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2562)."],[1144,"Saʿd ibn Mālik Abū Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (1589)، والبزار - كشف الأستار (2051)، وأبو يعلى (720)."],[1145,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A Muslim should not boycott another Muslim for more than three days. If he meets him and gives him salām three times, but each time the other person refuses to return it, then the one who refuses bears the sin.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4913)، وأبو يعلى (4583)."],[1146,"Hishām ibn ʿĀmir narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott another Muslim for more than three nights. If their severance continues beyond three, then both of them have deviated from the truth for as long as they remain estranged. The first of them to return and reconcile has that initiative as an expiation for him. If he gives salām to the other but the other does not return it, the angels return his salām, while Satan responds to the other. If they both die while persisting in their severance, they will never be together in Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (16257)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (402، 407)، وصححه ابن حبان (5664)."],[1147,"Abū Khirāsh al-Sulamī narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever boycotts his brother for a year, it is like shedding his blood.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4915)، وأحمد (17935)، وصححه الحاكم (7292)."],[1148,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is enough of a lie for a person to relate everything he hears.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (5)، وأبو داود (4992)."],[1149,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is kufr.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (48)، ومسلم (64)."],[1150,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fighting a Muslim is kufr, insulting him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days.”","حسن: رواه النسائي (4104)، وأحمد (1519)."],[1151,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is kufr.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (3940)."],[1152,"Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is kufr.”","حسن: رواه المروزي في تعظيم قدر الصلاة (1104)."],[1153,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever two people who insult one another say, the sin of it falls upon the one who began it, so long as the wronged person does not exceed the limit.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2587)."],[1154,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whatever two people who insult one another say, the burden falls upon the one who began it until the wronged person exceeds the limit.”","حسن: رواه البخاري في الأدب المفرد (424)."],[1155,"ʿIyāḍ ibn Ḥimār narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what about a man from my people who insults me even though he is beneath me in status?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The two people who exchange insults are two devils, speaking recklessly and lying against one another. Whatever they say is upon the one who began it, until the wronged person exceeds the limit.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود الطيالسي (1176)، ومن طريقه البيهقي (21087)، وأحمد (17486، 17488)."],[1156,"Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not insult the dead, for by doing so you hurt the living.”","صحيح: رواه الترمذي (1982)، وصححه ابن حبان (3022)."],[1157,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a person of utmost truthfulness to be someone who frequently curses.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2597)."],[1158,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was neither abusive, obscene in speech, nor one who frequently cursed. When reproaching one of us, he would merely say: “What is the matter with him? May dust be upon his forehead.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6031)."],[1159,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Those who frequently curse will not be intercessors or witnesses on the Day of Resurrection.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2598، 85)."],[1160,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, supplicate against the polytheists.” He replied: “I was not sent as one who curses. I was only sent as a mercy.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2599)."],[1161,"Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk—who was among the Companions who pledged allegiance beneath the tree—narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he has said. A son of Ādam has no binding vow concerning something he does not own. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever curses a believer is like one who kills him, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like one who kills him.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6047)، ومسلم (110)."],[1162,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The believer is not one who curses others, attacks people’s honor, speaks obscenely, or uses foul language.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (3948)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (312)، وصححه ابن حبان (192)، والحاكم (30)."],[1163,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a believer to be someone who frequently curses.”","حسن: رواه الترمذي (2019)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (309)، وصححه الحاكم (145)."],[1164,"Al-ʿAyzār ibn Jarwal al-Ḥaḍramī narrated from a man of his people known as Abū ʿUmayr, who was a friend of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd: ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd once visited him at his home but did not find him there. He sought permission from his family, greeted them with salām, and asked for something to drink. The woman of the house sent a servant girl to bring him a drink from the neighbors, but she was delayed, so the woman cursed her. ʿAbdullāh then left. When Abū ʿUmayr returned, he said: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, someone like you should not be made to feel unwelcome. Why did you not greet your brother’s family, sit down, and have something to drink?” He replied: “I did. She sent the servant girl, but she was delayed. Perhaps they had nothing, or perhaps the neighbors were reluctant to give what they had. When the servant girl was delayed, she cursed her.” Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a curse is directed toward someone, if it finds a valid path to him, or finds something in him that deserves it, then it reaches him. Otherwise it says: ‘My Lord, I was directed toward so-and-so, but I found no path to him and found nothing in him deserving it.’ It is then told: ‘Return from where you came.’” ʿAbdullāh said: “So I feared that the servant girl might have had a valid excuse, and that the curse would return, with me being the cause of it.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (3876)."],[1165,"Jarmūz al-Hujaymī narrated: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He replied: “I advise you not to be one who frequently curses.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (20678)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (1189)، والطبراني في الكبير (2180)."],[1166,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated: A man cursed the wind in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse the wind, for it is commanded. Whoever curses something that does not deserve the curse, the curse returns upon him.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4908)، والترمذي (1978)، وصححه ابن حبان (5745)."],[1167,"Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a servant curses something, the curse rises toward the sky, but the gates of the sky are closed before it. It then descends toward the earth, but its gates are closed before it. It then turns to the right and to the left. If it finds no place to go, it returns to the one who was cursed. If that person deserves it, it reaches him; otherwise, it returns to the one who uttered it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4905)، وابن أبي الدنيا في الصمت (384)."],[1168,"Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the wrath of Allah, nor with the Fire.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4906)، والترمذي (1976)، وأحمد (20175)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (320)."],[1169,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Might is His lower garment, and greatness is His cloak; whoever contends with Me regarding them, I will punish him.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2620)."],[1170,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: “Greatness is My cloak, and majesty is My lower garment. Whoever contends with Me regarding either of them, I will cast him into the Fire.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4090)، وابن حبان (5671)، وأحمد (8894)."],[1171,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who has an atom’s weight of arrogance in his heart will enter Paradise.” A man said: “A man likes his clothes to be good and his sandals to be good.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Indeed, Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty. Arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down upon people.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (91، 147)."],[1172,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who has a mustard seed’s weight of faith in his heart will enter the Fire, and no one who has a mustard seed’s weight of arrogance in his heart will enter Paradise.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (91، 148)."],[1173,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A handsome man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, beauty has been made beloved to me, and I have been given of it what you see. I do not even like anyone to surpass me”—either he said—“in the strap of my sandal,” or, “in the lace of my sandal. Is that arrogance?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “No. Rather, arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down upon people.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (4092)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (556)، وصححه ابن حبان (5467)."],[1174,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ narrated: A man ate with his left hand in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Eat with your right hand.” The man replied: “I cannot.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “May you not be able to.” Nothing prevented him except arrogance. Salamah said: “After that, he was never able to raise that hand to his mouth.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2021)."],[1175,"Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ met at al-Marwah and spoke together. Then ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr went on, while ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar remained behind weeping. A man asked him: “Why are you crying, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He replied: “This man”—meaning ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr—“claims that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever has a mustard seed’s weight of arrogance in his heart, Allah will cast him face-first into the Fire.’”","حسن: رواه أحمد (7015)، وابن أبي الدنيا في التواضع (196)."],[1176,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever considers himself great or walks arrogantly will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”","صحيح: رواه الإمام أحمد (5995)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (549)."],[1177,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are three whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: an elderly adulterer, a lying ruler, and an arrogant poor man.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (107)."],[1178,"Salmān narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three will not enter Paradise: an elderly adulterer, a lying leader, and an impoverished man who is conceited and arrogant.”","حسن: رواه البزار (2529)."],[1179,"Ḥārithah ibn Wahb al-Khuzāʿī narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you who the people of Paradise are? Every weak person whom people regard as insignificant; if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath. Shall I tell you who the people of the Fire are? Every harsh, arrogant, overbearing person.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6071)، ومسلم (2853)."],[1180,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is enough evil for a person that he despise his Muslim brother. Everything belonging to a Muslim is sacred to another Muslim: his blood, his wealth, and his honor.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2564، 32)."],[1181,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How many a disheveled person, driven away from people’s doors, is such that if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would surely fulfill his oath.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2622)."],[1182,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a man from the Anṣār who was ill. As he approached his house, he heard him speaking to someone inside. When the Prophet ﷺ sought permission and entered, he saw no one there. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “I heard you speaking to someone.” The man replied: “O Messenger of Allah, I entered the house distressed by what people were saying about the fever that has afflicted me. Then a man entered upon me. After you, I have never seen anyone more dignified in company or more pleasant in speech than him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “That was Jibrīl. Indeed, among you are men such that if one of them were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath.”","حسن: رواه البزار - كشف الأستار (2811)، والطبراني في الكبير (12264)."],[1183,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you did not commit sins, I would fear for you something even worse than that: self-admiration.”","حسن: رواه البزار (6936)."],[1184,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: “I am the One who has no need whatsoever of partners. Whoever performs a deed in which he associates someone else with Me, I abandon him and his association.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2985)."],[1185,"Jundub narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs deeds so that people will hear of them, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6499)، ومسلم (2987)."],[1186,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks reputation through his deeds, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2986)."],[1187,"Abū Saʿd ibn Abī Faḍālah al-Anṣārī, who was among the Companions, narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gathers the first and the last for a Day about which there is no doubt, a caller will announce: ‘Whoever associated anyone with Allah, Blessed and Exalted, in a deed he performed, let him seek his reward from other than Allah, Mighty and Majestic. For Allah has absolutely no need of any partner.’”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (15838) - والسياق له -، والترمذي (3154)، وابن ماجه (4203)، وابن حبان (404)."],[1188,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever publicizes his deeds so that people will hear of them, Allah will make the creation hear of him, and He will belittle and humiliate him.”","صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (14414)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (911)."],[1189,"Abū Hind al-Dārī narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever takes a position for the sake of showing off and seeking reputation, Allah, the Exalted, will expose his showing off and reputation-seeking on the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (22322)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (2026)، والطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 803)."],[1190,"Abū Bakrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks reputation through his deeds, Allah will expose him; and whoever shows off, Allah will expose his showing off.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (20456)، والبزار (3691)."],[1191,"Bashīr ibn ʿAqrabah al-Juhanī narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever stands to deliver a sermon seeking nothing through it except showing off and reputation, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will make him stand on the Day of Resurrection in a position of showing off and reputation-seeking.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (16073)."],[1192,"Shaddād ibn Aws narrated: “During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to regard showing off as minor shirk.”","حسن: رواه البزار في كشف الأستار (3565)، والطبراني في الأوسط في مجمع البحرين (4941)."],[1193,"Maḥmūd ibn Labīd narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came out and said: “O people, beware of hidden shirk.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is hidden shirk?” He replied: “A man stands to pray and exerts himself in beautifying his prayer because he sees people looking at him. That is hidden shirk.” In another narration, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The thing I fear most for you is minor shirk.” They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is minor shirk?” He replied: “Showing off. On the Day of Resurrection, when people are rewarded for their deeds, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to them: ‘Go to those for whom you used to show off in the world and see whether you find any reward with them.’”","صحيح: رواه ابن خزيمة (937)، وابن أبي شيبة (8489)، وأحمد (23631)، والبغوي في شرح السنة (4135)، والبيهقي في شعب الإيمان (6831)."],[1194,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said three times: “O heralds of the death of the Arabs! Indeed, what I fear most for you is showing off and hidden desire.”","حسن: رواه أبو يعلى كما في المطالب العالية (3222)، والبيهقي في الزهد (316)."],[1195,"Shahr ibn Ḥawshab narrated that he heard Ibn Ghanm say: When Abū al-Dardāʾ and I entered the mosque of al-Jābiyah, we met ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit. He took my right hand with his left and the left hand of Abū al-Dardāʾ with his right, and walked between us while we were speaking privately—and Allah knows best what we were speaking about. ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit said: “If either one of you, or both of you, live long enough, you will soon see a man from the very midst of the Muslims who has learned the Qur’an directly from the tongue of Muḥammad ﷺ, repeating and reciting it, treating its lawful as lawful and its unlawful as unlawful, and observing its proper limits; or who learned it from his brother exactly as it was recited from the tongue of Muḥammad ﷺ, repeating and reciting it, treating its lawful as lawful and its unlawful as unlawful, and observing its proper limits—yet among you he will be of no more benefit than the head of a dead donkey.” While we were in that state, Shaddād ibn Aws and ʿAwf ibn Mālik arrived and sat with us. Shaddād said: “O people, what I fear most for you is what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention: ‘Hidden desire and shirk.’” ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit and Abū al-Dardāʾ said: “O Allah, forgive us! Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not tell us: ‘Satan has despaired of being worshiped in the Arabian Peninsula’?” They continued: “As for hidden desire, we know what that is: the desires of this world, including its women and other attractions. But what is this shirk about which you are frightening us, O Shaddād?” Shaddād replied: “Suppose you saw a man praying for the sake of another person, fasting for his sake, or giving charity for his sake. Would you consider that shirk?” They replied: “Yes, by Allah. Whoever prays, fasts, or gives charity for another person has committed shirk.” Shaddād said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever prays to show off has committed shirk; whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk; and whoever gives charity to show off has committed shirk.’” ʿAwf ibn Mālik then said: “Would Allah not take from the entirety of that deed what was sincerely intended for His Face, accept what was purely for Him, and leave aside what involved association?” Shaddād replied: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I am the best One with whom a share may be assigned. Whoever associates anything with Me, then the entirety of his deed—little or much—is for the partner whom he associated with Me, and I have no need of it.’”","حسن: رواه أحمد (17140) واللفظ له، والطبراني في الكبير (7/337)، والحاكم (4/329)، وأبو نعيم في الحلية (1/268-269)."],[1196,"Al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Qays narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah says: ‘I am the best of partners. Whoever associates someone with Me, then his deed belongs to that partner.’ O people, make your deeds sincere for Allah, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, accepts no deed except that which is sincerely for Him. Do not say, ‘This is for Allah and for maintaining family ties,’ for then it is for the family ties and Allah has no share in it. And do not say, ‘This is for Allah and for gaining people’s favor,’ for then it is for gaining people’s favor and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has no share in it.”","حسن: رواه ابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (473)."],[1197,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were discussing al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl. He said: “Shall I tell you what I fear for you even more than al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl?” We replied: “Yes.” He said: “Hidden shirk: a man stands to pray and beautifies his prayer because he notices another man watching him.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (4204). وإسناده حسن من أجل ربيح بن عبد الرحمن؛ مختلف فيه، غير أنه حسن الحديث. قال أبو زرعة: شيخ، وقال ابن عدي: أرجو أنه لا بأس به، وذكره ابن حبان في الثقات، فيحسن حديثه إذا كان له أصل، وهذا منه. وقد حسنه أيضا البوصيري في الزوائد."],[1198,"Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of injustice, for injustice will be layers of darkness on the Day of Resurrection. And beware of avarice, for avarice destroyed those who came before you. It drove them to shed one another’s blood and to make lawful what was sacred among them.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2578، 56)."],[1199,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The worst traits that can be in a man are overwhelming avarice and devastating cowardice.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2511)، وأحمد (8010، 8263)، وابن حبان (3250)، والبيهقي (150)."],[1200,"Abū al-Aʿwar al-Sulamī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I fear only three things for my Ummah: avarice that is obeyed, desire that is followed, and a misguided leader.”","حسن: رواه ابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (707)، وأبو نعيم في معرفة الصحابة (5071)."],[1201,"One of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so owns a date-palm in my garden. Tell him to sell it to me or give it to me.” The man refused. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Do so, and in exchange you will have a date-palm in Paradise.” He still refused. The Prophet ﷺ then said: “This is the most miserly of people.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23085)."],[1202,"Jābir narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “So-and-so owns a cluster-bearing date-palm in my garden, and its location has caused me harm and hardship.” The Prophet ﷺ sent for its owner and said: “Sell me your date-palm that is in so-and-so’s garden.” He replied: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Then give it to me as a gift.” He replied: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Then sell it to me in exchange for a date-palm in Paradise.” He again replied: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I have not seen anyone more miserly than you except one who is miserly even with the greeting of salām.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (14517)."],[1203,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O people, purchase your own souls from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. If one of you is too miserly to give his wealth to other people, then let him at least spend charitably upon himself: let him eat and clothe himself from what Allah has provided him.”","صحيح: رواه البيهقي في شعب الإيمان (4250)."],[1206,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Advise me.” He replied: “Do not become angry.” The man repeated his request several times, and each time the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not become angry.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (6161)."],[1207,"Jāriyah ibn Qudāmah narrated: A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell me something, but keep it brief so that I may understand and retain it.” He replied: “Do not become angry.” The man repeated the request several times, and every time the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not become angry.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (15964)، وابن حبان (5690). وإسناده صحيح، ووقع اختلاف طويل في إسناده، وما ذكرته هو أسلمها كما لمح ابن حجر في ترجمته في الإصابة."],[1208,"A man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated: A man said: “Advise me, O Messenger of Allah.” He replied: “Do not become angry.” The man said: “I reflected upon what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said and realized that anger gathers together every form of evil.”\nIn another wording, a man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Tell me some words by which I may live, but do not give me too many lest I forget.” He said: “Avoid anger.” The man repeated his request, and the Prophet ﷺ again said: “Avoid anger.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (23171) عن عبد الرزاق - وهو في مصنفه - (20286). وإسناده صحيح، وجهالة الصحابي لا تضر."],[1209,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “What will keep me far from the anger of Allah, Mighty and Majestic?” He replied: “Do not become angry.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (6635)."],[1210,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whom do you consider to be the bereaved person among you?” We replied: “The one to whom no children are born.” He said: “That is not the truly bereaved person. Rather, it is the man who has not sent any of his children ahead of him in death.” Then he said: “Whom do you consider to be the strong wrestler among you?” We replied: “The one whom other men cannot throw down.” He said: “That is not the truly strong one. Rather, it is the one who controls himself when angry.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2608، 106)."],[1211,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The strong man is not the one who defeats others in wrestling. The truly strong man is the one who controls himself when angry.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (12)، والبخاري (6114)، ومسلم (2609، 107)."],[1212,"Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ passed by some people who were lifting a heavy stone. He asked: “What are these people doing?” They replied: “They are lifting a stone to demonstrate their strength.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you who is stronger than him—or words to that effect? The strongest among you is the one who has the greatest control over himself when angry.” In another narration, the Prophet ﷺ passed by some people wrestling and asked: “What is this?” They replied: “O Messenger of Allah, this man is an unbeatable wrestler. He wrestles no one except that he throws him down.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you who is stronger than him? A man whom another person wrongs, yet he suppresses his anger. In doing so, he overcomes him, overcomes his own devil, and overcomes the devil of his companion.”","حسن: رواهما البزار في مسنده (7270، 7272)."],[1213,"Sulaymān ibn Ṣurad narrated: Two men insulted one another in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ while we were sitting with him. One of them was angrily insulting the other, and his face had become red. The Prophet ﷺ said: “I know a statement which, if he were to say it, what he is experiencing would leave him. If he said: ‘I seek refuge in Allah from Satan, the accursed.’” The people said to the man: “Do you not hear what the Prophet ﷺ is saying?” He replied: “I am not insane.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6115)، ومسلم (2610)."],[1214,"Abū Dharr narrated: He was drawing water at a trough belonging to him when some people came. He said: “Which of you will draw water for Abū Dharr and earn a reward, even if it costs him a few hairs from his head?” A man said: “I will.” The man came to draw water at the trough and broke it. Abū Dharr had been standing, so he sat down and then lay down. He was asked: “O Abū Dharr, why did you sit down and then lie down?” He replied: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “If one of you becomes angry while standing, let him sit down. If his anger leaves him, then so be it; otherwise, let him lie down.”","صحيح: رواه أحمد (21348)."],[1216,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while there was a curtain in the house containing images. His facial expression changed, then he seized the curtain and tore it down. ʿĀ’ishah said that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who make these images.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6109)، ومسلم (2107، 91)."],[1217,"Abū Masʿūd narrated: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I sometimes delay attending the morning prayer because so-and-so prolongs the prayer for us.” Abū Masʿūd said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more intensely angry while delivering an admonition than he was that day. He said: “O people, some of you drive people away. Whoever among you leads the people in prayer should keep it reasonably brief, for among them are the sick, the elderly, and those who have needs.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6110)، ومسلم (466)."],[1218,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: While the Prophet ﷺ was praying, he saw some phlegm on the qiblah wall of the mosque. He scraped it away with his hand and became angry. Then he said: “When one of you is in prayer, Allah is before his face, so he must not spit phlegm in front of himself while praying.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6111)، ومسلم (547)."],[1219,"Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī narrated: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about lost property. He said: “Announce it for a year. Then remember the tying-string of its container and its covering, and afterward make use of it. If its owner comes, return it to him.” The man asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what about a stray sheep?” He replied: “Take it, for it belongs either to you, to your brother, or to the wolf.” The man then asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what about a stray camel?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until his cheeks—or his face—turned red. Then he said: “What concern is it of yours? It has its own feet and its own water supply, and it can survive until its owner finds it.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6112)، ومسلم (1722، 2)."],[1220,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face.” In another wording: “When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face, for Allah created Ādam in his image.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2559)، ومسلم (2612)."],[1221,"Hishām ibn Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah will punish those who torture people in this world.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2613، 117)."],[1222,"ʿĀ’ishah narrated: Some Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Death be upon you.” ʿĀ’ishah replied: “And upon you, and may Allah curse you and be angry with you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Easy, O ʿĀ’ishah. You must be gentle, and beware of harshness and obscene speech.” She said: “Did you not hear what they said?” He replied: “Did you not hear what I said? I answered them, so my supplication concerning them will be answered, while theirs concerning me will not be answered.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6030)، ومسلم (2165)."],[1223,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever withdraws from obedience, separates from the community, and then dies, dies a death of jāhiliyyah. Whoever fights beneath a blind banner, becoming angry for tribal partisanship, calling to tribal partisanship, or supporting tribal partisanship, and is killed, his death is a death of jāhiliyyah. And whoever rises against my Ummah, striking both its righteous and its wicked, showing no restraint toward its believers, and not fulfilling the covenant of those who have a covenant, is not from me and I am not from him.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (1848)."],[1224,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: We were on a military expedition when a man from the Muhājirūn struck a man from the Anṣār on the backside. The Anṣārī called out: “O Anṣār!” And the Muhājir called out: “O Muhājirūn!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard this and said: “What is this call of jāhiliyyah?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Muhājirūn struck a man from the Anṣār.” He said: “Leave it, for it is foul.” When ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy heard about this, he said: “They have done it! By Allah, when we return to Madinah, the mightier will surely expel the more humiliated from it.” This reached the Prophet ﷺ. ʿUmar stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Leave him, lest people say that Muḥammad kills his own companions.” The Anṣār were more numerous than the Muhājirūn when they first came to Madinah, but later the Muhājirūn increased in number.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4095، 4907)، ومسلم (2584، 63)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[1225,"Jābir narrated: Two young men fought, one from the Muhājirūn and one from the Anṣār. The Muhājir—or the Muhājirūn—called: “O Muhājirūn!” And the Anṣārī called: “O Anṣār!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: “What is this? The call of the people of jāhiliyyah?” They replied: “No, O Messenger of Allah. It is only that two young men fought and one struck the other.” He said: “Then there is no harm. Let a man support his brother whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is an oppressor, let him restrain him, for that is supporting him. And if he is oppressed, then let him help him.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2584، 62)."],[1226,"Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ narrated: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, what is tribal partisanship?” He replied: “That you support your people in wrongdoing.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5119)."],[1227,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has removed from you the arrogance of jāhiliyyah and its boasting about forefathers. A person is either a God-fearing believer or a wretched sinner. You are all children of Ādam, and Ādam was created from dust. People must stop boasting about peoples who are merely pieces of coal from the coal of Hell, or else they will become more insignificant before Allah than dung beetles that push filth with their noses.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (5116) واللفظ له، والترمذي (3956)."],[1228,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not boast about your forefathers who died in jāhiliyyah. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, what a dung beetle rolls away with its nostrils is better than your forefathers who died in jāhiliyyah.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود الطيالسي (2804)، ومن طريقه أحمد (2739)، وابن حبان (5775)."],[1229,"Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated: Two men boasted of their lineage during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One of them said: “I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so,” and continued naming his lineage, then said: “Who are you? May you have no mother!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two men boasted of their lineage during the time of Mūsā, peace be upon him. One of them said: ‘I am so-and-so son of so-and-so,’ until he counted nine ancestors, then said: ‘Who are you? May you have no mother!’ The other said: ‘I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, a son of Islam.’ Allah then revealed to Mūsā, peace be upon him, concerning the two men: ʿAs for you who affiliated yourself with nine men in the Fire, you are their tenth. And as for you who affiliated yourself with two men in Paradise, you are their third in Paradise.’”","حسن: رواه عبد الله بن أحمد في زوائد المسند (21178)، وعبد بن حميد (179)."],[1230,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “All of my Ummah may be pardoned except those who openly publicize their sins. Part of openly publicizing sin is that a man commits a deed at night, then wakes in the morning after Allah has concealed it for him, and says: ‘O so-and-so, last night I did such-and-such.’ His Lord had concealed him throughout the night, yet in the morning he removes Allah’s covering from himself.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6069)، ومسلم (2990)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[1231,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Zamʿah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and admonished the people concerning their laughter when someone passed wind. He said: “Why does one of you laugh at something that he himself does?”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4942)، ومسلم (2855)."],[1232,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not laugh excessively, for excessive laughter deadens the heart.”","حسن: رواه ابن ماجه (4193)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (253)."],[1235,"Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The Muslim who commits the gravest offense against the Muslims is the one who asks about something that had not been prohibited, and it then becomes prohibited because of his questioning.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7289)، ومسلم (2358، 132)."],[1236,"Anas ibn Mālik narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People will continue asking one another questions until they say: ‘Allah created everything, so who created Allah?’” In another wording, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ‘Your Ummah will continue saying: What about this? What about that? Until they say: Allah created creation, so who created Allah?’”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7296)، ومسلم (136)."],[1237,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about matters that he disliked being asked about. When they persisted in questioning him, he became angry and said: “Ask me.” A man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?” He replied: “Your father is Ḥudhāfah.” Another man stood and asked: “O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?” He replied: “Your father is Sālim, the freedman of Shaybah.” When ʿUmar saw the anger on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “We repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7291)، ومسلم (2360)."],[1238,"Warrād, the secretary of al-Mughīrah, narrated: Muʿāwiyah wrote to al-Mughīrah: “Write to me what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Al-Mughīrah wrote back that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to say after every prayer: “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, without partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth or status of the fortunate cannot benefit him against You.” He also wrote that the Prophet ﷺ used to prohibit idle hearsay, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth, and that he prohibited disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, withholding what one owes, and constantly demanding from others.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (7292)، ومسلم (593)."],[1239,"Anas narrated: We were with ʿUmar when he said: “We were prohibited from affectation and unnecessary burdening of ourselves.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (7293)."],[1240,"Ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The extremists who go beyond proper bounds are ruined.” He said it three times.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2670)."],[1241,"ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sā’ib ibn Yazīd narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Let none of you take his brother’s belongings, whether jokingly or seriously. Whoever takes his brother’s stick must return it.”","صحيح: رواه أبو داود (5003)، والترمذي (2160)، وأحمد (17940)، والحاكم (6686)."],[1242,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of al-qasāmah.” They asked: “What is al-qasāmah?” He replied: “It is something shared among people, and a person comes and takes a portion away from it.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (2783)، ومن طريقه البيهقي (13024)."],[1243,"Qays ibn Saʿd said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Scheming and deception are in the Fire,” I would have been among the most cunning of people.","حسن: رواه ابن عدي في الكامل (351)، ومن طريقه البيهقي في الشعب (10595)."],[1244,"Abū Hurayrah narrated: An effeminate man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ who had dyed his hands and feet with henna. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “What is the matter with this man?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, he imitates women.” So the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be exiled to al-Naqīʿ. They asked: “O Messenger of Allah, should we not kill him?” He replied: “I have been prohibited from killing those who pray.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4928)، وأبو يعلى (6126)، والبيهقي (16987)."],[1245,"Umm Salamah narrated: An effeminate man was in her home while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was also in the house. The man said to Umm Salamah’s brother: “O ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Umayyah, if Allah grants you victory over al-Ṭā’if tomorrow, I will direct you to the daughter of Ghaylān. She approaches with four and turns away with eight.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard him and said: “Do not allow such people to enter upon you.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4324)، ومسلم (2180)."],[1246,"Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who adopted the mannerisms of men, and said: “Expel them from your homes.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Prophet ﷺ expelled one such person, and ʿUmar expelled another.","صحيح: رواه البخاري (5886)."],[1248,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks, he lies; when he promises, he breaks his promise; and when he is entrusted, he betrays the trust.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (33)، ومسلم (59)."],[1249,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “There are four traits which, if all are found in a person, make him a pure hypocrite. Whoever has one of them has a trait of hypocrisy until he abandons it: when entrusted, he betrays; when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a covenant, he acts treacherously; and when he disputes, he behaves wickedly.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (34)، ومسلم (58)."],[1250,"ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever possesses three traits is a hypocrite, and whoever possesses one of them has a trait of hypocrisy: when he speaks, he lies; when entrusted, he betrays; and when he promises, he breaks his promise.”","صحيح: رواه البزار (1662)."],[1251,"Anas narrated: Rarely would the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deliver a sermon to us without saying: “There is no complete faith for the one who is not trustworthy, and there is no true religion for the one who does not honor his covenant.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (12383)، وأبو يعلى (12863)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (100)، والطبراني في الأوسط (2627)."],[1252,"ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Most of the hypocrites of my Ummah will be among its reciters.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (6637)، والبخاري في التاريخ الكبير (1/257)، والبغوي في شرح السنة (39)."],[1253,"ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Most of the hypocrites of this Ummah will be among its reciters.”","حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (17410)."],[1254,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the worst of people is the two-faced person, who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another face.” In another wording: “You will find among the worst people before Allah on the Day of Resurrection the two-faced person, who comes to these people with one face and to those people with another.”","متفق عليه: رواه مالك (21)، ومسلم (2526، 98) عقب الحديث (2604)، والبخاري (7179)."],[1255,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a two-faced person to be trustworthy.”","حسن: رواه أحمد (8781)، والخرائطي في مساوئ الأخلاق (291)، والبيهقي في السنن (154)."],[1256,"The Mother of the Believers, ʿĀ’ishah, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not fitting for a two-faced person to be honored or distinguished on the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه الخرائطي في مساوئ الأخلاق (294)."],[1257,"ʿAmmār narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has two faces in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.”","حسن: رواه أبو داود (4873)، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (1310)، وأبو يعلى (1620)."],[1258,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated: When ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy died, his son ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him to give him his shirt so that his father could be shrouded in it. The Prophet ﷺ gave it to him. Then he asked the Prophet ﷺ to perform the funeral prayer over his father. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to pray over him. ʿUmar stood and took hold of the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you pray over him when your Lord has forbidden you from doing so?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Allah has only given me a choice. He said: ‘Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them. Even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them. That is because they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger, and Allah does not guide the defiantly disobedient people.’ I will ask more than seventy times.” ʿUmar said: “But he is a hypocrite.” Nevertheless, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over him. Then Allah revealed: “And never pray over any of them who dies, nor stand at his grave.” [Sūrat al-Tawbah 9:84]","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4670)، ومسلم (2400)."],[1259,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Prophet ﷺ came to the grave of ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy. He had him taken out of his grave, placed him upon his knees, blew some of his saliva upon him, and clothed him in his shirt. And Allah knows best.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1270)، ومسلم (2773)."],[1260,"Qays ibn ʿUbād narrated: I said to ʿAmmār: “Regarding what you have done in the matter of ʿAlī, was it an opinion you formed yourselves, or was it something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ specifically entrusted to you?” He replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not entrust us with anything that he did not also convey to the people generally. However, Ḥudhayfah informed me from the Prophet ﷺ that the Prophet ﷺ said: ‘Among my companions are twelve hypocrites. Eight of them will not enter Paradise until a camel passes through the eye of a needle. As for eight of them, al-dubaylah will suffice against them.’” Regarding the remaining four, Aswad ibn ʿĀmir said: “I did not retain what Shuʿbah said concerning them.” In another narration, they said to ʿAmmār: “Regarding your fighting, was it merely an opinion you formed? Opinions can be right or wrong. Or was it something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ specifically entrusted to you?” He replied: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not entrust us with anything that he did not also entrust to all the people.” Then he said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, among my Ummah…” Shuʿbah said: “I think he said: ‘Ḥudhayfah narrated to me.’”\nGhundar said: “I think he said: ‘Among my Ummah are twelve hypocrites who will neither enter Paradise nor smell its fragrance until a camel enters through the eye of a needle. Eight of them will be dealt with by al-dubaylah: a lamp of fire that will appear in their shoulders until it emerges from their chests.’”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2779، 9)."],[1261,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever ascends this mountain pass—the pass of al-Murār—will have his sins removed just as they were removed from the Children of Israel.” Jābir said: The first to ascend it were our horses, the horses of Banū al-Khazraj, and then the rest of the people followed one after another. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “All of you have been forgiven except the owner of the red camel.” We went to him and said: “Come, so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ may seek forgiveness for you.” He replied: “By Allah, finding my lost property is more beloved to me than having your companion seek forgiveness for me.” Jābir said: The man was searching for something he had lost.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2780)."],[1262,"Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey. When he came near Madinah, a fierce wind began to blow, so strong that it nearly overturned a rider. It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This wind has been sent because of the death of a hypocrite.” When he arrived in Madinah, it was found that one of the prominent hypocrites had died.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2782)."],[1263,"Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ narrated: We visited a man suffering from fever together with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I placed my hand upon him and said: “By Allah, I have never seen a man as intensely hot with fever as this man today.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I tell you of two men who will be even hotter than him on the Day of Resurrection? Those two riders who are turning away.” He was referring to two men who were then among his companions.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2783)."],[1264,"Anas narrated: There was a Christian man who accepted Islam and learned Sūrat al-Baqarah and Āl ʿImrān. He used to write for the Prophet ﷺ. Then he returned to Christianity and began saying: “Muḥammad knows nothing except what I wrote for him.” Allah caused him to die, and they buried him. By morning, the earth had cast his body out. They said: “This is the doing of Muḥammad and his companions. Because our companion fled from them, they dug him up and threw him out.” So they dug another grave for him and made it deeper. By morning, the earth had again cast him out. They said: “This is the doing of Muḥammad and his companions. They dug our companion up because he fled from them and threw him out.” So they dug as deeply into the earth as they possibly could and buried him again. By morning, the earth had cast him out once more. Then they realized that this was not the work of people, so they left him exposed.","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3617) - واللفظ له -، ومسلم (2781)."],[1265,"Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated: During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, some men from among the hypocrites would remain behind whenever the Prophet ﷺ went out on a military expedition. They rejoiced in remaining behind in opposition to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ returned, they would make excuses to him, swear oaths, and love to be praised for things they had not done. Then the following verse was revealed: “Do not think that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they have not done—do not think that they are safe from the punishment.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4567)، ومسلم (2777)."],[1266,"Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man says to a hypocrite, ‘My master,’ he has angered his Lord, the Exalted.”","حسن: رواه الحاكم (7865)، وعنه البيهقي في الشعب (4854)."],[1267,"Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The example of the hypocrite is like a wandering sheep between two flocks, going to this one at one time and to that one at another.” In another wording: “It turns toward this flock once and toward that flock once.”","صحيح: رواه مسلم (2784)."],[1268,"Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of the believer is like a crop that the wind continually bends, and the believer continually experiences trials. The example of the hypocrite is like the cedar tree: it does not move until it is finally cut down all at once.”","متفق عليه: رواه مسلم (2809)، والبخاري (5644)."],[1269,"Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “The example of the believer is like a tender stalk of crop: the wind bends it at one time and straightens it at another. The example of the hypocrite is like the cedar tree, which remains rigid until it is uprooted all at once.”","متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (5643)، ومسلم (2810، 62)، واللفظ للبخاري."],[1270,"Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated: There was some disagreement of the kind that occurs between people between a man from among the people of the mountain pass and Ḥudhayfah. The man said: “I adjure you by Allah, how many were the men of the mountain pass?” The people said to Ḥudhayfah: “Tell him, since he has asked you.” Ḥudhayfah said: “We were informed that they were fourteen. If you were one of them, then they were fifteen. I testify by Allah that twelve of them were at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the Day when the witnesses will stand.” Three were excused because they said: “We did not hear the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor did we know what the people intended.” The Prophet ﷺ had been traveling through a stony plain and said: “The water is scarce, so let no one reach it before me.” But he found that some people had already reached it before him, so he cursed them that day.","صحيح: رواه مسلم (11:2997)."],[1271,"Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was returning from the expedition of Tabūk, he ordered a caller to announce: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ will take the mountain pass, so no one else is to take it.” Ḥudhayfah was leading the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while ʿAmmār was driving it from behind. A group of masked men then approached on their mounts and crowded around ʿAmmār while he was driving the mount of the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAmmār began striking the faces of their mounts to drive them away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ḥudhayfah: “Enough, enough.” They continued until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pass. When he had descended, he dismounted, and ʿAmmār returned. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “O ʿAmmār, did you recognize the people?” He replied: “I recognized most of the mounts, but the men had covered their faces.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Do you know what they intended?” ʿAmmār replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “They intended to startle the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that they could throw him down.” ʿAmmār, may Allah be pleased with him, then asked one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “I adjure you by Allah, how many do you know the people of the mountain pass to have been?” He replied: “Fourteen.” ʿAmmār said: “If you were among them, then they were fifteen.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ excused three of them, because they said: “By Allah, we did not hear the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor did we know what the people intended.” ʿAmmār then said: “I testify that the remaining twelve are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the Day when the witnesses will stand.” Abū al-Walīd said: Abū al-Ṭufayl also mentioned concerning that expedition that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was told that the water was scarce. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a caller to announce: “No one is to reach the water before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached it, he found that a group had arrived there before him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed them that day.","حسن: رواه أحمد (23792)."],[1272,"Ḥudhayfah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out during the expedition of Tabūk. He was informed that the water was scarce, so he ordered a caller to announce among the people: “Let no one reach the water before me.” When he reached the water, he found that some people had preceded him to it, so he cursed them.","حسن: رواه أحمد (23395)."],[1273,"Maḥmūd ibn Labīd narrated from some men of Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal. He was asked: “Did the people know who the hypocrites among them were?” He replied: “Yes, by Allah. A man might know hypocrisy in his own brother, father, paternal uncle, or within his own clan, yet they continued interacting with one another despite that.” Maḥmūd then said: Some men from my people informed me about a man whose hypocrisy was well known. He would travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wherever he went. When the incident at al-Ḥijr occurred and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated, Allah sent a cloud which rained until the people had enough water. They went to the hypocrite and said: “Woe to you! Is there anything left to say after this?” He replied: “It was merely a passing cloud.” Ibn Isḥāq said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then continued traveling until, at one point on the road, his she-camel became lost. His Companions went out searching for it.\nWith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at that time was a Companion named ʿUmārah ibn Ḥazm, who had attended the pledge at al-ʿAqabah and the Battle of Badr and was the paternal uncle of Banū ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm. Staying in ʿUmārah’s camp was Zayd ibn al-Luṣayt al-Qaynuqāʿī, who was a hypocrite. Ibn Isḥāq said: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated to me from Maḥmūd ibn Labīd, from some men of Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal, that Zayd ibn al-Luṣayt said while he was in ʿUmārah’s camp and ʿUmārah was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Does Muḥammad not claim that he is a Prophet and that he informs you of news from heaven, yet he does not even know where his camel is?”\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while ʿUmārah was with him, then said: “A man has said: ‘This Muḥammad tells you that he is a Prophet and claims that he informs you about matters of heaven, yet he does not know where his camel is.’ By Allah, I know nothing except what Allah teaches me. Allah has now shown me where it is. It is in this valley, in such-and-such a ravine, where a tree has caught its reins. Go and bring it to me.” They went and brought the she-camel back. ʿUmārah ibn Ḥazm returned to his camp and said: “By Allah, how astonishing is something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just told us! He told us that Allah had informed him of a statement made by someone, namely such-and-such.” It was exactly what Zayd ibn al-Luṣayt had said. A man who had been in ʿUmārah’s camp but had not been present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By Allah, Zayd said those very words before you came.” ʿUmārah turned upon Zayd and began striking him in the neck, saying: “Come here, servants of Allah! There was a calamity in my own camp and I did not even realize it. Get out, O enemy of Allah, from my camp. Do not accompany me.”","حسن: رواه محمد بن إسحاق، والبيهقي في الدلائل (1722)."],[1274,"Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān said: “The hypocrites today are worse than they were during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. At that time they concealed their hypocrisy, whereas today they openly display it.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (7113)."],[1275,"Ḥudhayfah said: “Hypocrisy was during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. As for today, it is disbelief after faith.”","صحيح: رواه البخاري (7114)."]])